1 NAME Sárán /mac Cóelbad/
2 GIVN Sárán
2 _MARNM mac Cóelbad
1 SEX M
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Sárán mac Cóelbad==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Coelbad Mac Cruind Ba Drui, High King of Ireland and Ceindi ingen Ó Labrada 
2 CONT * Sárán mac Cóelbad (flourished circa third quarter of 5th century) was a Dal nAraide king in the time of Saint Patrick. He was the son of Cáelbad mac Cruind Ba Druí, a high king of Ireland and King of Ulster.
2 CONT * He is listed in king lists such as in the Book of Leinster and Laud Synchronisms but is not mentioned in the Irish annals. Genealogies such as Laud Genealogies and Rawlinson Genealogies give him a reign of 26 years. Another ment
2 CONC ion of Sárán is in the Vita tripartita Sancti Patricii. According to this, Sárán had made a raid on the Irish portion of Dál Riata and took away some captives.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Mac Artán of Kinelarty, County Down were said to be descended from him according to the Keating Genealogies.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Condlae mac Cóelbad Wikipedia==
2 CONT
2 CONT Condlae mac Cóelbad (flourished later 5th century) was a Dal nAraide king in the time of Saint Patrick. He was the son of Cáelbad mac Cruind Ba Druí, a high king of Ireland and King of Ulster and brother of the previous Dal nAraid
2 CONC e king Sárán mac Cóelbad.
2 CONT
2 CONT His exact dates are unknown as he is only listed in king lists and not in the Irish annals. The Vita tripartita Sancti Patricii preserves the story that he received Patrick with humility and granted him Domnach Combair (Muckamore,
2 CONC  County Antrim) for a church. As a result Patrick gave him and his descendants his blessing over those of Sárán who had violently opposed him.
2 CONT
2 CONT Condlae's descendants the Uí Chóelbad would eventually dominate the kingship. His son Eochaid mac Condlai (died 553) was king of all Ulaid. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source- Condlae mac Cóelbad Wikipedia - https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Condlae_mac_Cóelbad
2 CONT
