1 OCCU king of Osraige
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Anmchad mac Con Cherca''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Konge av Osraige fra 742 til ca 760'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * f. ca 712 sønn av Con Cherca mac Fáeláin. Moren var ukjent
2 CONT * Hans kone er ukjent. de hadde sønnen Fergal mac Anmchada 
2 CONT
2 CONT Anmchad var en aktiv hersker, som gjentatte ganger gikk til angrep på  sine østlige naboer i Leinster  .
2 CONT Første gangen en hører om Anmchads regjering er i 742, året da Cathal Mac Finguine døde. Her forteller Annals of Ulster og Annales of Tigernach at Osraige ødela landene Cenél Fiachach og Delbna. Disse lå over elven Brosnas dal , m
2 CONC ellom Durrow Abbey og River Shannon , i moderne County Offaly. Anmchad, tok sannsynligvis Déisi Mumain i 745 og  dreper kongen Uargus mac Fiachrae. Året etter beseiret og drepte Anmchad de tre sønnerne til Cumascrach, men hvem Cum
2 CONC ascrach og hans sønner var, og årsakene til at Anmchad var i krig med dem, er nå tapt.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hovedmålene for Anmchads senere kriger var Leinster, og særlig kongene og folket i sørlige Leinster, moderne County Carlow, blant annet Uí Bairrche Tire og Uí Cheinnselaig .  Kampen ved Inis Snaic i 750 som Anmchad vant, bekymret 
2 CONC Leinster, og i 754  vant han Fotharta Feai i den østlige delen av moderne Carlow. I  I 759, og igjen i 761, kjempet Anmchad ved Belach Gabraín-passet til Gowran-hovedruten mellom sør Leinster og Osraige. Begge ganger beseiret han 
2 CONC Leinstermen, og i den andre kampen ble  Donngal mac Laidcnén, konge av Ui Cheinnselaig drept. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Det er antatt at  Anmchad døde til en tid mellom hans siste opptreden i 761 og  da Tóim Snámas ble kongei kraft i 769 eller tidligere. Anmchad hadde minst en sønn som overlevde ham, Fergal mac Anmchada , som også var konge i Osrai
2 CONC ge og døde i 802
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anmchad_mac_Con_Cherca
2 CONT
2 CONT The kingdom of Osraige, later anglicised as Ossory, was one of over 100 small kingdoms which existed in 8th century Ireland. The Osraige—their name means people of the Deer—inhabited much of modern County Kilkenny and parts of nei
2 CONC ghbouring County Laois. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The first record of Anmchad's reign is in 742, the year in which Cathal mac Finguine died. Here the Annals of Ulster and the Annals of Tigernach state the Osraige devastated the lands of Cenél Fiachach and Delbna. These lay across
2 CONC  the valley of the River Brosna, between Durrow Abbey and the River Shannon, in modern County Offaly. Probably following this, perhaps in 745, Anmchad defeated the Déisi Mumain, of what is now the east of County Waterford, killing
2 CONC  their king Uargus mac Fiachrae. The following year Anmchad defeated and killed the three sons of Cumascrach, but who Cumascrach and his sons were, and the reasons why Anmchad was at war with them are now lost.
2 CONT
2 CONT The principle target of Anmchad's later wars was Leinster, and in particular the kingdoms and peoples of southern Leinster, modern County Carlow, chief among which were Uí Bairrche Tire and Uí Cheinnselaig. It may be that the batt
2 CONC le at Inis Snaic which Anmchad won, against whom is not stated, recorded in about 750, concerned Leinster. in 754 when the Osraige ravaged a territory to their east known as Fotharta Fea, in the eastern portion of modern Carlow. I
2 CONC n 759, and again in 761, Anmchad fought at Belach Gabraín—the pass of Gowran—the main route between south Leinster and Osraige. Both times he defeated the Leinstermen, and in the second battle Donngal mac Laidcnén, king of Uí Chei
2 CONC nnselaig, was killed.
2 CONT
2 CONT No mention of Anmchad is found in the Irish annals after the death of Donngal mac Laidcnén. In 769 a war among the Osraige is recorded in which Tóim Snáma mac Flainn, apparently now ruling Osraige, defeated the sons of Anmchad's p
2 CONC redecessor Cellach, among whom will have been his eventual successor Dúngal mac Cellaig. Accordingly, is presumed that Anmchad died at some time between his last appearance in 761 and the coming to power of Tóim Snáma in 769 or ea
2 CONC rlier. Anmchad had at least one son who survived him, Fergal, who was also king of Osraige and died in 802.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ==Succession of Kings from ''Book of Leinster==
