1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1.         '''[https://www.geni.com/people/Cerbhall-mac-Dunghal-King-of-Osraige-in-Ireland/6000000000161001437?through=6000000079325821064  CERBALL] (-888).  King of Ossory.  The Annals of Inisfallen record the dea
2 CONC th in 888 of "Cerball son of Dúngal, king of Osraige”[709].  m ---.  The name of Cerball´s wife is not known.The Fragmentary Annals of Ireland name in 854 "Cerball son of Dunlang king of Osraige" and "Mael Sechlainn´s daughter" as
2 CONC  his wife[14].  This daughter must have been born from an earlier otherwise unrecorded marriage of her father as her husband´s sister is recorded in the same passage as her father´s current wife.https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/IR
2 CONC ELAND.htm ''' 
