2 CONC tach Ua Briain, a great-grandson of Brian Bóruma, and Caithréim Chellacháin Chaisil (Deeds of Cellachán Caisil), written a generation later for Cormac Mac Cárthaig, a great-great-grandson of the eponymous Cellachán Caisil; O
2 CONC ́ Corráin, "Afterthoughts", pp. 18-19 [page numbers after etext]; Radner, "Writing history", p. 323; Flanagan, "High-kings with opposition", pp. 916 & 919; 
2 CONT ^ Byrne, p. 162; Ó Corrain, "Viking Ireland - Afterthoughts", pp. 17ff. 
2 CONT ^ Hudson, Prophecy of Berchán, pp. 135-138. 
