1 OCCU Dottir Eivind Eystman í Dublin, Husfrue I Skotland ("Skotlandi"), Sögð Eyvindardóttir í Landnámu, en „...ranglega talin dóttir Eyvindar austmanns...“
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Thurid Eyvindsdotter (Þuríðr Eyvindardóttir)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Hun bodde på Vestisland'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Thurid var født i Kaupanger, datter av Eyvind Ostmann og Raverta
2 CONT * Hun var gift med Thorstein, de hadde barna Olaf Fellan, Gro. Åløf. Osk. Thorhild, Thorgerd og Vigdis 
2 CONT
2 CONT Þuríðr Eyvindardóttir Tilnavn / fordanskning: Thurid Lokalitet: Vestl. Island Relationer: Datter af Eyvind Østmand. Søster til Helge den Magre. Gift med Thorstein Rød. De fik mange børn: Olaf Feilan, Gro, Åløf, Osk, Thorhild, Thor
2 CONC gerd og Vigdis.Kilder: Landnamabogen 82, 83
2 CONT
2 CONT http://heimskringla.no/wiki/Landnamabogen
2 CONT
2 CONT Turid Eysteinsdatter
2 CONT
2 CONT == Basics ==
2 CONT * Father: Eyvind "Austmann"
2 CONT * Mother: Raverta of Ossory
2 CONT * Husband: Torstein, son of Aud the Deep-minded (also called Unn)
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT THE LAXDAELA SAGA
2 CONT
2 CONT CHAPTER IV
2 CONT
2 CONT Ketill goes to Scotland, A.D. 890.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ketill Flatnose brought his ship to Scotland, and was well received by the great men there; for he was a renowned man, and of high birth. They offered him there such station as he would like to take, and Ketill and his company of 
2 CONC kinsfolk settled down there all except Thorstein, his daughter's son, who forthwith betook himself to warring, and harried Scotland far and wide, and was always victorious. Later on he made peace with the Scotch, and got for his o
2 CONC wn one-half of Scotland. He had for wife Thurid, daughter of Eyvind, and sister of Helgi the Lean. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Scotch did not keep the peace long, but treacherously murdered him. Ari Thorgils' son the Wise, writing of his death, says that he fell in Caithness. Unn the Deepminded was in Caithness when her son Thorstein fell. When she he
2 CONC ard that Thorstein was dead, and her father had breathed his last, she deemed she would have no prospering in store there. So she had a ship built secretly in a wood, and when it was ready built she arrayed it, and had great wealt
2 CONC h withal; and she took with her all her kinsfolk who were left alive; and men deem that scarce may an example be found that any one, a woman only, has ever got out of such a state of war with so much wealth and so great a followin
2 CONC g. From this it may be seen how peerless among women she was. Unn had with her many men of great worth and high birth. 
2 CONT
2 CONT A man named Koll was one of the worthiest amongst her followers, chiefly owing to his descent, he being by title a "Hersir". There was also in the journey with Unn a man named Hord, and he too was also a man of high birth and of g
2 CONC reat worth. When she was ready, Unn took her ship to the Orkneys; there she stayed a little while, and there she married off Gro, the daughter of Thorstein the Red. She was the mother of Greilad, who married Earl Thorfinn, the son
2 CONC  of Earl Turf-Einar, son of Rognvald Mere-Earl. Their son was Hlodvir, the father of Earl Sigurd, the father of Earl Thorfinn, and from them come all the kin of the Orkney Earls. After that Unn steered her ship to the Faroe Isles,
2 CONC  and stayed there for some time. There she married off another daughter of Thorstein, named Olof, and from her sprung the noblest race of that land, who are called the Gate-Beards.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT  descent from Aud "the Deep-Minded":
2 CONT
2 CONT Aud Kettilsdatter, whose adventurous life took her from Norway to Ireland and finally to Iceland where she died in AD 900, married Olaf "the White" Ingjaldsson (c 840-877), a Viking who was briefly king of Dublin; they had a son, 
2 CONC Thorstein "the Red" (c 858-888) who took his family to Iceland and there married Thurid Eyvindsdatter. Their daughter Groa married Duncan, Earl of Caithness in Scotland, and was the mother of the Grelauga who married Thorfinn of O
2 CONC rkney (above).
2 CONT
2 CONT  Født i Amla i Kaupanger, Sogn og Fjordane
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT It is reported she was married to The Red in 868 in Dala, Iceland.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://heimskringla.no/wiki/Landnamabogen_2 (72)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''Tjodhild Eyvindsdotter (Þjóðhildar Eyvindardóttir)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Þjóðhildar Eyvindardóttir Tilnavn / fordanskning: Tjodhild Lokalitet: Vestl. Island Relationer: Søster til Helge den Magre. Gift med Thord Vikingson. Moder til Thorkel Kæmpe og Thorvald Hvid. Kilder: Landnamabogen 112 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://heimskringla.no/wiki/Landnamabogen
