2 CONC ters record the death in 973 of “Ceallach son of Domhnall, lord of Ui-Faelain” killed by “Broen son of Murchadh”[621].  The Annals of the Four Masters record that “Braen son of Murchadh royal heir of Leinster” was killed in 978 in
2 CONC  “the battle of Teamhair”[622], the battle being dated between 978 and 980 in different sources. 
2 CONT
