2 CONT >>>>a)         '''[https://www.geni.com/profile/index/6000000079501196019?from_flash=1&through=6000000079501196019&fsession_id=1529777196241 CONGALACH] (-killed 1014 or 1017).  The Annals of the Four Masters record that “Conghalac
2 CONC h son of Conchobhar, lord of the Ui-Failghe” was killed in 1014 when the army of “Maelseachlainn, Ua Neill, and Ua Maeldoraidh” was attacked while they were plundering “Ui-Cennsealagh”[628].  The Annals of the Four Masters record 
2 CONC the death in 1017 of “Conghalach son of Conchobhar son of Finn lord of Ui-Failghe”[629].  It is probable that these two entries refer to the same person.  Neither entry is found in the Annals of Ulster or the Annals of Inisfallen.
2 CONC   m ---.  The name of Congalach´s wife is not known.  Congalach & his wife had one child:''' 
2 CONT
