2 CONC a son of Torfeinar" when recording that he was Jarl in Orkney when the islands were invaded by the sons of King Eirik "Blodøks"[200]. Joint Jarl of Orkney with his brothers. Sole Jarl of Orkney 954, and 955-976. Orkneyinga Saga re
2 CONC cords that “Earl Thorfinn Skull-Splitter…died in his bed” and was “laid in a burial mound at Hoxa in North Ronaldsway”[201]. The Complete Peerage estimates Thorfinn´s death to “soon after 977” which appears broadly consistent with
2 CONC  the events in which his children are reported as involved[202].
