1 NOTE Leif Ericson, in the year 1000, visited the newly discovered mainland of North America.  He had left Greenland with several ships, and reported that this country, which he called Vinland, had grape vines which grew wild, and they 
2 CONC spent the winter.  A later settlement was made there.  He succeeded his father, Eric The Red, as leader in Greenlande, and during the reign of Olaf Tryggvason, introduced Christianity in Greenland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Leif Erickson, son of Eric the Red, led  an exploration to the mainland of North America, and called it Vinland.(Wine-land)  Said to have been near L'Anse aux Meadows at the northern tip of Newfoundland. His exploration and discov
2 CONC ery of Vinland mentioned in the chronicles of Adam of Bremen. (who d. 1076
