2 CONT The ''Annals of Inisfallen'' record the death in 1011 of "Domnall son of Brian.[1003] The ''Annals of the Four Masters'' record the death in 1010 of ''Domhnall son of Brian son of Ceinneidight, son of the king of Ireland.[1004] Th
2 CONC e name of Domnall's wife is not known. Domnall and his wife had one child: Toirdelbach ([1008/1009 - CennCoradh 14 Jul 1086)...."
2 CONT '''''Annals of Inisfallen''''', 1011.3, p. 181  [https://celt.ucc.ie/published/T100004/index.html]
2 CONT '''''Annals of the Four Masters''''', 1010.12, p. 765  [https://celt.ucc.ie/published/T100005B/index.html]  
2 CONT '''The reason for differing death years is unknown'''. While the Julian calendar was in use in 11th-century Ireland, the difference in years cannot be explained by the 1582 origin of the Gregorian calendar. These Annals were penne
2 CONC d before 1582. Moreover, the Gregorian calendar was not embraced by all nations and churches for over 100 years.
