1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===NOTE: Snorre in his ''King Olav Trygvason's Saga'' varies between describing her as a sister and as a daughter of "King Olaf Kvaran". She is shown on Geni as a daughter per:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/IRELAND.htm#_Toc389126206
2 CONT
2 CONT 7.         GYDA .  Snorre records the betrothal and marriage of Olaf Trygvason to "a queen called Gyda…a sister of Olaf Kvaran who was king of Dublin in Ireland [who] had been married to a great earl in England" after whose death 
2 CONC "she was at the head of his dominions"[1318].  In a later passage, Snorre refers to "King Olaf Kvaran" as his wife's father[1319].  m firstly ---.  m secondly (in England 988) as his second wife, OLAV Trygveson, son of TRYGVE Olav
2 CONC sson [Norway] & his wife Åstrid Eiriksdatter (posthumously [968][1320]-drowned Øresund o. b. Svold, near Rügen 9 Sep [1000]).  He imposed himself as OLAV I King of Norway in [995]. 
