2 CONC on of Conchobhar, lord of the Ui-Failghe” was killed in 1014 when the army of “Maelseachlainn, Ua Neill, and Ua Maeldoraidh” was attacked while they were plundering “Ui-Cennsealagh”[628].  The Annals of the Four Masters record the
2 CONC  death in 1017 of “Conghalach son of Conchobhar son of Finn lord of Ui-Failghe”[629].  It is probable that these two entries refer to the same person.  Neither entry is found in the Annals of Ulster or the Annals of Inisfallen.  m
2 CONC  ---.  The name of Congalach´s wife is not known.  Congalach & his wife had one child: 
