1 NOTE {geni:about_me} >[https://www.geni.com/people/Dairmait-King-of-Leinster-High-King-of-Ireland/6000000008630666266?through=6000000006831823543  DIARMAIT], son of MAEL na mBó & his wife --- (-killed in battle Odba 7 Feb 1072).  The A
2 CONC nnals of Tigernach record that “Ruaidri son of Tadg son of Lorcan” was blinded in 1036 by “Mael na mbó” (which must indicate the latter´s son assuming that the death date of Mail na mBó is correctly recorded above)[665].  The Anna
2 CONC ls of Tigernach record that “Diarmait son of Mael na mbó king of the Húi Cennselaig” plundered “Colomb cille´s Maein (Moone), Dísert Diarmata and my Senóc´s Mugna and Clonmore” in 1040[666].  The Annals of Tigernach record that “E
2 CONC chmarcach son of Ragnall king of the Foreigners went oversea” in 1052 and “the son of Mael na mbó assumed the kingship after him”, adding in a later passage that “the son of Mael na mbó took the kingship of Dublin by force” in 105
2 CONC 3[667].  King of Leinster.  High King of Ireland.  The Anglo-Saxon Chronicle records that Harold Godwinsson and his brother Leofwine, sons of Godwin Earl of Wessex, sought refuge with him in 1051 following the family's disgrace[66
2 CONC 8].  Orderic Vitalis records that “duo filii Heraldi regis Angliæ” had fled “ad Dyrmetum regem Hiberniæ” after their father was killed and, with his support, landed at Exeter with 66 ships, ravaged the interior of the country, but
2 CONC  were defeated by “Briennius Eudonis comitis Britanniæ minoris filius et Guillelmus Gualdi” and fled back to Ireland[669].  The Annals of Tigernach record that “Diarmait son of Mail na mbó, king of Britons and the Hebrides and Dub
2 CONC lin and Mug Nuadat´s Half [southern Ireland]” was killed in 1072 by “Conchobar Húa Mael-Sechlainn in the battle of Odba”[670].  The Annals of Ulster record the death in 1072 of "Diarmait son of Mael na mBó king of Laigin and the f
2 CONC oreigners…7 Feb” killed in battle by “Conchobar ua Mael Sechlainn king of Temair”[671]. m [https://www.geni.com/people/Dearbforgail-%C3%93-Briain/6000000005599447055?through=6000000006831823543  DERBORGAILL], daughter of ---, gran
2 CONC ddaughter of BRIAN Boru King of Ireland (-Imlech 1080).  The Annals of Ulster record the death in 1080 of "Derbhforgaill daughter of Brian´s son, wife of Diarmait son of Mael na mBó…in Imlech”[672]. Diarmait & his wife had three c
2 CONC hildren: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>1.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Murchad-Mac-Diarmata-O-Cheinnselaig/6000000006831823543  MURCHAD] (-Dublin 1070, bur Dublin).  The Annals of Tigernach record that “Murchad son of Diarmait son of Mael na mbó” invaded “Man
2 CONC n…and defeated Ragnall´s son” in 1061[673].  The Annals of Ulster record the death in 1070 of "Murchad son of Diarmait king of Laigin and the foreigners…buried in Áth Cliath”[674].  The Annals of Inisfallen record the death in 107
2 CONC 0 of "Murchad son of Diarmiat son of Mael na mBó king of foreigners and Gaedil…in Áth Cliath”[675].  m ---.  The name of Murchad´s wife is not known.  Murchad & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>a)        ''' [https://www.geni.com/people/Donal-Mac-Morough-Dublin/6000000008177419512 DOMNALL] (-1075).  The Annals of Inisfallen record that "the son of Murchad, grandson of Mael na mBó took the kingship of Áth Cliath” in 10
2 CONC 75 and died “in the same year”[676].  King of Dublin.  The Annals of Ulster record the death in 1075 of "Domnall son of Murchad, king of Áth Cliath…of a three nights' sickness"[677].''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>b)         [https://www.geni.com/people/Donnchad-mac-Murchada-King-of-Leinster-and-Dublin/6000000002043258537  DONCHAD] (-1115).  King of Leinster.  The Annals of Tigernach (Continuation) record that “the son of Murchad, son of
2 CONC  Diarmait, son of Máel na mbó” won a battle in 1114[678]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -        see below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>c)         [https://www.geni.com/profile/index/6000000010646172298?through=6000000002043258537&from_flash=1&fsession_id=1529943910321 ENDA] .  His parentage is confirmed by the Annals of Tigernach (Continuation) which names “Di
2 CONC armait son of Enda, son of Murchad, king of the Foreigners and Leinstermen”[679].  m ---.  The name of Enda´s wife is not known.  Enda & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>i)          [https://www.geni.com/profile/index/6000000079563782104?through=6000000079563782104&from_flash=1&fsession_id=1529943910321 DIARMUIT] (-[1117]).  King of Leinster.  The Annals of Tigernach (Continuation) record that
2 CONC  “Diarmait son of Enda, son of Murchad, king of the Foreigners and Leinstermen, rested in Dublin” in 1117[680]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>2.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Enna-King-Of-of-Leinster/6000000008177419563 ENNA] (-killed 1092).  His parentage is confirmed by the Annals of Ulster which name "Diarmait son of Enna son of Diarmait king of Laigin”[683]
2 CONC .  The Annals of Inisfallen record that "Enna son of Diarmait and the nobles of Desmumu” successfully held the fortress of “Port Láirge” in 1088 against “the Laigin and the son of Domnall Remar”[684].  The Annals of Inisfallen rec
2 CONC ord that "Muirchertach Ui Briain” imprisoned “Énna son of Diarmait” in 1089[685].  The Annals of Inisfallen record the death in 1092 of "Enna son of Diarmait…slain by the Uí Cheinnselaig”[686].  m ---.  The name of Enna´s wife is 
2 CONC not known.  Enna & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>a)         [https://www.geni.com/people/Diarmuid-MacEnna/6000000008248294284 DIARMUIT] (-killed Cell Dara 1098).  The Annals of Ulster record the death in 1098 of "Diarmait son of Enna son of Diarmait king of Laigin, killed by 
2 CONC the sons of Murchad son of Diarmait…in the middle of Cell Dara”[687]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>3.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Glunairn-of-Leinster/6000000008177419569 --- “Glún Iairn”] (-killed in battle 1070).  The Annals of Inisfallen record the death in 1070 of "Glún Iairn son of Diarmiat son of Mael na mBó…sl
2 CONC ain by Cartach´s son and the Gailenga and by the north of Ireland”[688]. 
