1 NOTE {geni:about_me} King Donnchad was killed in battle in 1115 by the Dublin Vikings that were ruled by his cousin Sigtrygg Silkbeard, and was buried in Dublin along with the body of a dog, considered to be a huge insult.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT King Donnchad MacMurchada was killed in battle against Domnall Ua Brianin in 1115
2 CONT [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/IRELAND.htm#DonchadLeinsterdied1115A]
2 CONT ------------------
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/Murchad-Mac-Diarmata-O-Cheinnselaig/6000000006831823543  MURCHAD] (-Dublin 1070, bur Dublin).  The Annals of Tigernach record that “Murchad son of Diarmait son of Mael na mbó” invaded “Mann…and defeate
2 CONC d Ragnall´s son” in 1061[673].  The Annals of Ulster record the death in 1070 of "Murchad son of Diarmait king of Laigin and the foreigners…buried in Áth Cliath”[674].  The Annals of Inisfallen record the death in 1070 of "Murchad
2 CONC  son of Diarmiat son of Mael na mBó king of foreigners and Gaedil…in Áth Cliath”[675].  m ---.  The name of Murchad´s wife is not known.  Murchad & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>a)         [https://www.geni.com/people/Donal-Mac-Morough-Dublin/6000000008177419512 DOMNALL] (-1075).  The Annals of Inisfallen record that "the son of Murchad, grandson of Mael na mBó took the kingship of Áth Cliath” in 1075 
2 CONC and died “in the same year”[676].  King of Dublin.  The Annals of Ulster record the death in 1075 of "Domnall son of Murchad, king of Áth Cliath…of a three nights' sickness"[677]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>b)  '''[https://www.geni.com/people/Donnchad-mac-Murchada-King-of-Leinster-and-Dublin/6000000002043258537 DONCHAD], son of MURCHAD King of Leinster & his wife --- (-1115).  King of Leinster.  The Annals of Tigernach (Continuati
2 CONC on) record that “the son of Murchad, son of Diarmait, son of Máel na mbó” won a battle in 1114[689].  The Annals of Tigernach (Continuation) record that “Donnchad son of Murchad king of Leinster” was killed in battle by “Domnall s
2 CONC on of Murchertach Húa Bríáin” in 1115[690]. m ---.  The name of Donchad´s wife is not known. Donchad & his wife had one child:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>1.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Enna-King-of-Leinster/6000000010646172298 ENNA] (-1126).  King of Leinster.  The Annals of Tigernach (Continuation) record that “Toirdelbach son of Ruaidri king of Ireland” gave “the kin
2 CONC gship of the Foreigners to the king of Leinster” in 1125[691].  The Annals of Tigernach (Continuation) record that “Enna son of Donnchad son of Murchad king of Leinster” died in 1126, after which “Toirdelbach Húa Conchobair king o
2 CONC f Ireland” was made king of Leinster, unsuccessfully challenged by “Cormac Mac Carthaig king of Desmond”[692].  m ---.  The name of Enna´s wife is not known.  Enna & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>a)         [https://www.geni.com/people/no-name/6000000079563782104 DIARMAIT] (-Fermanagh 1 May 1171).  King of Leinster.  The Annales Cambriæ record that "Diermit rex filius Murcath" was expelled from Ireland by his people a
2 CONC nd went to the English king, recording in later passages that he returned to Ireland and built "castellum Carrec iuxta Wisefordiam" in 1170, and died in 1172[693].  "Diarmicius Rex Lageniensium" donated "terram…Balidubgaill" to Al
2 CONC l Saints Dublin by undated charter witnessed by "…Enna filio meo…"[694].  The Annals of Tigernach (Continuation) record that Henry II King of England arrived in Ireland in 1171, went to Dublin where he received “the kingship of Le
2 CONC inster and of the men of Meath, Brefne, Oriel and Ulster”[695].  The Expugnatio Hibernica records the death "apud Fernas circa kal Mai" of "Dermitius Murchardi filius" [in 1171][696].  m [https://www.geni.com/people/no-name/600000
2 CONC 0079565452902 MOR], daughter of ---].  The primary source which confirms her marriage has not yet been identified.   Mistress: (1152) [https://www.geni.com/people/Derbforgaill/6000000079565324093?through=6000000079565128944 DERBFO
2 CONC RGAILL], wife of [https://www.geni.com/profile/index/6000000079565128944?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1529949407223&through=6000000079565128944 TIERNAN O'Rourke] King of Breifny, daughter of [https://www.geni.com/profile/index/6000000
2 CONC 079565326087?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1529949407223&through=6000000079565326087 MURCHAD O'Malaghlin] King of Meath & his wife ---.  The Expugnatio Hibernica records that "Dermitius…Murchardi filius Langeniensium princeps" eloped w
2 CONC ith "Ororicio…Medensium rege…uxor ipsius Omachlachelini filia" [in 1152][697].  The Annals of Tigernach (Continuation) record that “Diarmait Mac Murchada king of Leinster forcibly carried off out of Meath the wife of Húa Ruairc…De
2 CONC rb-forgaill daughter of Murchad with her wealth” in 1152, adding in a later passage that she “came again to Húa Ruairc by flight from Leinster” in 1153[698].  
2 CONT
2 CONT >c)         [https://www.geni.com/profile/index/6000000079563039097?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1529941156819&through=6000000079563039097 MURCHAD].  His parentage is confirmed by the Annals of Tigernach (Continuation) which name “Gor
2 CONC mlaith, daughter of Murchad, son of Mael na mbó”[663].  m ---.  The name of Murchad´s wife is not known.  Murchad & his wife had one child: 
