2 CONT Cressa ingen Aurchada Uí Briúin Seóla
2 CONT
2 CONT Children	
2 CONT # N. N. ingen Taidg Uí Conchobair+ 3. married Murchad mac Finn Uí Fáeláin, rí Laigin, son of rígdamna Laigin Finn mac Máel Mórda Uí Fáeláin, before 965.1,2
2 CONT # Conchobar, rí Connacht+ d. 9721. Child: Cathal, rí Connacht+ d. 10107,1
2 CONT # rígan Érenn Mór ingen Taidg Uí Conchobair d. 99211. Is this the wife of Murchad, King of Leinster, (d. 972)? 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT FMG Medlands 
2 CONT IRELAND  v5.0 Updated 01 March 2025
2 CONT Chapter 2.    CONNAUGHT
2 CONT A.      KINGS of CONNAUGHT (Ua CONCHOBAR)
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/IRELAND.htm#_Toc389126188
2 CONT
2 CONT The name of Cathal´s wife is not known.  Cathal & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT ii)         TADHG (-956).  The Annals of the Four Masters record that “Domnhall son of Cathal heir apparent of Connaught” was killed in 923 by “his brother Tadhg son of Cathal” and that “Tadhg assumed the place of his father”[278]
2 CONC .  King of Connaught.  The Annals of Inisfallen record the death in 956 of "Tadc son of Cathal king of Connachta”[279].  m ---.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The name of Tadhg´s wife is not known.  Tadhg & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT *(a)       CONCHOBAR (-973).  King of Connaught.  The Annals of Ulster record the death in 973 of "Conchobor son of Tadc king of Connacht"[280].  The Annals of Inisfallen record the death in 973 of "Conchobar son of Tadc son of Ca
2 CONC thal king of Connachta”[281].  m ---.  The name of Conchobar´s wife is not known.  Conchobar & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT **(1)       CATHAL (-1010).  King of Connaught.  The Annals of the Four Masters record the death in 1009 of “Cathal son of Conchobhar king of Connaught…he was the grandson of Tadhg of the Tower”[282]. -        see below. 
2 CONT *(b)       MUIRCHERTACH (-killed in battle Formaeil, Rath-beg 967).  The Annals of the Four Masters record the death in 965 of “Muircheartach Ua-Taidhg royal heir to Connaught” killed in “the battle of Formaeil at Rath-beg”[283]. 
2 CONC  The Annals of Ulster record the death in 967 of "Muirchertach Ua Tadc, heir designate of Connacht” killed in “the battle of Formaíl”[284]. 
2 CONT *(c)       CATHAL (-killed in battle Ceis-Corainn 973).  King of Connaught.  The Annals of Inisfallen record the death in 973 of "Cathal son of Tadc…killed immediately after taking the kingship”[285].  The Annals of the Four Maste
2 CONC rs record that “Cathal son of Tadhg king of Connaught” was killed in 971 in “the battle of Ceis-Corainn [against] Murchadh Ua Flaithbheartach i.e. Glun-Illar king of Aileach”[286]. 
2 CONT *(d)       MOR (-[990/91]).  The Annals of Tigernach record the death in [990/91] of “Mor, daughter of Tadg, son of Cathal, son of Conchobar, queen of Ireland”[287].  This passage does not name Mor´s husband.  However, Maelsechnai
2 CONC ll is the only person described in other passages in the Annals of Tigernach as king of Ireland at that time.  m as his second wife, MAELSECHNAILL King of Ireland, son of DOMNALL & his wife --- ([949/50]-Cró Inis of Lough Ennell 2
2 CONC  Sep 1022). 
2 CONT
