2 CONT # https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conchobar_mac_Tadg A son of Tadc in Túir (of the tower), Conchobar's father died in 956 as king of Connacht, but his sept of the Síol Muireadaigh were successfully opposed by Fergal ua Ruairc of the
2 CONC  Uí Briúin of Bréifne, who reigned till 967.
2 CONT # https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/O%27Conor_dynasty The O'Conor dynasty (Middle Irish: Ó Conchobhair; Modern Irish: Ó Conchúir) are an Irish noble dynasty and formerly one of the most influential and distinguished royal dynasties in
2 CONC  Ireland. The O'Conor family held the throne of the Kingdom of Connacht up until 1475.
