2 CONC ng and Magnus” as the two sons of “Earl Erlend Thorfinnson” and his wife “Thora, the daughter of Sumarlidi Ospaksson”[910].  He was installed as Jarl of ½ Orkney in Spring 1108 by Eistein I Magnusson Joint King of Norway.  Orkneyi
2 CONC nga Saga records that “Earl Magnus” was killed on the orders of his cousin Hakon “two days after St Tiburtius´ Mass…1091”, after ruling Orkney jointly for seven years, and was buried on “Mainland…at Christ Church”[911].  He was pu
2 CONC t to death by his cousin Hakon Paulsson Joint Jarl of Orkney, with whom he had quarrelled.  Canonised.  
