1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == ROBERT OF MONTGOMERY ==
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Roberto de Mundegumbri, Roberto de Mundegumbri, Roberto de Mungumri, Roberto de Mungumbry, Roberto de Mundgumri, Robertus de Mongummeri, Robto d. Mungubri, Rob de mote Gumi, Robto de Mungumij, Robto de Mundegumi'''<
2 CONC /blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Question of Identity ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The ancestry of Robert of Montgomery has not been satisfactorily identified. The late Sir William Fraser believed that he "could only have been" the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Arnulph-de-Montgomery-Earl-of-Pembroke/6000
2 CONC 000002043201668, the Castellan of Pembroke Castle. [https://archive.org/details/memorialsofmonv100fras/page/8/mode/1up Memorials of the Montgomeries: 8] However, the late John Anderson believed that the reasons advanced by Fraser 
2 CONC in support of his opinion were "very unsubstantial and without the sanction of any valid evidence." [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/page/424/mode/1up The Scots Peerage III: 422] M
2 CONC ore recently, the late G. W. S. Barrow had this to say; "It is most unlikely that the Scottish family of Montgomery were related to the family which held the earldom of Shrewsbury until 1102, who took their name from Montgomery in
2 CONC  Calvados. [The Kingdom of the Scots, Chapter 12, page 344]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert of Montgomery's name is noticed in at least one charter issued by Malcolm IV, King of Scots, 1153-65. In this charter his name is noticed in company with Walter son of Alan, the first of Scotland's family of hereditary s
2 CONC tewards, and this suggests that the charter belongs to the period 1163-65. [https://archive.org/details/libercartarump6900edinuoft/page/203 St. Andrew, p. 203] His name is also noticed in the witness list of another seven undated 
2 CONC charters which were either issued by Walter son of Alan, or were issued during his time as steward,1163-77. [https://archive.org/details/registrummonaste00mait/page/5 Passelet, p. 5 et seq.] [https://archive.org/details/libersmari
2 CONC edecal01kels/page/138 Kelso, charter number 170 on p. 138] [https://archive.org/details/libersanctemari01innegoog/page/n150 Melrose I, charter number 66 on pp. 55-6] The name of Robert of Montgomery is also noticed in an undated c
2 CONC harter that was issued by Jocelin, Bishop of Glasgow, which belongs to the time of Alan son of Walter, the second hereditary steward of Scotland, 1177-1204,  [https://archive.org/details/libersanctemari01innegoog/page/n129 Melrose
2 CONC  I, charter number 43 on pp. 36-7] and another which was probably also issued during the time of the second steward.  [https://archive.org/details/registrummonaste00mait/page/116 Passelet, p. 116] His name is usually found high up
2 CONC  on the witness lists.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Eaglesham in Renfrewshire ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert of Montgomery was one of the most prominent of the followers of Walter son of Alan, the first hereditary steward of Scotland. It seems quite likely, therefore, probable even, that he received a fief from his lord. Sir Wi
2 CONC lliam Fraser claimed that the fief in question was the lands of Eaglesham : "Robert obtained from Water the Steward a grant of the lands of Eagleshame" [https://archive.org/details/memorialsofmonv100fras/page/7 Memorials: 7] but t
2 CONC here is nothing in the evidence reviewed here to suggest that this was actually the case.The Reverend John Anderson correctly observed that Sir William Fraser's statement was entirely conjectural. [https://archive.org/details/scot
2 CONC speeragefoun03paul/page/423 Scots Peerage III: 423]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Priory of St. Andrew ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1163 X 1165: Cart' M . R . de t'ra Balwini I pt . Malcolm' Rex Scottor' Prepositis t aliis omnibz suis burgensib' de pert . salt . Sciatis me dedisse t concessisse homini meo Baldwino q'anda' t'ram in pert habente decem pedes I
2 CONC  latitudine . uiginti quatuor in longitudine . juxta domu vilchil  . ita liberam t quietam ut habet domu sua pp'am Test. Walto' cancell . Walto filio Alani . Hugone ridal . Robto de Mundegumi . ap Berewic . [https://archive.org/de
2 CONC tails/libercartarump6900edinuoft/page/203 St. Andrew, p. 203]'''
2 CONT
