1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Conchobar na Fiodhbha O'Neill (also recorded as Conchabhair na Fiadhbhuidhe or Connor of Tir-Eoghain) was born circa 1070–1100. His traditional death date is recorded in genealogical tracks as 1170. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His epithet "na Fiodhbha" translates to "of the Yellow Woods" or "of the Deer Woods", indicating the localized forest district where his branch maintained their territory, still recognized regionally as the Feeragh. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Flaithbheartach Locha Feadha O'Neill, the Prince of Ulster.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Wives: Unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the father of Tadhg Glinne O'Neill (Tiege "of the Glinnes"), who was his direct biological son and successor.His historical significance is defined by his violent death. He was assassinated by the rival Mac Lochlainn dynast
2 CONC y in 1170. This murder marked a brutal escalation in the long-running territorial war for supreme control over the kingship of Ulster, a conflict that his descendants eventually won to establish the sovereign Kingdom of Tyrone.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----  
