2 TITL Dermot MacMurrough - Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 NOTE He was the 58th and last Christian King of Leinster, called "Dermod MacMurough." His rule began in 1135. He was deposed in 1166 by King Roderick O'Connor of Ireland. He was aided by Tierman O'Ruarc, Prince of West Brefni. In 1153 
2 CONC he carried off Dearvolga, daughter of O'Melahlin, the 1st King of Meath and wife of O'Ruark, Prince of Brefney.
1 NOTE He was the 58th and last Christian King of Leinster, called "Dermod MacMurough." His rule began in 1135. He was deposed in 1166 by King Roderick O'Connor of Ireland. He was aided by Tierman O'Ruarc, Prince of West Brefni. In 1153 
2 CONC he carried off Dearvolga, daughter of O'Melahlin, the 1st King of Meath and wife of O'Ruark, Prince of Brefney.
