1 NOTE REF: "Yale Genealogy and History of Wales", 1908, Rodney Horace Yalep. 40:  During King Stephen's reign of 17 years in England, he leftWales much to
2 CONT itself and Owain materially added to the resources of his country &re-occupied several districts, which the Welsh had lost in formeryears. In the meantime however, he and Cadwaladr quarreld and thelatter fled to England.  Also dur
2 CONC ing these years (C25) Rhys apGruffydd, a son of Gruffydd ap Rhun, who was son of Rhys ap Tewdwr,had won several comparatively important engagements and successes inthe south.
1 NOTE REF Univ of Hull: They had two sons older than Iorwerth; & a daughter& two more sons younger than Rhodri. Cynan is probably one of theseunnamed sons (REF: Penman, Falls the Shadow).
1 NOTE He ruled from 1137 to 1170.
1 NOTE OR "GWINEDH"; PRINCE OF NORTH WALES; KING 1137-1170; HAD 3 SONS AND 2 DAUGHTERS
2 CONT BESIDES THOSE SHOWN; THERE EXISTS A SOMEWHAT ROMANTIC LEGEND THAT HE HAD
2 CONT ANOTHER SON NAMED MADOC, AROUND WHOM A MYTH OF THE WELSH DISCOVERY OF AMERICA
2 CONT AND A BAND OF WHITE INDIANS (THE "MANDAN") ROSE - THERE IS EVEN A PLAQUE
2 CONT (RAISED BY THE D.A.R. IN 1953) AT FORT MORGAN, MOBILE, ALABAMA, WHICH READS:
2 CONT "IN MEMORY OF PRINCE MADOC, A WELSH EXPLORER WHO LANDED ON THE SHORES OF MOBILE
2 CONT BAY IN 1170 AND LEFT BEHIND, WITH THE INDIANS, THE WELSH LANGUAGE. AUTHORITY IS
2 CONT - RNCYCLOPEDIA AMERICANA COPYRIGHT 1918 - WEBSTER'S ENCYCLOPEDIA - RICHARD
2 CONT HAKLUYT, 1552-1610, A WELSH HISTORIAN AND GEOGRAPHER - RIDPATH'S HISTORY OF THE
2 CONT WORLD - ANCIENT ROMAN COINS FOUND IN FORTS IN TENN.  THESE FORTS RESEMBLE THE
2 CONT FORTS OF WALES OF THE 9TH AND 10TH CENTUIRES AND OF THE WHITE INDIANS OF THE
2 CONT TENNESSEE AND MISSOURI RIVERS."
1 NOTE
