1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/240937520/susanna_ferch-gruffydd
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: The Royal Family of Gwynedd - The Children of Gruffudd, Nephew of Iago; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id80.html. (Steven Ferry, December 13, 2019.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: Owain Brogyntyn and His Family; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id224.html. (Steven Ferry, July 28, 2020.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: Kingship of Gwynedd - 1170 to 1175: http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id301.html (Steven Ferry, September 8, 2022.)
2 CONT
2 CONT  -------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Susanna verch Gruffydd b abt 1110, Aberffraw Castle, Anglesey, Wales, daughter of Gruffydd ap Cynan and Angharad verch Owain. She md Madog ap Maredudd abt 1130, prob Wales, son of Maredudd ap Bleddyn, Prince of Powys, and Hunydd v
2 CONC erch Einudd.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Madog ap Maredudd and Susanna verch Gruffydd were:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Gruffydd-Maelor ap Madog, Lord of Bromfield, b abt 1146.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Marared verch Madog b abt 1150, Aberffraw Castle, Anglesey, Wales. She md Iorwerth-Drwyndwn ap Owain abt 1168, son of Owain-Gwynedd ap Gruffydd and Gwladys verch Llywarch.
2 CONT
2 CONT or, according http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madog_ap_Maredudd#Children :
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Llywelyn ap Madog
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Gruffydd Maelor
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Owain Brogyntyn
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Gwenllian ferch Madog, married Rhys ap Gruffydd, prince of Deheubarth
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Marared ferch Madog, married Iorwerth Drwyndwn and was the mother of Llywelyn the Great
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Efa ferch Madog, married Cadwallon ap Madog
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Courtesy of fantastically full family tree cf.:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hughes of Gwerclas 1/2/3/4:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.maximiliangenealogy.co.uk/burke1/Royal%20Descents/hughesofgwerclas_1.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.maximiliangenealogy.co.uk/burke1/Royal%20Descents/hughesofgwerclas_2.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.maximiliangenealogy.co.uk/burke1/Royal%20Descents/hughesofgwerclas_3.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.maximiliangenealogy.co.uk/burke1/Royal%20Descents/hughesofgwerclas_4.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT # 12694-Welsh Medieval Database
2 CONT
2 CONT Susanna was the 2nd wife of Madog ab Maredudd, Brenin of Povys. Source- Griffith-Pedigrees of Anglesey and Caernarvan,Page 331
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Daughter of Gruffydd ap Cynan
2 CONT * Wife of Madoc (Madog, Madwg) ap Maredudd
2 CONT
2 CONT Welsh wives *'''did not'''* take their husbands' patronymics. It was not until the Welsh started using regular surnames (c. 16th century with isolated earlier examples) that women started taking their husbands' last names.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Susanna_Gruffydd_(1)
2 CONT
