1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sturla Þórðarson (1214–1284) was an Icelandic politician/chieftain and writer of sagas and contemporary history during the 13th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sturla was the son of Þórður Sturluson and his mistress Þóra, and grandson of Sturla Þórðarson the elder. He was a nephew and pupil of the famous saga-writer Snorri Sturluson. He fought alongside Þórður kakali Sighvatsson during t
2 CONC he Age of the Sturlungs.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is best known for writing Íslendinga saga, the longest saga within Sturlunga saga, and Hákonar saga Hákonarsonar, the story of Haakon IV of Norway. He also wrote a saga of Haakon's son, Magnus the lawmender (Magnúss saga lagabœ
2 CONC tis), of which only fragments have survived. Some scholars also believe him to have written Kristni saga and Sturlubók, a transcript of Landnáma. He is moreover listed in Skáldatal as the court skald of the Swedish ruler Birger Ja
2 CONC rl.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sturla was appointed law speaker over all of Iceland for a brief period after the dissolution of the Icelandic Commonwealth, and wrote the law book Járnsíða.
2 CONT
2 CONT His brother was Ólafur Þórðarson hvítaskáld.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sturla_%C3%9E%C3%B3r%C3%B0arson
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sagnarritari, skjald og lögsögumadur 1251, lögmadur land allt 1272-6, nordan og vestan 1277-82. Bjo lengstum a Stadarholi i Saurbæ. launsonur Thordar" 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sagnarritari" (sagn-sekretær) betyder måske den, der nedskriver sagn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sturla Tordarson, även Sturla Tordsson eller Sturla Þórðarson (hans isländska namnform), född 1214, död 1284, var en isländsk hövding, lagman, historiker och skald, samt bror till Olaf Tordsson och brorson till Snorre Sturlasson. 
2 CONC Han är känd för att ha skrivet bland annat Håkon Håkonssons saga, Íslendinga saga, och den delvis bevarade Magnus Lagabötes saga.
