2 CONT 27.    ISABEL DE CLARE, d. 1220; m. in London, Aug 1189, SIR WILLIAM MARSHALL, b. prob. 1146, d. 14 May 1219 at Caversham, bur. in the Temple Church, London, 3dr Earl of Pembroke, Marshal of England, Protector, Regent of the Kingd
2 CONC om, 1216-1219, son of JOHN MARSHALL, by his 2nd wife, SIBYL, daughter of WALTER de SALISBURY, hereditary sheriff of Wilts & Constable of Salisbury Castle.  (CP I 22; IV 670 chart; V 736; X 358-364).
2 CONT
2 CONT Also page 73, line (69-27):
2 CONT
2 CONT 27.   Isabel de Clare (66-27), m. William Marshall, Earl of Pembroke. (CP X 364, and note a).
