2 CONT
2 CONT Isabel became in ward to King Henry II and remained under the royalguardianship for the space of fourteen years, when she was given inmarriage to William Marshal, who thereupon became Earl of Pembroke. [SirBernard Burke, Dormant a
2 CONC nd Extinct Peerages, Burke's Peerage, London,1883, p. 121, Clare, Earls of Pembroke]
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabel de Clare, only child and heiress of Richard de Clare (surnamedStrongbow), Earl of Pembroke, and justice of Ireland, who had been underthe guardianship of Henry II, was given in marriage by King Richard I toWilliam Marshal. 
2 CONC [Sir Bernard Burke, Dormant, Abeyant, Forfeited, andExtinct Peerages, Burke's Peerage, Ltd., London, 1883, p. 358, Marshal,Earls of Pembroke]
