2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL1.htm#GilbertClarePembrokedied1148
2 CONT
2 CONT (1173-[1185/86])
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert of Torigny records the death in 1176 of "Richardus comes de Streguel filius comitis Gisleberti" leaving "parvulum filium ex filia regis Duvelinæ"[1254].  He succeeded his father in 1176 as Earl of Pembroke, but was never in
2 CONC vested with the earldom.  
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Gilbert de Striguil, 3rd Earl of Pembroke was born on 1172 in Dublin, County Dublin, Leinster, Ireland to Richard FitzGilbert De Clare, Earl of Pembroke and Eva MacMorrough De Clare.  He passed away on 1185 in Dublin, County Dubli
2 CONC n, Leinster, Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilbert de Striguil "Chepstow,"3rd Earl of Pembroke is my 28th great uncle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT * 1.  [http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=gonefishin&id=I134970]
