2 CONT Name: John Fitzthomas ?Of Callan? Fitzgerald Suffix: Lord Of Decies & Desmond Sex: M Death: 24 JUL 1261 in Callan, nr Kenmare, Co. Kerry, Ireland Burial: Dominican Friary, Tralee, Ireland Residence: Shanid 1 Cause: Killed in battl
2 CONC e, with son Note: 2
2 CONT
2 CONT     ?Think he founded Tralee, Co.Kerry, c.1216?
2 CONT     Founded Dominican Friary, Tralee, 1243 (note he is NOT Baron of Offaly).
2 CONT     Created his 3 sons Knights 1259.
2 CONT     Died in Battle of Callan, nr Kenmare, Co.Kerry, 1261 (NOT 1216), when Norman advance was halted in S Kerry.
2 CONT     ---
2 CONT     Married (first) Margery, daughter and heir of Sir Thomas Fitz-Anthony, Lord of Decies and Desmond. These domains were confirmed to him by Prince Edward in 1260.
2 CONT     He married (second) Honora, daughter of Hugh O'Connor, of Kerry.
2 CONT     By his first wife he had a child:
2 CONT     1. Maurice Fitz-John Fitzgerald, who was Lord of Decies and Desmond, and ancestor of the Fitzgeralds, Earls of Desmond, who ranked among the most powerful nobles of Ireland for more than two centuries.
2 CONT     Children of second wife:
2 CONT     2. Gilbert Fitz-John, ancestor of the White Knight.
2 CONT     3. Sir John Fitz-John, mentioned below.
2 CONT     4. Maurice Fitz-John, ancestor of the Knight of Kerry.
2 CONT     5. Thomas Fitz-John, ancestor of the Fitzgerald of the Island of Kerry.
2 CONT     John Fitz-Thomas Fitzgerald, by virture of his royal seigniory as a Count Palatine, created three of his sons by the second marriage, knights; and their descendants have been so styled in acts of parliament, patents under the 
2 CONC great seal, and all legal proceedings, up to the present (1910) time. He founded the monastary of Tralee, and was buried there in 1260.
2 CONT     ---
2 CONT     The Geraldines were defeated by Connor O'Brien in Thomond, and again at Kilgarvan, near Kenmare, by Fineen MacCarthy. The Annals of Innisfallen give long details of this engagement, the sight of which is still pointed out by t
2 CONC he country people. John FitzThomas, the founder of the Dominican Monastery at Tralee, was killed. The MacCarthys immediately proceeded to level all the castles which had been erected by the English; they were very numerous in that
2 CONC  district. Soon after the hero of the fight was killed himself by the De Courcys.
2 CONT
