1 NOTE {geni:about_me} = Nicholas de Carew, of Carews Castle=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of William Fitz Odo de Carew and Avice Ireland 
2 CONT * Note: Nicholas de Carew, a minor in September 1213, ward of William Fitz John de Harptree, a Somerset knight, until after March 1224 when he succeeded his father as Lord of Carew, Pembrokeshire, Cymru; Moulsford, Berkshire, Engl
2 CONC and, & Idrone, County Carlow, Ireland. He died before July 1228 leaving "heirs" supposedly female who died before reaching marriageable age. In July 1228, Moulsford manor was committed to Bertram de Crioil, Constable of Dover, for
2 CONC  his maintenance in the king's service during pleasure. In the following September, the grant was extended until the heir of Nicholas should come of age. John le Marshal endeavored to gain the custody of the lands and heir of Nich
2 CONC olas Carew in December 1230 and Crioil was disseised, but restored again in November 1234. 1 2 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/CAREW1.htm#Nicholas%20De%20CAREW%20of%20Carew%20Castle The Tudor Place]
2 CONT
2 CONT =Katherine de Courcye Married Nicholas De CAREW of Carew Castle=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Father: William De CAREW (B. Odrone)
2 CONT * Mother: ?
2 CONT * Died: BEF Jul 1228
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Notes'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas De Carew and John Marshall had the custody of Moulsford manor for a short time after his death. In Jul 1228, the manor was committed to Bertram De Crioil, Constable of Dover, for his maintenance in the king's service duri
2 CONC ng pleasure. In the following Sep, the grant was extended until the heir of Nicholas should be of age. John Marshall endeavored to recover the custody of the lands and heir of Nicholas Carew in 1230 and Crioil was disseised, but r
2 CONC estored again in 1232.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children:=
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. '''William De CAREW'''
2 CONT
