1 NAME Tadgh Glinne /O'Neil/ King of Ulster
2 GIVN Tadgh Glinne
2 NSFX King of Ulster
2 _MARNM O'Neil
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1105
2 PLAC Ireland
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1129
2 ADDR
3 STAE Ulster
3 CTRY Ireland
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Tadhg Glinne O'Neill (also recorded as Teige of the Glinnes or Tiege O'Neill) was born circa 1090–1120. His traditional death date is recorded in genealogical tracks in the mid-to-late 12th century. His epithet "Glinne" translates
2 CONC  to "of the Glens", denoting the rugged valley districts of Antrim and north-central Ulster where his branch consolidated their cattle herds and territorial strongholds.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Conchobar na Fiodhbhuidhi O'Neill, King of Ulster.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Wives: Unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the father of Muircheartach Muighe Line O'Neill (Murtagh of Moylinny), who was his direct biological son and successor.His historical significance is defined by his role as a territorial commander. He successfully preserved
2 CONC  the family's geographical assets in eastern Ulster during the intense multi-generational warfare against the Mac Lochlainn dynasty, providing the vital survival link that allowed the core O'Neill line to endure.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 👑 The Royal O'Neill Lineage
