2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: The Children of Owain Gwynedd; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id302.html [ NOTE: besides the Gwenllian born to Owain Gwynedd and Gladys ferch Llywarch, Bartum charts an illegitimate Gwenllian, born 
2 CONC to an unknown mistress, and married to 1) Hwfa ap Cynwrig and 2) Cadwgan of Nannau.(https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173392989825) Wolcott charts two illegitimate Gwenllians, 1) born c.1125, married to Cadwgan, an
2 CONC d 2) born c. 1135 and married to Hwfa. He bases this on the dating of Gruffudd ap Cadwgan to c.1155, based on his marriage to Gwenllian/Angharad ferch Dafydd ap Owain Gwynedd of c. 1170. This would preclude a Gwenllian, married to
2 CONC  Cadwgan and having son Gruffudd at c. 1155, from having a daughter with Hwfa in c. 1150 (Angharad ferch Hwfa.) However, if these dates do not hold up, there is the possibility that a Gwenllian born c,1125 could have been married 
2 CONC first to Cadwgan, having his children, and then marrying Hwfa and having Angharad.]  (Steven Ferry, September 11, 2022.)
2 CONT
