1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''''''Margery de Burgh (died after 1 March 1253), was a Norman- Irish noblewoman and the wife of Theobald Le Botiller. She was a descendant of Brian Boru, High King of Ireland, and the ancestress of the Earls of Or
2 CONC mond.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''''''Margery de Burgh was born in Ireland, the eldest daughter of Richard Mor de Burgh, Lord of Connacht and Justiciar of Ireland, and Egidia de Lacy. She had three brothers and three sisters, including Walter de Burgh, 1st Earl 
2 CONC of Ulster who married Aveline FitzJohn, by whom he had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''''''Margery's paternal grandparents were William de Burgh and More O'Brien, a granddaughter of Dermot MacMurrough,[1] and a descendant of Brian Boru. Her maternal grandparents were Walter de Lacy, Lord of Trim Castle in Meath an
2 CONC d Ludlow Castle in Shropshire, and Margaret de Braose.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''''''Sometime before 1242, Margery married Theobald Le Botiller (1224–1248), the eldest son of Theobald le Botiller, Chief Butler of Ireland and his first wife, Joan, daughter of Geoffrey de Marsh (or Mareys), Knt., Justiciar of 
2 CONC Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''''''Margery and Theobald had two children:
2 CONT * Theobald Le Botiller (1242- 26 September 1285), who married, in 1268, Joan FitzJohn ( died 26 May 1303), daughter of John FitzGeoffrey, Justiciar of Ireland, and Isabel Bigod. Joan was a younger sister of his uncle's wife, Aveli
2 CONC ne FitzJohn. The marriage produced issue, from whom descended the Earls of Ormond.
2 CONT * Elizabeth Butler (Le Botiller)
2 CONT
2 CONT ''''''Margery's husband died in 1248. He was buried before 3 August 1248 at Arklow, Co. Limerick. On 27 April 1250, she made a fine to remarry.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT ''''''Margery de Burgh died on an unrecorded date after 1 March 1253.
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT * 1.^ Charles Cawley, Medieval Lands, Earls of Ulster
2 CONT * 2.^ thePeerage.com
2 CONT * 1.Charles Cawley, Medieval Lands, Earls of Ulster
2 CONT
