1 OCCU 2nd Clan Chief of Clann Gunn
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Snaekollr''' (c1175-after 1231). His given name means "White Head". Victorian clan histories claim him as 2nd Chief of Clan Gunn. He was said to have been the son of [http://www.geni.com/people/Gunni-Andresson/6
2 CONC 000000003828029572 Gunni], the first chief, by [http://www.geni.com/people/Ragnhildr-Staegbrellsd%C3%B3ttir/6000000003828029579 Ragnhildr Staegbrellsdóttir], but seems to have been Ragnhildr’s brother rather than her son. He left 
2 CONC no known descendants although he is often said to be father of [https://www.geni.com/people/%C3%93ttarr-Snaekollson/6000000003828029636 Óttarr Snaekollson].
2 CONT
2 CONT His patronymic is not given in primary sources. If he was a brother of Ragnhild, he was '''Snaekollr Eiríksson'''. If he was her son, he was '''Snaekollr Gunnason'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT Snaekollr inherited estates in Caithness and Sutherland. He was among the rival heirs of the ancient jarls of Orkney. He came to represent one of two rival lines descended from [https://www.geni.com/people/Thorfinn-Sigurdsson/6000
2 CONC 000001052002306 þórfinnr Sigurdsson], Jarl of Orkney, who died in 1064. þórfinnr's elder son [http://tinyurl.com/ze9pv2o Páll þórfinnsson] was ancestor of the later Jarls and ultimately of the Sinclair Earls of Caithness. His youn
2 CONC ger son [https://www.geni.com/people/Erlend-Thorfinsson-Jarl-of-Orkney-and-Caithness/6000000003646023907 Erlendr þórfinnsson] founded a line that included Jarls Saint Magnús, Rögnvaldr Kali, and Haraldr Ungi. Snaekollr was a nephe
2 CONC w of Haraldr Ungi.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is said to have built Castle Gunn at Bruan, on the east coast of Caithness south of Wick. Only the foundations of that castle now remain. There is a tradition that Castle Gunn was destroyed by the King of Norway, whose daughter
2 CONC  one of the Gunn chiefs had married, though he already had a wife at Castle Gunn. When the second wife sailed to Caithness to join her husband, the Gunn clan arranged for the beacon to be placed on a dangerous rock at Ulbster and 
2 CONC so wrecked the ship and all aboard were drowned. The castle was destroyed in revenge and the Gunn chief and his retainers were slain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Snaekollr's land claims involved him in many wars with his cousins. He murdered his cousin [https://www.geni.com/people/Jon-Haraldsson/6000000002188364998 Jon Haraldsson], the last Norwegian jarl, in a dispute over lands. By that 
2 CONC murder, he lost the war and any hope of gaining the title himself. After the murder, he fled to Kelben Hougas Castle on the Island of Weir. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1232 he went to Bergen to claim Earl Jon's inheritance and lived out the remainder of his life of his life there. In 1239 he was arrested by the king’s men as a rebel in the service of the rebel Duke Skule. He was probably exec
2 CONC uted. (''Hákonar saga Hákonarsonar'') There is no proof Snaekoll married, had a child or returned to Scotland.
2 CONT
