1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT " Maud Marshal, Countess of Norfolk, Countess of Surrey (1192 – 27 March 1248) was an Anglo-Norman noblewoman and a wealthy co-heiress of her father William Marshal, 1st Earl of Pembroke, and her mother Isabel de Clare suo jure 4t
2 CONC h Countess of Pembroke. Maud was their eldest daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT She had two husbands: Hugh Bigod, 3rd Earl of Norfolk, and William de Warenne, 5th Earl of Surrey.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maud was also known as Matilda Marshal."
2 CONT
