1 NOTE {geni:about_me} First Name  	Sybil , Sibyl or Sibilla
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Name 	de Ferrers or Marshall
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth Date 	1191, 1193, 1195, 1201, 1204 or 1209
2 CONT
2 CONT Death Date 	1238 or 1254 or 4/27/1245
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/99QR-57N
2 CONT
2 CONT All five of William and Isabel Marshal’s sons (Sibyl's brothers) died without any children, and the division of all the lands these two individuals inherited, acquired, and held would eventually be split among the children of thei
2 CONC r five daughters. There is no direct male lineal descent from William Marshal’s line. Of his five sons, three died in unexplained and/or undiscovered manner, Richard was murdered, and Gilbert died in a tournament. There are many u
2 CONC nanswered questions about William Marshal’s sons.
2 CONT
2 CONT The five daughters of Marshal were all married, some more than once, and all had children. The daughters will be presented in regard to whom they married and the names of the children they had by each marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sibyl (or Sybil or Sibilla) 
2 CONT
2 CONT (b c1201-d 1245) married, before 1219, William de Ferrers, 5th Earl of Derby, and they had seven daughters. 
2 CONT
2 CONT These daughters were: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes (d1290) who married William de Vesci of Alnwick; Isabel (d1260) who married Gilbert Basset of Wycombe; Maud (d 1299) who married Simon de Kyme of Sotby; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sybil (d 1173/4) who married Franco de Bohun of Midhurst; Joan (d1268) who married John de Mohun of Dunster; Agatha (d1306) who married Hugh de Mortimer of Chelmarsh; and 
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor (d1274) who married William de Vaux. Sibilla died after 1238 and William de Ferrers died in 1254.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Problems here. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) according to FMG Sibyl Marshall d. bef 1238 when her husband William Ferrers m. Margaret de Quiincy 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) according to tudorplace and royalancestry, Sibyl d. 1245, m2 Ingeram Pratellis, m3 Walter Dunstanville.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thoughts? 
2 CONT
2 CONT (Janet Palo-Jackson, Sep 16, 2010, curator)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sibyl Marshall was born circa 1209 at Pembroke, Pembrokeshire, Wales.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was Christened in 1209 at St. David's, Pembroke, Pembrokeshire, Wales.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married William de Ferrers, circa May 13, 1219, at Pembroke, Pembrokeshire, Wales.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sibyl Marshall was third daughter and co-heir of Sir William Marshal by Isabel de Clare.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was heiress of Kildare at Leinster, Ireland, between 16 March 1219 and 1245.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sibyl married William III, 5th Earl of Derby, son of William II, 4th Earl of Derby and Alice of Chester, before 14 May 1219.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sibyl died before 1238.
2 CONT
2 CONT See "My Lines"
2 CONT
2 CONT ( http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/p391.htm#i8278 )
2 CONT
2 CONT from Compiler: R. B. Stewart, Evans, GA
2 CONT
2 CONT ( http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/index.htm ).
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT When Sibyl, Countess of Derby MARSHAL was born in 1201, her father, William, was 55, and her mother, Lady, was 29. She married Sir William, 5th Earl of Derby FERRERS on May 14, 1219, in Pembroke, Pembrokeshire, Wales. They had sev
2 CONC en children in 18 years. She died on April 27, 1245, at the age of 44.
2 CONT
