1 NOTE Eve/Eva (d1246) married William de Braose (Briouze), son of Reginald deBraose, before 1219. They had four daughters, and William de Braose washanged by Llywelyn ap Iorwerth in 1230. The stated reason for the hangingwas the accusat
2 CONC ion that William had dallied with Llywelyn’s wife Joan,bastard of King John. This does not withstand close scrutiny, and Williamwas in all probability hung for the crimes of his grandfather, William deBraose lord of Bramber and Ab
2 CONC ergavenny, against the Welsh.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eve’s and de Braose’s daughters were: Maud/Matilda (d1301) who marriedRoger de Mortimer of Wigmore; Isabel (d?) who married (1229) David(d1246), son of Llywelyn ap Iorwerth; Eve (d1255) who married William deCantelou; and Eleanor 
2 CONC (d c 1250) who married Humphrey de Bohun earl ofHereford. It is worth noting that Eve’s daughter, Isabel, was married tothe son of the man who had hung her father. Her fate is not known exceptfor the fact that she and David had no
2 CONC  children. There are records ofletters between Isabel’s uncle William, her mother Eve, and Llywelynabout her marriage contract to David after her father’s death. Given thetime period and known practices, it must be assumed that Is
2 CONC abel’s uncle,William, decided that the marriage was necessary for the good of the“feudal” family.
1 NOTE !Place of, Gower, Glamorganshire, Wales Or Pembroke, Pembrokeshire, Wales
1 NOTE Source: "The Rufus Parks Pedigree" by Brian J.L. Berry. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 80 Chart:  EVE MARSHALL
2 CONT
2 CONT !Availability: The libraries of Ken, Kevin, Karen, Kristen, Brian, Adam, Amy, and FAL.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: "Ancestral Roots of Sixty Colonists" by Frederick Lewis Weis
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 73, line: (66-28 & 67-28):
2 CONT
2 CONT 28. -- EVE (or EVA) MARSHALL, d. bef 1246; m. WILLIAM DE BRAIOSE (177-8), BRAOSE or BRIOUZE), d. 2 May 1230, 6th Baron de Braiose and a descendant of Griffith, King of Wales. (CP I 22; IV 670 chart III;IX 276; X 364 note e).
2 CONT
