1 NAME Maurice FitzThomas /FitzMaurice/
2 GIVN Maurice FitzThomas
2 SURN FitzMaurice
2 _MARNM FitzMaurice
1 NAME Maurice FitzThomas Fitzmaurice, 2nd Lord of Kerry
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1240
2 PLAC Ireland
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 14 APR 1305
2 PLAC Mayflayth, Kerry, Ireland
2 ADDR
1 OCCU 1st Baron of Kerry and Lixnaw
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Maurice fitzThomas fitzMaurice, 2nd Baron of Kerry
2 CONT
2 CONT According to one record, Maurice was lying on his deathbed 14 April 1305 (Justiciary Rolls, Vol. II, p. 422)79. Maurice sat in the Parliament held in Dublin in 1295, and attended Edward I in 1297, with horse and arms, in an expedi
2 CONC tion against Scotland in compliance with a writ of summons79.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Burke's Peerage79, Maurice (2nd Baron) married firstly, Elena, daughter and heiress of William FitzElie, with whom he got Listowel and other lands in Kerry, and by her had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Nicolas, 3rd Baron of Kerry
2 CONT     Peter. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Maurice married secondly, Sibilla, and by her had a son, Gerald79.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 2 Nov. 1304, Sibilla sued for her dower in the lands of her husband which he had acquired by his first marriage (Plea Roll 32 Edward I)79.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maurice (2nd Baron) died at Mayflayth (Molahiffe) in Kerry near Easter 1305. Another story says that he died in 130479.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Cusack86, Maurice (2nd Baron) married Mary MacLeod, daughter of Sir John MacLeod. Such a marriage would be plausible since the Norse clan of MacLeod was probably allied with the Norman King Edward I in his war against
2 CONC  the Gaels of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John MacLeod was a descendant of either Tormod or Torquil sons of Leod (for whom the clan was named) son of Olaf the Black descendant of Harald Hardraada who married the daughter of Yaroslav the Wise, Prince of Kiev.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Hardraada" means hard-speaker or judge or ruler. Harald Hardraada was in Kiev in the eleventh century. He was a descendant of the Vikings who had invaded Russia from Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Magnus, the last Norse King of Man (died in A.D. 1265), was the brother of Olaf the Black.
2 CONT
2 CONT The fact that the two sons of Maurice (2nd Lord) by his first wife were named Nicholas and Peter is certainly suggestive of Russian ancestors.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sibilla" probably comes from "Isibéal", the French form of "Elizabeth".
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://fitzmaurice-family.com/irish.html
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT 2nd Baron of Kerry
2 CONT
2 CONT According to one record, Maurice was lying on his deathbed 14 April 1305 (Justiciary Rolls, Vol. II, p. 422)79. Maurice sat in the Parliament held in Dublin in 1295, and attended Edward I in 1297, with horse and arms, in an expedi
2 CONC tion against Scotland in compliance with a writ of summons79.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Burke's Peerage79, Maurice (2nd Baron) married firstly, Elena, daughter and heiress of William FitzElie, with whom he got Listowel and other lands in Kerry, and by her had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Nicolas, 3rd Baron of Kerry
2 CONT     Peter. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Maurice married secondly, Sibilla, and by her had a son, Gerald79.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 2 Nov. 1304, Sibilla sued for her dower in the lands of her husband which he had acquired by his first marriage (Plea Roll 32 Edward I)79.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maurice (2nd Baron) died at Mayflayth (Molahiffe) in Kerry near Easter 1305. Another story says that he died in 130479.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Cusack86, Maurice (2nd Baron) married Mary MacLeod, daughter of Sir John MacLeod. Such a marriage would be plausible since the Norse clan of MacLeod was probably allied with the Norman King Edward I in his war against
2 CONC  the Gaels of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John MacLeod was a descendant of either Tormod or Torquil sons of Leod (for whom the clan was named) son of Olaf the Black descendant of Harald Hardraada who married the daughter of Yaroslav the Wise, Prince of Kiev.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Hardraada" means hard-speaker or judge or ruler. Harald Hardraada was in Kiev in the eleventh century. He was a descendant of the Vikings who had invaded Russia from Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Magnus, the last Norse King of Man (died in A.D. 1265), was the brother of Olaf the Black.
2 CONT
2 CONT The fact that the two sons of Maurice (2nd Lord) by his first wife were named Nicholas and Peter is certainly suggestive of Russian ancestors.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sibilla" probably comes from "Isibéal", the French form of "Elizabeth".
2 CONT
2 CONT At least one genealogist205 has written that Maurice (identified here as the 2nd Baron) was actually the 1st Baron of Kerry. If he is correct, then the numbers for the other Barons of Kerry must be changed accordingly. I have not 
2 CONC yet seen any quotation of a primary source that might resolve this question. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://fitzmaurice-family.com/irish.html
