1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''Complete Peerage'' erroneously calls her a sister of William le Marshal, Earl of Pembroke, not his sister. She was his niece. See the relevant discussion at [https://groups.google.com/forum/?hl=en&fromgroups#!sea
2 CONC rchin/soc.genealogy.medieval/margaret$20le$20gras/soc.genealogy.medieval/ZPIUJnysSYo/RXmUaVC8uZoJ soc.genealogy.medieval]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Historian Douglas Richardson bases his proposition on John Hunt's book, Lordship and the Landscape  (1994), which discusses the early history of the Somery family.  "On pages 34–35," Richardson writes, "he presents concrete eviden
2 CONC ce from the Brooksby Cartulary that Ralph de Somery's wife, Margaret, was actually the daughter of William le Gras, which William is thought to have been married to a sister of Earl William Marshal.  Thus, it would appear that Mar
2 CONC garet de Somery was the Earl's niece,"
2 CONT
2 CONT This makes the following models obsolete:
2 CONT
2 CONT =<nowiki>---------------------------------</nowiki>=
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret MARSHALL [Pedigree]
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of John FITZGILBERT (1106-1165) and Sybil de Salisbury (1120-)
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Sir Ralph de SOMERY Baron Dudley (1151-1210)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: [listed under entry for Ralph de SOMERY]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. "Some Early English Pedigrees",
2 CONT
2 CONT          Vernon M. Norr.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. "Ancestral roots of certain American colonists who came
2 CONT
2 CONT          to America before 1700",
2 CONT
2 CONT          Frederick Lewis Weis, 1992, seventh edition.
2 CONT
2 CONT          The earlier editions were called: "Ancestral roots of
2 CONT
2 CONT          sixty colonists who came to New England 1623-1650"
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Marshal1
2 CONT
2 CONT F, #129624
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=18 Sep 2004
2 CONT
2 CONT      Margaret Marshal is the daughter of John Marshal.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Margaret Marshal and Sir Ralph de Somery
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan de Somery+1 d. a 1273
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct 
2 CONC or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume II, page 127. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Margaret Marshall was a sister of William Marshal, Earl of Pembroke.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born before 1165.
2 CONT
2 CONT See "My Lines"
2 CONT
2 CONT ( http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/p54.htm#i8401 )
2 CONT
2 CONT from Compiler: R. B. Stewart, Evans, GA
2 CONT
2 CONT ( http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/index.htm )
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born before 1165.
2 CONT
2 CONT See "My Lines"
2 CONT
2 CONT ( http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/p54.htm#i8401 )
