2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p50630.htm#i506297
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothea Ross1
2 CONT
2 CONT F, #506297 Last Edited=14 Oct 2012
2 CONT      Dorothea Ross is the daughter of William de Ross, 3rd Earl of Ross and Euphemia de Berkeley.2 She married Torquil MacLeod, 2nd of the Lewes, son of Leod (?) and unknown daughter MacRailt.1
2 CONT      Her married name became MacLeod.1 Child of Dorothea Ross and Torquil MacLeod, 2nd of the Lewes
2 CONT
2 CONT Norman MacLeod, 3rd of the Lewes+2 Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S37] BP2003 volume 2, page 2530. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37] [S37] BP2003. [S37]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 - Dorothea, who married her cousin, Torquil Macleod II. of Lewis, with issue.
2 CONT Dorothea, daughter of William, second O'Beolan Earl of Ross by his wife, Joan, daughter of John the first Red Comyn, and sister of John the Black Comyn, Lord of Badenoch and Earl of Buchan. [ http://www.fullbooks.com/History-Of-Th
2 CONC e-Mackenzies1.html ]
2 CONT
2 CONT another source shows her as daughter of her brother William the 3rd Earl.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT William, 3rd Earl of Ross, married a lady named Euphemia, who was likely the daughter of Sir Hugh de Berkeley, Justiciar of Lothian.[7] They had three sons and two daughters:[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT * Hugh, Earl of Ross
2 CONT * Sir John Ross, married Margaret Comyn, daughter of John, Earl of Buchan
2 CONT * Sir Walter Ross, killed at Bannockburn
2 CONT * Isabella Ross, married Edward Bruce, Earl of Carrick
2 CONT * Dorothea Ross, married Torquil MacLeod of Lewis
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William,_3rd_Earl_of_Ross Wikipedia]
