1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT Conn O'Neill was born circa 1125 in Ulster, Ireland. He was slain in battle in the mid-to-late 12th century during the intense dynastic wars of Central Ulster. His death location is recorded as Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Tadhg Glinne O'Neill.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Wives: Unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Lineal descendants who established the southern septs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Conn operated during the early, turbulent formative generations of the Cenél nEógain dynasty in Ulster. While his brother Muircheartach's line remained in the north to contest the Ulster kingship, Conn's lineage ultimately shifted
2 CONC  southward after his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT His historical significance is defined as the foundational progenitor of the prominent O'Neill septs of Munster and South Leinster. He is generally regarded as the direct ancestral link for the O'Neills of Ballyniell (County Tippe
2 CONC rary), the O'Neills of Ooning (County Kilkenny), and the O'Neills of Lisronagh (County Tipperary). His legacy established a powerful, enduring O'Neill presence in the south that maintained its status independent of the senior Ulst
2 CONC er trunk line for centuries.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT #https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/O'Neill-1570
