1 NAME Sir Archibald Campbell of Lochawe
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1199
2 ADDR
3 CITY Lochowe
3 STAE Scotland
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1280
2 ADDR
3 CITY Menstrie
3 STAE Scotland
1 OCCU Lord of Lochawe, Peer of the Realm
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Campbells arrived in Argyll as part of a royal expedition in c.1220. They settled on Lochaweside where they were placed in charge of the King's lands in the area. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From Bruce's time, the family headquarters had been the great castle at Innischonnell on Loch Awe, and remained so until the 1400's when Sir Duncan Campbell (great grandson of Sir Colin) moved to to Inveraray. He was created Lord 
2 CONC Campbell and thereafter a steady string of titles were awarded to the family. His grandson was created Earl of Argyll in 1457.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sir Gillespic Campbell of Menstrie died circa 1280.1
2 CONT Sir Gillespic Campbell of Menstrie lived at Menstrie, Clackmannanshire, Scotland.1
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT FamilySearch []https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LTBC-QTH?1=1&spouse=LBSD-396
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY%20UNTITLED.htm#_Toc389126070
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ='''Sir Gillespic Campbell, 1st of Menstrie'''=
2 CONT
2 CONT Son and heir of '''Duglad Campbell'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: c. 1199
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: Wife unnamed, possibly a dau. of Sinclair of Roslin (a.k.a. St. Clair of Roslin)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sir Colin Mor Campbell, later Chief of Clan Campbell
2 CONT # Beatrice Campbell
2 CONT # Gillespic Campbell
2 CONT
2 CONT Created: 1263 1st Lord of Menstrie
2 CONT
2 CONT Died: c. 1280
2 CONT
2 CONT Tenure: 1263 - 1280
2 CONT
2 CONT Other Titles: 9th Knight of Lochow
2 CONT
2 CONT Preceded by: '''Dugald Campbell''' (b. 1161)
2 CONT
2 CONT Succeeded by: eldest son, '''Sir Colin Campbell''', 2nd of Menstrie, 1st Lord of Lochow
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Gillespic's first historical appearance dates to 1263, when he appeared in a charter of King Alexander III of Scotland, being named as "Gilascoppe Cambell". He was granted the estates of Menstrie and Sauchie in Clackmannansh
2 CONC ire.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.ccsna.org/sir-gillespic-campbell-1st-menstrie
