2 CONT  Llywelyn ap Iorwerth ~ Llywelyn Fawr (the Great)
2 CONT
2 CONT     Llywelyn ap Iorwerth Drwyndwn ab Owain Gwynedd ap Gruffudd ap Cynan[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT     Llywelyn Fawr,[2] Prince of Gwynedd (1195–1240[3]) in north Wales and eventually de facto ruler over most of Wales,[4] was also called 
2 CONT
2 CONT     Llywelyn I of Wales (Welsh: Cymru)[5]
2 CONT     Llywelyn of Cymru, of Gwynedd, of Powys Wenwynwyn[citation needed]
2 CONT     Prince of Wales[6] (1218–1240)
2 CONT     Prince of North Wales[7]
2 CONT     Prince of Powys Wenwynwyn (1216–1240)[citation needed]
2 CONT     Prince of Aberffraw[7] (1230[3])
2 CONT     Lord of Snowdon[7] (1230[3]) 
