2 CONC Llywelyn's mother was a Corbet. (See, for example,Meisel's Barons of the Welsh Frontier, which, however, does not evenmention the Welsh version of Llywelyn's maternity in JC.) However, as thesource of JC.29 appears to have been wr
2 CONC itten during Llywelyn's lifetime,and there are others ways in which an uncle-nephew relationship betweenWilliam Corbet (an obscure individual) and Llywelyn could be explained,there seems to be no good reason to reject the statemen
2 CONC t of JC.29regarding the identity of Llywelyn's mother.]
