2 CONT !RESEARCH NOTES:
2 CONT     1. The Dictionary of National Biography indicated Gwenllian, child #3 married William de Lacy and was the daughter of Llewelyn by Tanglwyst. Some of the less reliable sources indicate she was the daughter of Llewelyn by Joan, 
2 CONC Princess of England and that she married Robert de Lacy. See also notation on the family group record of the above Gwladys with her first husband, Reginald de Braose.
1 NOTE     From Ancestral File (TM), data as of 2 January 1996.
1 NOTE He ruled from 1194 until his death in 1240.
1 NOTE Source: LDS-FHC: (AFN:8HRJ-T6)
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: "The Rufus Parks Pedigree" by Brian J.L. Berry
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 79 Chart:  Llewellyn Fawr 1194-1240
2 CONT
2 CONT !Availability: The libraries of Ken, Kevin, Karen, Kristen, Brian, Adam, Amy, and FAL.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: "Ancestral Roots of Sixty Colonists" by Frederick Lewis Weis
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 149,  Line (176-7):
2 CONT
2 CONT 7.    Llewellyn ap Iorworth, The Great, 1173-1240, Prince of North Wales; m. Joan (27-27), natural dau. of John (1-26), King of England.  (CP IX 276; ASC; Turton 76, 119, 120; Jacobus: Bulkeley Genealogy 87-88).  He had a number o
2 CONC f mistreses, one of which, Tangwyltl, was the mother of Gwladys Dhu (27-28) who m. Ralph de Mortimer.
2 CONT
2 CONT !Availability: The library of Ken
