2 CONT >Duncan MacDougall of Dunollie and of Lorn, who first assumed the name of MacDougall; d 1248 ...
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donnchadh_of_Argyll
2 CONT
2 CONT Donnchadh of Argyll or Donnchadh mac Dubhghaill (Anglicized: "Duncan, son of Dougall") was a late 12th and early 13th century Scottish noble. He was the son of Dubhghall mac Somhairle, son of Somhairle mac Gille Bhrighde. He is th
2 CONC e first of the MacDougall lords of Argyll to take the title de Argadia, and can be regarded as the founder of the successful MacDougall lordship of Argyll. He was also a prominent builder, notable for his construction of Ardchatta
2 CONC n Priory and Dunstaffnage Castle.
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clan_MacDougall
