2 CONT
2 CONT =<nowiki>---------------------------------------</nowiki>=
2 CONT
2 CONT The clan takes its name from Donald, the 3rd Lord of the Isles and grandson of Somerled, who lived until 1269. Donald's son was the original "Mac" (meaning "son of"). It was Donald's great-grandson, Angus Og, the 6th Lord of the I
2 CONC sles, who sheltered Robert the Bruce at the lowest ebb of his career. Later, leading a small band of Islemen, Angus Og was instrumental in Bruce's defeat of the English at Bannockburn. This battle won independence for Scotland. In
2 CONC  recognition of Clan Donald's part in the victory, Robert the Bruce proclaimed that Clan Donald would forever occupy the honored position on the right wing of the Scottish Army.
2 CONT
2 CONT Angus Og's grandson, Donald, the 8th Lord of the Isles, married the heiress of the Earldom of Ross and in 1411 fought the Battle of Harlaw to keep his wife's inheritance from being usurped by the Regent Duke of Albany. His army of
2 CONC  10,000 men included the forces of almost every clan of the Highlands and Isles. All these clans were willing vassals of the Lord of the Isles. They regarded the MacDonald Chiefs as the heads of the ancient "Race of Conn," and lin
2 CONC eal heirs of the ancient Kings of the Dalriadic Scots, going back to the 6th century and beyond. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''' note: Birth and Death dates are best-guess estimates.
2 CONT  Recent, albeit slim, evidence has surfaced as to this man's existence in the contents of a poem addressed to him (see/read source from Wikipedia) [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Domhnall_mac_Raghnaill]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Title: Lord of the Isles
2 CONT
2 CONT  Date of Death: Domhnall (Donald, the Progenitor of Clan Donald) had a son, Angus, who reigned in the year 1249. Knowing this, we must assume Domhnall must have died before 1249. See page 13 of 95 [https://dcms.lds.org/view/action
2 CONC /ieViewer.do?dps_pid=IE1216898&dps_dvs=1377424908111~384&dps_pid=IE1216898&change_lng=en]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Children  
2 CONT   1. Alexander 'Alasdair Mor' MacDonald 
2 CONT   2. Angus Mhor 'Engull' MacDonald, of the Isles, b. 1249 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes  ◦1 - DONALD of Isla 1228 -1250 son of Rèognvald from him the name MacDonald is derived. Donald held the mainland territories of Kintyre, Morvern and Ardnamurchan with the island of Islay.
2 CONT
2 CONT  2 - The clan takes it's name from Donald "de Isla", the 3rd Lord of the Isles and grandson of Somerled, who succeeded his father Reginald, and under his guidance the clan attained great eminence. According to Highland tradition, 
2 CONC Donald made a pilgrimage to Rome to do penance and obtain absolution for the various enormities of his former life; and, on his return, evinced his gratitude and piety by making grants of land to the monastery of Saddel, and other
2 CONC  religious houses in Scotland. He died in 1269.
2 CONT  (http://www.celtic-twilight.com/atlanta/clans/macdonald/index.htm)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources  1.[S67] Macdonald genealogy, Roddy Macdonald of the Clan Donald Society of Edinburgh, (http://www.clandonald.org.uk/genealogy.htm), genealogy/d0004/g0000034.html#I0036 (Reliability: 3)
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I3880&tree=CC
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''Donald'',''' son of Reginald, and progenitor of the '''Clan Donald''', carried on the line of the Kings of Innsegall. He married a daughter of Walter Stewart of Scotland, and had two sons, who appear on record:
2 CONT 1.''' ''Angus Mor.'''''
2 CONT 2. ''Alexander'', known as Alastair Mor.
2 CONT '''
2 CONT ''Source: "The Clan Donald" Vol 3, page 180.'''''
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clan_Donald
