1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hugh or Aed was son of Milo.  and at this stage of their clans connected septs, the DE Angulo under Milo become MacGoisdealbhs(MacCostelloes) in Connacht , the Barons Navan become De Naungles in Meath/Leinster,  by
2 CONC  the 9th Baron werer called Nangle, from then on.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Nagels of Balinamona ,  Cork, in Munster,  descended  from Richard de Angulo, , kia in 1200 by ODonovan  (FOUR MASTERS) who was brother to Gilbert Mor, and one of the MAC OISTELB  (Sons of Gausslyn(jocelyn in French) from the 
2 CONC Annals.
2 CONT
2 CONT Annals of Ulster, Boyle, Loch Ce  and Clonmacnoise differ in descriptions of events from Four Masters, which was written last of all Annalas, in 1635, in Belgium..
2 CONT
2 CONT The MacDermots edited this Version of the four Masters, so it  is heavuily slanted towards their clan, eternal enemies of the MacCostelloes.
2 CONT
2 CONT This family has absolutely NO connections with Spain or the New World, their original name was a latin translation of the place they were from in Wales, Angle in Pembrokeshire. in Latin it was DeAngulo, of Angle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Prior to that this clans progenitor followed William the Conquerer to England for the Battle of Hastings, 1066, and hailed frommST Germaine Des Angles, in Normandy France, and the De Evereux  clan ( later Deverreaux) were their ll
2 CONC eige lords in France and originally in Wales.
