1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Do not confuse with Amicia/Avice de CLERE, of Yorkshire, wife of Nigel de Plumpton.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT First marriage was to Baldwin, 6th Earl of Devon (who died young). Robert de Guines obtained permission to marry her circa 1248 "if she consents", but it is not clear that she did - his wife of record in France was Maroitte, dame 
2 CONC de Hames, and she survived him.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ====FMG: England, Earls Created [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL.htm#AmiciaClaredied1283 1067–1122]
2 CONT * '''GILBERT de Clare''', son of RICHARD de Clare Earl of Hertford & his wife Amice of Gloucester ([1180]–Penros, Brittany 25 Oct 1230, bur Tewkesbury)....'''m''' (9 Oct 1214 or 1217) as her first husband, [https://fmg.ac/Projects
2 CONC /MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL1.htm#IsabelMarshaldied1240 '''ISABEL Marshal'''], daughter of WILLIAM Marshal Earl of Pembroke & his wife Isabel de Clare (Pembroke Castle 9 Oct 1200-Berkhamstead Castle, Hertfordshire 15 or
2 CONC  17 Jan 1240, bur Beaulieu Abbey, Hampshire)....Matthew Paris records that she died of jaundice contracted in childbirth[1919]. '''Earl Gilbert & his wife had six children:'''
2 CONT ** 1. '''AMICE de Clare''' (27 May 1220-27 Nov, before 21 Jan 1284). The ''Chronica de Fundatoribus et Fundatione'' '''of Tewkesbury Abbey''' records the birth in 1220 of “''filiam Amiciam” to “Gilberto…Gloucestriæ et Hertfordiæ c
2 CONC omes''” and his wife “''domina Isabella filia Willielmi Marescalli senioris, comitis de Pembroke''”[1920]. The '''Annals of Tewkesbury''' record the birth “''VI Kal Jun''” in 1220 of “''Giliberto de Clare comiti Gloucestriæ filia…
2 CONC Amicia''”[1921]. The ''Fundationis et Fundatorum Historia'' of Ford Abbey records that “''Baldwinum quartum''” married “''Amiciam filiam Gilberti de Clare comitis Gloucestriæ et Hertfordiæ''”[1922]. The '''Annals of Tewkesbury''' 
2 CONC record the marriage in 1226 of “''Amicia filia Gileberti comitis Glocestriæ''” and “''Baldwino de Ripariis comiti de Wicht''”[1923]. "G. de Clare earl of Gloucester" made a fine for the marriage of "his first-born daughter to Bald
2 CONC win, son of Baldwin de Redvers, son of William de Redvers earl of Devon", dated to [29 Oct] 1226[1924]. She is named as wife of Baldwin by Matthew Paris, who specifies that she was stepdaughter of Richard Earl of Cornwall and name
2 CONC s her mother[1925]. Henry III King of England confirmed the betrothal of "''Gilebertus de Clare comes Gloucestrie et Hertfordie…filia sua''" and "''Baldewino filio Baldewini de Riveres filii Willelmi de Riveres comitis Devoni''e" 
2 CONC dated 29 Oct 1226[1926]. '''The primary source which confirms her possible second marriage''' has not yet been identified. '''The necrology of the Priory of Saint-Martin-des-Champs''' records the death "''V Kal Dec''" of "''Amitia
2 CONC  comitissa Devonie''"[1927].
2 CONT ** '''m''' [firstly] (Betrothed 29 Oct 1226) [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL1.htm#BaldwinDevondied1245 '''BALDWIN de Reviers'''] Earl of Devon, son of BALDWIN de Reviers Earl of Devon & his wife Mar
2 CONC garet FitzWarin ([1216/17]–15 Feb 1245, bur Breamore Priory, Hampshire). 
2 CONT ** ['''m''' secondly (after 10 Jan 1248) [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORTHERN%20FRANCE.htm#RobertGuinesdiedafter1248 '''ROBERT de Guines'''], son of ARNOUL [II] Comte de Guines & his wife Beatrix de Bourbourg (–after 17 Mar 
2 CONC 1261).]
2 CONT
2 CONT ====England, Earls Created [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL1.htm#BaldwinDevondied1245 1138-1142]
2 CONT * '''Baldwin & his wife had two children:'''
2 CONT ** '''BALDWIN''' (1 Jan 1236–Paris 1262 before 13 Sep, bur Breamore Priory, Hampshire)....'''m''' (1257) as her first husband, [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SAVOY.htm#Avoiedied1292 '''AVOIE''' {Marguerite} '''de Savoie'''], [i
2 CONC llegitimate] daughter of [THOMAS I Comte de Savoie & his mistress ---] (–shortly before 14 May 1292)....Earl Baldwin & his wife had one child:...
2 CONT ** '''ISABEL''' (Jul 1237–Stockwell, Surrey 10 Nov 1293, bur Breamore Priory, Hampshire)....'''m''' (1248) as his second wife, [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/enguntdk.htm#WilliamForzdied1260 '''WILLIAM de Forz'''] Lord of Holde
2 CONC rness titular Comte d'Aumâle, son of GUILLAUME de Forz Lord of Holderness, titular Comte d'Aumâle & his wife Aveline de Montfichet ([1214/15]–Amiens 23 May 1260, bur Meaux Abbey).
