2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/L8PJ-FXZ
2 CONT
2 CONT He [William de Vescy] married, 2ndly, before 1244, Agnes, 1st daughter of William (DE FERRERS), 5th EARL OF DERBY, by his 1st wife, Sibyl, sister and, in her issue, coheir of Anselm, 9th EARL OF PEMBROKE, 3rd daughter of William (
2 CONC MARSHAL), 4th EARL OF PEMBROKE. He died in Gascony, shortly before 7 October 1253, and was buried at Watton Priory, co. York. His widow died 11 May 1290, and was buried in the Greyfriars, at Scarborough. [Complete Peerage XII/2:27
2 CONC 6-8, (transcribed by Dave Utzinger)]
2 CONT
