2 CONT 1256 Aug. 30. Westminster. <br>
2 CONT Pardon to Robert Agoylun and Joan de Mohun, late the wife of John de Mohun, for intermarrying without the king's licence, as the said Robert has made ﬁne by 200 marks with Peter de Chauvent, to whom the king had granted her marria
2 CONC ge.<br>
2 CONT Source: Calendar of the patent rolls, preserved in the Public Record Office : Henry III, 1216-1272, [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=uc1.31158002695830;view=1up;seq=509 Page 495]
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan (died 1267) married (1) Sir John de Mohun, of Dunster (died 1253) and (2) as his first wife Sir Robert Aguillon, of Addington.
2 CONT
2 CONT www.findagrave.com
