2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor was the daughter of William de Ferrieres (De Ferrers), Earl of Derby, by his 1st wife, Sybil Marshal, 3rd daughter and coheir of William (MARSHAL), Earl of Pembroke, sister of Walter, 8th Earl of Pembroke. Eleanor was the 
2 CONC widow, 1stly, of William De Vaux and, 2ndly, of Roger De Quincy, Earl of Winchester, and he died circa October 1271, being still alive in the middle of that month. Dower was assigned to his widow on November 2, 1271. She died befo
2 CONC re 26 October 1274, and was buried at Leeds Priory
