2 NOTE Pembroke Castle, Pembrokeshire Wales was the home of the Marshall family, and William Marshall, grandfather of Eva de Braose, who rebuilt it out of stone. William's sons all died childless and the castle inherited by  "William de 
3 CONC Valence (a half-brother of Henry III), who had become Earl of Pembroke through his marriage to Joan de Munchensi, William Marshal's granddaughter.
3 CONT
3 CONT The de Valence family held Pembroke for 70 years." per Wikipedia
3 CONT
3 CONT Eva never inherited this impressive castle, but would've known it, likely stayed there as it was in the family. William Marshall was her mother's father. She was however born in Bramber Castle, and apparently died in Abergavenny C
3 CONC astle. 
3 CONT
3 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pembroke_Castle
