2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ====Clan Campbell Socieity (North America) [https://www.ccsna.org/sir-colin-campbell-2nd-menstrie Sir Colin Campbell, 2nd of Menstrie]
2 CONT Sir Colin (Cailean Mór, the Great) Campbell, 2nd of Menstrie, later 1st Lord of Lochow, 9th Knight  (1230–1294)'''
2 CONT Son and heir of Sir Gillespic Campbell 1st of Menstrie.
2 CONT Created: 1st Lord of Lochow
2 CONT Other Titles: 2nd of Menstrie, Chief of Clan Campbell
2 CONT
2 CONT From "The Life of His Grace John Duke of Argyle" by his nephew Robert Campbell - 1765.
2 CONT
2 CONT The first remarkable man of this family, we find mention'd in History is Colin surnamed More, or Great; from whom the Heads of this Family are term'd in the Highland Tongue, M'calen More, or the sons of Colin More. He was one of t
2 CONC he Magnates Scotiae, that were summon'd to Berwick upon the part of Robert de Bruce, when he and all the other competitors for the crown of Scotland, on the demise of Queen Margaret, had referred the decision of their claims to Ed
2 CONC ward I. of England, He had been engaged in many conflicts, with McDougald of Lorn his neighbour, in one of which he was slain. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was succeeded by his Son Sir Neil.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Death: 1294 in String of Lorne, Scotland 
2 CONT Burial: Kilchrenan (Killed at the Red Ford in Lorne) 
2 CONT '''
2 CONT Ancestry:''' Colin Campbell of Lochow, Knight, son of Sir Gillespic Campbell of Menstrie (d ca 1280), killed ca 1294, fighting Alexander, Lord of Lorne,at the Ath-dea rg (red ford) of Lorn (where a cairn marks the site of his grav
2 CONC e). Sir Colin married, possibly a daughter of Sinclair of Roslin (alias St Clair of Roslin). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Colin Campbell of Lochow, the real founder of the family, sixth in descent from the first Gillespie, distinguished himself by his warlike actions, and was knighted by King Alexander the Third in 1280. He added largely to his e
2 CONC states, and on account of his great prowess he obtained the surname of Mohr or More ("great"); from him the chief of the Argyll family is in Gaelic styled Mac Chaillan More.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Colin Campbell had a quarrel with a powerful neighbour of his, the Lord of Lorn, and after he had defeated him, pursuing the victory too eagerly, was slain (in 1294) at a place called the string of Cowal, where a great obelisk
2 CONC  was erected over his grave. This is said to have occasioned bitter feuds betwixt the houses of Lochow and Lorn for a long period of years, which were put to an end to by the marriage of the daughter of the Celtic proprietor of Lo
2 CONC rn, with John Stewart of Innermeath about 1386. Sir Colin married a lady of the name of Sinclair, by whom he had five sons.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Sir Colin Campbell of Lochow was the son of Sir Gillespic Campbell of Menstrie.1 He died circa 1294 at Ath-dearg of Lorn, Argyllshire, Scotland, killed while fighting Alexander, Lord of Lorne.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Colin Campbell of Lochow lived at Lochow, Argyllshire, Scotland.1
2 CONT ----
2 CONT In 1296 Sir Colin Campbell the great, Cailein Mor, was killed by MacDougalls in the hills between Lochawe and the sea, a cairn of stones still marks the place.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT >aka "Great Colin" — Knighted by King Alexander III in 1280
2 CONT >Killed abt 1294 fighting Alexander, Lord of Lorne, at the Ath-dearg (Red Ford) of Lorn (where a cairn markes the site of his grave)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT The Chief of Clan Campbell takes his Gaelic title of 'MacCailein Mor' from Colin Mor Campbell - 'Colin the Great' who was killed in 1296, and was succeeded by his son Sir Neil Campbell, companion and brother-in-law of Robert the B
2 CONC ruce.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Cailean Mor Caimbeul was knighted about 1280 and appears in a charter about 1281 by Malcolm, Earl of Lennox to the lands of Luse.  He was also one of the supporters of his cousin Robert Bruce's claim to the Scottish throne and was
2 CONC  one of his advocates to King Edward I in 1291.  In 1293 he received from Sir William Lindsay the lands of Symontoun, Ayrshire and agreed to pay the feu-duty yearly to the monks of Newbattle. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Newbattle Registrum c.1293 he is called the son of "Gylascop Kambel". Cailean witnessed a charter of James Stewart to Paisley Abbey in 1295 and attested to the marriage of James to the sister of Richard de Burgh, Earl of Ul
2 CONC ster in 1296 also in the Paisley Registrum. Cailean also witnessed a charter of Maol Choluim, the contemporary Mormaer or Earl of Lennox, and in another Lennox charter in which he is granted lands in Cowal by John Lamont, one of M
2 CONC aol Chaluim's vassals. 
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1296, and perhaps by 1293, Cailean held the position of "Ballie" of Loch Awe and Ardscotnish, a position he was granted either by King John Balliol or Edward I of England. It was this position that made him the enemy for Iain o
2 CONC f Lorn, the MacDougall Lord of Lorne. Sometime after September 1296, Cailean was killed by the MacDougalls at the "Red Ford" on the borders of Loch Awe and Lorne at a place known as the String of Lorne where a cairn marks the spot
2 CONC . So many died in this battle that the stream ran red with their blood, hence the name Red Ford. His tombstone may still be seen.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Ancestor of Duke of Argyle 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Notes: from JOHN Campbell 
2 CONT Birth: Nov. 16, 1674 Drumabodan County Donegal, Ireland
2 CONT Death: 1741 Fincastle Botetourt County Virginia, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Born on his father's estate "Drumboden", 7 miles from Londonderry, Ireland. Married in 1695 to Grace Grissell Hay, daughter of Patrick Hay. In 1726, John and Grace settled in Sweet Awe, Dongal Township, Lancaster Co., Pennsylvania
2 CONC . In 1730, They moved to Fincastle Co., Virginia. Bought land in Orange, Augusta Co., Virginia. Grace lived 93 years. Many of their descendants are from Washington Co., Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had 10 children:
2 CONT # Patrick Campbell, Sr., b. 1696, Antrim, Ireland; d. March 17, 1767 in Augusta County, Virginia.
2 CONT # Arthur Campbell b. between 1697 - 1735 '''<— Disputed'''
2 CONT # Catherine Campbell b. between 1697 - 1735.
2 CONT # John Campbell, Jr., b. between 1697 - 1735 in Drumboden, Ireland.
2 CONT # Margaret Campbell b. between 1697 - 1735.
2 CONT # William Campbell b. abt. 1700 in Ulster, Ireland d. 1759 in Augusta County, Virginia. Some records state that this William Campbell married Sarah Gay, and other records state that he did not marry anyone.
2 CONT # James Campbell b. abt 1704. Had a son named Hugh Campbell Hugh 2nd marriage to Elizabeth Buchanan, has a son with 1st unknown wife named Robert Campbell.
2 CONT # David "White David" Campbell, Sr. b. March 8, 1705 or 1706 in Drumboden, Ireland d. October 17, 1790 in Washington County, Virginia.
2 CONT # Robert Campbell, Sr. b. 1708 in Drumboden, Ireland d. December 24, 1810 in Carter's Valley, Hawkins County, Tennessee.
2 CONT # Mary Campbell b. 1710 m. John Patrick Campbell b. between 1700 - 1720.
2 CONT
2 CONT John's Father: Duncan Campbell was born 1645 in Drumboden, Ireland, and died between 1700 - 1725. He 1st married Marjorie Campbell. She was born Bet. 1640 - 1653. He 2nd he married Mary McCoy in 1672. She was born in 1648.
2 CONT
2 CONT John's Grandfather: Andrew Campbell was born abt 1609, and died 1717. He married Mary Rich on December 17, 1637, daughter of Henry Rich, Earl. She was born abt 1615. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John's G-Grandfather: Hugh Campbell was born abt. 1560 in Ireland, and died aft. 1612. He married Mary Graham, daughter of William Graham. She was born Bet. 1580 - 1595.
2 CONT
2 CONT John's GG-Grandfather: Patrick Campbell was born abt. 1530 in Inverary, Argylshire, Scotland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John's GGG-Grandfather: Duncan Campbell was born Bet. 1490 - 1518 in Inverary, Argylshire, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT John's GGGG-Grandfather: Dugal Campbell was born 1480 in Inverary, Argylshire, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT John's GGGGG-Grandfather: Colin Campbell III was born abt. 1482, and died October 9, 1529. He married Jane Gordon, daughter of Alexander Gordon and Jane Stewart. She was born August 11, 1479, and died May 9, 1530.
2 CONT
2 CONT John's GGGGGG-Grandfather: Colin Campbell II was born abt. 1434. He married Marion Houstoun abt. 1460. She was born abt. 1433.
2 CONT
2 CONT John's GGGGGGG-Grandfather: Colin CAMPBELL, SR., 1ST EARL OF ARGYLL was born abt. 1433, and died May 10, 1493. He married Elizabeth Isabel Steward, daughter of John Steward. She was born abt. 1437, and died October 26, 1510.
2 CONT
2 CONT John's GGGGGGGG-Grandfather: Archibald Campbell was born Abt. 1394. He married Elizabeth Sommerville. She was born abt. 1413.
2 CONT
2 CONT John's GGGGGGGGG-Grandfather: Duncan "NA-ADH" Campbell was born abt. 1373 in Argylshire, Scotland, and died 1453 in Scotland. He married Margaret Stewart, OF Scotland on February 6, 1391 or 1392, daughter of Robert Stewart and Ana
2 CONC belle Drummond. She was born Bet. 1365 - 1380 in Renfrewshire, Scotland, and died March 4, 1459 or 1460 in Scotland. Duncan's date of birth is shown by some sources to be 1390. Margaret's date of birth is shown by some sources to 
2 CONC be April 7, 1387. Also, in some sources, her father is shown to be John Stewart. Duncan and Margaret's date of marriage is shown by other sources to be January 17, 1422.
2 CONT
2 CONT John's GGGGGGGGGG-Grandfather: Colin "Iongantach" Campbell was born abt. 1344 in Lochow, Argylshire, Scotland, and died 1413 in Scotland. He married Margaret Campbell, daughter of John Campbell. She was born 1348.
2 CONT
2 CONT John's GGGGGGGGGGG-Grandfather: Archibald More4 CAMPBELL was born abt. 1310 in Lochow, Argylshire, Scotland, and died bet. 1372 - 1392. He married Isabelle Mary Lamont, daughter of John Lamont. She was born Abt. 1318 in Lochow, Ar
2 CONC gylshire, Scotland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John's GGGGGGGGGGGG-Grandfather: Colin OIG3 Campbell was born in 1280, and died in 1340. He married Helena MOORE. She was born 1285, and died May 2, 1343.
2 CONT
2 CONT John's GGGGGGGGGGGGG-Grandfather: Neil "MacCailen More" Campbell was born 1258, and died 1315. He married Mariota Cameron. She was born abt. 1260.
2 CONT
2 CONT John's GGGGGGGGGGGGGG-Grandfather: Colin Mor1 Campbell was born 1230, and died 1294. He married Isabel Sinclair or ST. Clair. She was born abt. 1232.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Grizella Grace Hay Campbell (1677 - ____)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT John Campbell*
2 CONT Patrick Campbell (1696 - 1767)*
2 CONT David Campbell (1703 - 1790)*
2 CONT Robert Campbell (1718 - 1810)*
