1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Please see Peter Bartrum: Llywarch Howlbwrch 1; https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173393240860 & Gruffudd ap Cynan 4; https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173392980834. The mother of Gw
2 CONC ladus Ddu is given as Tangwystl ferch Llywarch Goch. Please also see Medlands: Wales; https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/WALES.htm#Gwladusdied1251, which give the mother of Gwladus Ddu as "Mistress (1) or (2)", with (1) being the af
2 CONC orementioned Tangwystl. Wolcott concurs with Bartrum in his chart "B7". (Steven Ferry, July 26, 2026.)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===From Medlands:===
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/WALES.htm#Gwladusdied1251
2 CONT (daughter of Llewellyn ap Iowerth and unknown misress)
2 CONT
2 CONT GWLADUS Ddu ("the Black") (-Windsor 1251).  The Annals of Dunstable record that “Reginaldus frater eius” (referring to “Ægidius Herefordensis episcopus”) married “Leulini Regis Walliæ…filiam” in 1216[277].  Henry III King of Engla
2 CONC nd granted protection to "Gwladosa filia…[L.] principis [Norwallie] que fuit uxor Reginaldi de Brausa" dated [May] 1229, issued at the same time as letters of protection to her brother David[278].  Henry III King of England grante
2 CONC d safe passage to "David filium L. principis Norwallier in veniendo ad regem ad faciendum ei homagium suum, et sororem ipsius David" dated 5 Sep 1229[279].  It is likely that this unnamed sister of David was Gwladus, coming to Eng
2 CONC land with her brother before her second marriage.  The Annals of Worcester record that “Radulphus de Mortuomari” married “filiam Lewelini, conjugem quondam Reginaldi de Breusa” in 1230[280].  A manuscript narrating the foundation 
2 CONC of Wigmore Abbey records that “Radulphus” married “Lewelinus princeps…Gwladusam Duy filiam suam”, who brought her husband “omnibus terries de Kery et Kedewyn”[281].  The Annales Cambriæ record the death in 1251 of "Gladus filia do
2 CONC mini Lewelini" at Windsor[282].  m firstly ([1215/16]) as his second wife, REYNOLD de Briouse, son of WILLIAM [III] de Briouse & his wife Mathilde de Saint-Valéry Dame de la Haye (-[5 May 1227/9 Jun 1228]).  He succeeded in 1215 a
2 CONC s Lord of Abergavenny[283].  m secondly (1230) RALPH de Mortimer of Wigmore, son of ROGER de Mortimer & his wife Isabel de Ferrers (-6 Aug 1246, bur Wigmore).  
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL2.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT RALPH Mortimer of Wigmore (-6 Aug 1246, bur Wigmore).  A manuscript narrating the foundation of Wigmore Abbey records that “Radulphus frater eius” succeeded on the death of “Hugo”, adding that he was born from his father´s second 
2 CONC marriage, built “duo castra…Kevencles et Knoclas”, died “VIII Id Aug 1247” and was buried “in abbathia de Wygemore”[286].  "Ralph de Mortimer" made a fine "for having seisin of the lands formerly of Hugh de Mortimer, his brother",
2 CONC  dated [Nov] 1227[287].  The Annales Cambriæ record the death in 1246 of "Radulphus de Mortuo Mari"[288].  m (1230) as her second husband, '''GWLADUS Ddu ("Dark-eyed"),''' widow of REYNOLD de Briouse, illegitimate daughter of LLYW
2 CONC ELLYN ap Iorwerth Fawr ("the Great") Prince of Wales & his mistress --- (-Windsor 1251).  The Annals of Worcester record that “Radulphus de Mortuomari” married “filiam Lewelini, conjugem quondam Reginaldi de Breusa” in 1230[289]. 
2 CONC  A manuscript narrating the foundation of Wigmore Abbey records that “Radulphus” married “Lewelinus princeps…Gwladusam Duy filiam suam”, who brought her husband “omnibus terries de Kery et Kedewyn”[290].  Ralph & his wife had five
2 CONC  children
2 CONT
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
2 CONT not listed at FMG http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/WALES.htm#Gruffydddied1244B [This statement is refuted by the above] ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT of Caernarvonshire, Cymru. Also called "the Black" because of her dark coloring.
2 CONT
2 CONT Some Corrections and Additions to the Complete Peerage, www.uk-genealogy.org.uk/cp/index.shtml, Page: I:22: Not a daughter of Joan, but of Llewellyn's mistress Tangwystl.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT 1st husband Reginald De Braose (Breos) 2nd husband Ralph (Roger) De Mortimer
2 CONT
2 CONT Burke's Guide to the Royal family states the 2nd husband was Roger De Mortimer, yet the IGI states that it was Ralph, as does Sanders. The death date of Ralph matches the death date that Burke's Guide gives for Roger, so Ralph wil
2 CONC l be the accepted husband. The IGI and Cokayne also state that Ralph married Gwladus Ddu Llewelyn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Foster, Cokayne and Sanders has her mother as Princess Joan, daughter of King John, the other wife of Llewelyn.
