2 CONT *''''''Sir Edmond Butler1
2 CONT *''''''M, #151404, d. 13 September 1321
2 CONT *Last Edited=27 May 2011
2 CONT *''''''     Sir Edmond Butler was the son of Theobald Butler and Joan fitz John.2 He married Lady Joan FitzGerald, daughter of John FitzThomas FitzGerald, 1st Earl of Kildare and Blanche de la Roche, in 1302.3 He died on 13 Septem
2 CONC ber 1321 at London, England.1,3 He was buried on 9 November 1321 at Gowran, County Kilkenny, Ireland.3
2 CONT *''''''     He was invested as a Knight in 1309 at London, England, by King Edward II.4 He held the office of Chief Governor of Ireland from 1312 to 1313.4 He held the office of Chief Governor of Ireland from 4 January 1314/15 to 
2 CONC 1317, and was active in suppressing a rebellion.4 On 1 September 1315 he received the feodum of "the Castle and manors of Karryk Macgriffyn and Roscrea", for his services against Edward Bruce and against the rebel Irish. However t
2 CONC his creation is held not to have created the title of Earl of Carrick.4
2 CONT *''''''Children of Sir Edmond Butler and Lady Joan FitzGerald
2 CONT ** 1.James Butler, 1st Earl of Ormonde+1 b. c 1305, d. 6 Jan 1337
2 CONT ** 2.John Butler+5 b. 1305, d. 1330
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S34] Peter Townend, editor, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 105th edition (London, U.K.: Burke's Peerage Ltd, 1970), psge 2048. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage, 105th ed.
2 CONT * 2.[S34] Peter Townend, Burke's Peerage, 105th ed., psge 2047.
2 CONT * 3.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume II, page 450. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT * 4.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume II, page 449.
2 CONT * 5.[S5382] Lindsay Butler, "re: Butler Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger LUNDY (101053), 26 May 2011. Hereinafter cited as "re: Butler Family."
