1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *''''''John Butler
2 CONT *M, #44215
2 CONT *Father      Theobald le Boteler (Butler) b. c 1242, d. 26 Sep 1285
2 CONT *Mother     Joan FitzJohn d. 4 Apr 1303
2 CONT *''''''     John Butler was born at of Paulstown.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1471.htm#i44215
2 CONT *_____________________
2 CONT *Theobald Butler, 4th Chief Butler of Ireland (circa 1242 – 26 September 1285) was the son of Theobald Butler, 3rd Chief Butler of Ireland and Margery de Burgh, daughter of Richard Mor de Burgh, 1st Lord of Connacht. He assisted K
2 CONC ing Edward I of England in his wars in Scotland. He died at castle of Arklow, County Wicklow, Ireland and was buried at Arklow Monastery.[1] He married Joan FitzJohn, the fourth and youngest daughter of John FitzGeoffrey, Lord of 
2 CONC Kirtling, Sheriff of Yorkshire, and Isobel Bigod and the granddaughter of Geoffrey FitzPeter, Earl of Essex.[2] She was co-heir with her three sisters to her brothers John and Richard.[3] On her marriage, she brought Theobald the 
2 CONC manor of Faubridge in Essex, the hamlet of Shippeley in Hants, the manor of Shire in Surrey, the hamlet of Vacherie and the manor of Ailesbury (in Buckinghamshire). Joan died around 1303. Their children were:
2 CONT ** Theobald Butler, 5th Chief Butler of Ireland (1269–1299)
2 CONT ** Edmund Butler, Earl of Carrick (c. 1270 – 13 September 1321)
2 CONT ** Thomas Butler, 1st Baron Dunboyne (died 9 Oct 1329)
2 CONT **'''''' John Butler
2 CONT ** Richard Butler
2 CONT ** Gilbert Butler
2 CONT ** Nicholas Butler, elected Archbishop of Dublin by the Prior and Convent of the Holy Trinity in January 1306, but was never consecrated.
2 CONT ** James Butler
2 CONT *References
2 CONT * 1.^ Lodge, John The Peerage of Ireland or, A Genealogical History Of The Present Nobility Of That Kingdom, 1789, Vol IV, p 5.
2 CONT * 2.^ The Peerage.
2 CONT * 3.^ Lodge, John The Peerage of Ireland or, A Genealogical History Of The Present Nobility Of That Kingdom, 1789, Vol IV, p 5.
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theobald_Butler,_4th_Chief_Butler_of_Ireland
2 CONT *__________________
