1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''''''Thomas Butler, 1st Baron Dunboyne (also known as Thomas le Botiller) was the third son of Theobald Butler, 4th Chief Butler of Ireland and Joan FitzJohn.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''''''He married Synolda le Petit, daughter of William le Petit[1]
2 CONT * Piers Butler, 2nd Baron Dunboyne (died 5 Aug 1370)
2 CONT * Eleanor Butler, married Gerald FitzGerald, 15th Earl of Desmond
2 CONT
2 CONT ''''''In 1324 he was called to the Irish Parliament (as were intermittently his descendants in the succeeding two centuries before the creation of the Barony of Dunboyne as a lordship of Parliament by patent 1541). He was created 
2 CONC 1st Baron Dunboyne 1324, by prescription. He fought in the Battle of Ardnocher on 9 October 1329 and was killed in action by the Chief of the Clan Geoghegan. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Ardnocher
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT * 1. ^ Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 1211.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Butler,_1st_Baron_Dunboyne
2 CONT *____________________
2 CONT *''''''Sir Thomas Butler, 1st Lord of Dunboyne1
2 CONT *''''''M, #44213, d. 1329
2 CONT *Father       Theobald le Boteler (Butler) b. c 1242, d. 26 Sep 1285
2 CONT *Mother      Joan FitzJohn d. 4 Apr 1303
2 CONT *''''''     Sir Thomas Butler, 1st Lord of Dunboyne married Synolda le Petit, daughter of William le Petit, Lord of Dunboyne.1 Sir Thomas Butler, 1st Lord of Dunboyne died in 1329.1
2 CONT *''''''Family      Synolda le Petit 
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Piers Butler, 2nd Lord of Dunboyne+1 d. 1371
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S147] Burke's Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Peerage, Baronetage, and Knightage, 1938 ed., by Sir Bernard Burke, p., 871.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1471.htm#i44213
2 CONT *_____________________
2 CONT *''''''Thomas Butler, 1st Baron Dunboyne1 
2 CONT *''''''M, #272439, d. 9 October 1329
2 CONT *Last Edited=17 Mar 2011
2 CONT *''''''     Thomas Butler, 1st Baron Dunboyne was the son of Theobald Butler and Joan fitz John. He married Synolda le Petit, daughter of William le Petit.1 He died on 9 October 1329, killed in action, by the MacGheoghan.1
2 CONT *''''''     He was also known as Thomas le Botiller.1 In 1324 he was called to the Irish Parliament (as were intermittently his descendants in the succeeding two centuries before the creation of the Barony of Dunboyne as a lordshi
2 CONC p of Parl by patent 1541), whereby what in England might have been regarded as a feudal lordship beca.1 He was created 1st Baron Dunboyne [Ireland] in 1324, by prescription.1 He fought in the Battle of Ardnurcher on 9 October 1329
2 CONC .1
2 CONT *''''''Child of Thomas Butler, 1st Baron Dunboyne and Synolda le Petit
2 CONT ** 1.Piers Butler, 2nd Baron Dunboyne+1 d. 5 Aug 1370
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 1211. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p27244.htm#i272439
2 CONT *___________________
2 CONT *''''''Thomas BUTLER (Sir)
2 CONT *''''''Died: 1329
2 CONT *Father: Theobald BUTLER
2 CONT *Mother: Joan FITZGEOFFREY
2 CONT *''''''Married: Synolda Le PETIT (dau. of William Le Petit of Dunboyne)
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Peter BUTLER of Dunboyne
2 CONT *From:  http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/BUTLER.htm#Thomas BUTLER (Sir)1
2 CONT *________________
