2 ADDR
3 STAE England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 2 JUL 1316
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/IRELAND.htm#_Toc389126214
2 CONT
2 CONT MATILDA de Burgh (-2 Jul 1316, bur Tewkesbury Abbey).  The Chronica de Fundatoribus et Fundatione of Tewkesbury Abbey records the marriage of “Gilbertus tertius” and “Matilda, filia Johannes de Borow comitis Ultoniæ”[1517].  The A
2 CONC nnales Londonienses record the marriage "ad festum Sancti Michaelis" in 1308 of "comes Claudiocestriæ" and "filiam comitis Ultoniæ de Hibernia, id est Ulstre"[1518].  The Chronica de Fundatoribus et Fundatione of Tewkesbury Abbey 
2 CONC records the death “VI Non Jul 1315” of “Gilbertus tertius…domina Matilda uxor eiusdem” and her burial “in sinistra viri sui”[1519].  m (Waltham Abbey 29 Sep 1308) GILBERT de Clare Earl of Gloucester and Hertford, of GILBERT de Cla
2 CONC re Earl of Gloucester & his second wife Joan of England "of Acre" (10/11 May 1291-killed in battle Bannockburn 24 Jun 1314, bur Tewkesbury).  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT p. 155 of "A List of Monumental Brasses in the British Isles, (pub 1926, appendiced 1938, reprinted 1964) in Tewkesbury there was listed an "indent for a brass attributed to Maud de Burgh, widow of Gilbert de Clare, earl of Glouce
2 CONC ster and Hertford, 1315, which was reproduced in M.B.S. Porffolio, III, pl. 6." 
