2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gylle_de_Burgh
2 CONT
2 CONT De Burgh was the only daughter of Sir William Liath de Burgh (died 1323) and a sister of Sir Walter Liath de Burgh. Walter was captured and starved to death by his cousin, the Earl of Ulster, in 1332.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gylle, married to Richard de Manderville, had her husband and his family kill the earl at Carrickfergus on 6 June 1333 in revenge. This murder was directly responsible for the destruction of the great de Burgh lordship of Connacht
2 CONC , and the loss of Ulster to the Gaelic-Irish till the Ulster Plantations of 1610.[1][2]
