1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Walter de Moravia, of Duffus''', d. abt. 1263, bur. at the church of Duffus, m. Euphemia Ross, daughter of Ferquhard, Earl of Ross.
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded to the lands of Duffus, and married Euphemia, daughter of Ferquhard, Earl of Ross. He died about 1263, and was buried at Duffus. His line ended in two heiresses, and his estates finally passed to the Keiths of Inverug
2 CONC ie and Sutherlands of Duffus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: Balfour Paul, J. (1911) The Scots Peerage, vol. 8. Edinburgh: David Douglas.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://sites.google.com/site/fivegateways/alphabetical-index-s/sutherland/suth0030
2 CONT
