2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E%C3%B3ghan_of_Argyll
2 CONT
2 CONT Eóghan MacDubhghaill (Anglicized: Ewan MacDougall, Ewan of Argyll or Ewan of Lorne) was a 13th-century Scottish nobleman and warrior who was styled "King of the Isles", "Lord of Argyll". He was the son of Donnchadh, son of Dubhgha
2 CONC ll, son of Somhairle mac Gille Brighde.
2 CONT ---------------
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/Dougal-MacRory-1st-of-Dunollie-and-of-Lorn/6000000005398287081 DUGALD], son of SOMERLED Lord of Argyll & his wife --- of Man (-after 1175).  The Chronicon Manniæ et Insularum names “Dulgallum, Reginald
2 CONC um, Engus et Olavum” as the four sons of “Sumerledo regulo Herergaildel” and his wife the daughter of Olav King of Man[1042].  The Obituario of Durham records that "Dusgal filius Sumerledi et Stephanus capellanus suus et Adam de S
2 CONC tanford" donated two gold rings to St Cuthbert in 1175[1043].  The Liber Vitæ of Durham names "Dunegal filius Sumerledi, et filii sui, Olaf et Dunechal et Raynald et Adam de Stanford. Stephanus Capellanus"[1044]. m [https://www.ge
2 CONC ni.com/people/Unknown-Wife-MacDougall/6000000001828593786?through=6000000005398287081 ---].  The name of Dugald’s wife is not known. Dugald & his wife had four children:
