2 CONT >*3.[https://www.geni.com/people/Duncan-MacDougall-2nd-of-Dunollie-and-of-Lorn-King-of-the-Isles/6000000002188081857?through=6000000005398287081 DUNCAN] (-[1237/48]).  The Liber Vitæ of Durham names "Dunegal filius Sumerledi, et f
2 CONC ilii sui, Olaf et Dunechal et Raynald et Adam de Stanford. Stephanus Capellanus"[1048].  The Saga of Eirspennill’s Hakon Hakon’s son records that "the kings of the Hebrides were Dugald Screech and his brother Duncan, the father of
2 CONC  John who was king afterwards…the sons of Dungal, Somerled’s son"[1049].  m [https://www.geni.com/people/NN/6000000002188081873 ---].  The name of Duncan’s wife is not known.  Duncan & his wife had three children [says Cawley, but
