1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =William de Warenne of Surrey=
2 CONT
2 CONT William was killed in a tournament at Croydon as a young man and did not live to inherit the earldom of Surrey; his son John inherited it instead.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''son of John de Warenne, Earl of Surrey, and Alex de Lusignan'''
2 CONT married '''Joan de Vere''' Children:
2 CONT * '''John de Warenne, Earl of Surrey'''
2 CONT * '''Alice de Warenne''' married Edmund FitzAlan
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL.htm:
2 CONT
2 CONT '''WILLIAM de Warenne''' (1256-murdered Croydon 15 Dec 1286).  He was ambushed and slain after attending a tournament at Croydon[1152].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ([Jun 1285]) '''JOAN de Vere''', daughter of ROBERT de Vere Earl of Oxford & his wife Alice de Sanford (-23 Nov 1293 or before, bur Lewes Priory).  
2 CONT
2 CONT William de Warenne & his wife had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT i)         ''' JOHN de Warenne''' (30 Jun 1286-29 Jun 1347, bur Lewes St Pancras).  He '''succeeded his grandfather in 1304 as Earl of Surrey'''.  He unsuccessfully attempted to divorce his wife to marry his mistress Matilda de Ne
2 CONC rford[1153].  The testament of "Johan Counte de Warenne de Surrey et de Strathorne Seigneur de Bromfeld et de Yal" is dated 24 Jun 1347, requests burial "en l´esgise Saint Pancratz de Lewes", makes bequests to "…Monsieur William d
2 CONC e Warenne mon filz…ma fille sa compaigne…Edward de Warenne mon filz…Johanne de Basyngg ma fille…Katerine ma fille…Isabell ma fille Noneyn de Sempyngham…William de Warenne mon fil…Isabelle de Holand ma compaigne"[1154].  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>m (25 May 1306) '''JEANNE de Bar''', daughter of HENRI III Comte de Bar & his wife Eleanor of England (-31 Aug 1361).  The Chronicle of Lanercost names "filium…Edwardum et filiam quam Johannes de Warenna comes duxit in uxorem" a
2 CONC s the children of "Alianora filia regis" and "Henrico comiti Barienti"[1155].  The Annales Londonienses record the marriage "VIII Kal Jun" in 1306 of "dominus Johannes de Warenne" and "filiam comitis de Bar et Elianoræ filiæ…regis
2 CONC  Edwardi"[1156].  Froissart records that "la contesse de Garanes…estoit suer au conte de Bar"[1157].  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>Mistress (1): '''MATILDA de Nerford''', wife of S. de Diriba, daughter of ---.  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>Mistress (2): '''ISABEL de Holand''', daughter of ---.  The testament of "Johan Counte de Warenne de Surrey et de Strathorne Seigneur de Bromfeld et de Yal" is dated 24 Jun 1347 and makes bequests to "…Isabelle de Holand ma comp
2 CONC aigne"[1158].  
2 CONT
2 CONT >Earl John had six illegitimate children by Mistress (1): 
2 CONT
2 CONT >(a)        JOHN Warenne (-after Jun 1347).  The testament of "Johan Counte de Warenne de Surrey et de Strathorne Seigneur de Bromfeld et de Yal" is dated 24 Jun 1347 and makes bequests to "…Monsieur William de Warenne mon filz…ma
2 CONC  fille sa compaigne…Edward de Warenne mon filz…Johanne de Basyngg ma fille…Katerine ma fille…Isabell ma fille Noneyn de Sempyngham…William de Warenne mon fil…Isabelle de Holand ma compaigne"[1159]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >(b)        THOMAS Warenne (-before 24 Jun 1347).  It is assumed that Thomas predeceased his father in whose testament he is not named. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >(c)        EDWARD Warenne (-after Jun 1347).  The testament of "Johan Counte de Warenne de Surrey et de Strathorne Seigneur de Bromfeld et de Yal" is dated 24 Jun 1347 and makes bequests to "…Monsieur William de Warenne mon filz…
2 CONC ma fille sa compaigne…Edward de Warenne mon filz…Johanne de Basyngg ma fille…Katerine ma fille…Isabell ma fille Noneyn de Sempyngham…William de Warenne mon fil…Isabelle de Holand ma compaigne"[1160].  Founder of the WARENN family 
2 CONC of Poynton. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >(d)        JOAN Warenne (-after Jun 1347).  The testament of "Johan Counte de Warenne de Surrey et de Strathorne Seigneur de Bromfeld et de Yal" is dated 24 Jun 1347 and makes bequests to "…Monsieur William de Warenne mon filz…ma
2 CONC  fille sa compaigne…Edward de Warenne mon filz…Johanne de Basyngg ma fille…Katerine ma fille…Isabell ma fille Noneyn de Sempyngham…William de Warenne mon fil…Isabelle de Holand ma compaigne"[1161].  m (before 24 Jun 1347) --- de B
2 CONC asing, son of ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >(e)        CATHERINE Warenne .  The testament of "Johan Counte de Warenne de Surrey et de Strathorne Seigneur de Bromfeld et de Yal" is dated 24 Jun 1347 and makes bequests to "…Monsieur William de Warenne mon filz…ma fille sa co
2 CONC mpaigne…Edward de Warenne mon filz…Johanne de Basyngg ma fille…Katerine ma fille…Isabell ma fille Noneyn de Sempyngham…William de Warenne mon fil…Isabelle de Holand ma compaigne"[1162].  m (after 24 Jun 1347) ROBERT Heveningham . 
2 CONT
2 CONT >(f)         ISABEL Warenne .  The testament of "Johan Counte de Warenne de Surrey et de Strathorne Seigneur de Bromfeld et de Yal" is dated 24 Jun 1347 and makes bequests to "…Monsieur William de Warenne mon filz…ma fille sa comp
2 CONC aigne…Edward de Warenne mon filz…Johanne de Basyngg ma fille…Katerine ma fille…Isabell ma fille Noneyn de Sempyngham…William de Warenne mon fil…Isabelle de Holand ma compaigne"[1163].  Nun at Sempingham. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ii)         '''ALICE de Warenne''' ([May/Jul 1287]-before 23 May 1338).  It is assumed that she was born posthumously as there was insufficient time for her birth between her parents' marriage and the birth of her brother, but no 
2 CONC proof has been found that this is correct.  m (1305)''' EDMUND Fitzalan''' Earl of Arundel, son of RICHARD FitzAlan Earl of Arundel & his wife Alasia di Saluzzo (1 May 1285-executed Hereford 17 Nov 1326). 
2 CONT =<nowiki>————————————————————————————————————-</nowiki>=
2 CONT
2 CONT >====British History Online: Inquisitions Post Mortem, Edward I, File 47; [https://www.british-history.ac.uk/inquis-post-mortem/vol2/pp377-383 633. William de Warrenna]
2 CONT >'''Writ, 15 Dec. 15 Edw. I.'''
2 CONT >'''[Oxford.] Inq. Friday after Epiphany, 15 Edw. I.'''
2 CONT >'''Croumers.''' The manor (extent given) of which the said William and Joan his wife were jointly enfeoffed by Sir Robert de Veer, earl of Oxford, father of the said Joan, to be held of Sir William de Valencia for the service of 
2 CONC 1 knight's fee.
2 CONT >John his son, born at the feast of the Nativity of St. John the Baptist, 14 Edw. I, is his next heir.
2 CONT >'''[Norfolk.]''' Extent, Thursday before St. Matthias the Apostle, 15 Edw. I.
2 CONT >'''Beston.''' The manor (extent given) including herbage in Godwynescarwe, wreck of the sea, and the advowson of the church, which Robert de Veer, earl of Oxford, gave to the said William with Joan his daughter in free marriage, 
2 CONC held of the said earl in chief for homage and service, doing 20s. yearly for the guard of the castle of Dover, and at the queen's hundred (court) of Northorpingham one suit.
2 CONT >He died on Sunday before St. Lucy in the said year. Heir as above.
2 CONT >'''Buckingham.''' Extent, Wednesday before SS. Fabian and Sebastian, 15 Edw. I.
2 CONT >'''Medmenham.''' The manor (extent given) held of the earl of Oxford by service of 1 knight's fee, and it is of the free marriage of Lady Joan his wife, who still survives.
2 CONT >'''Heir''' as above, aged ½ year at Christmas in the said year.
2 CONT >'''Essex.''' Inq. Thursday after St. Matthias (Mathi) the Apostle, 15 Edw. I.
2 CONT >'''Pritelwell.''' The manor (extent given) held of Robert de Ver, earl of Oxford, service unknown, but he held nothing of the king in chief there, for Joan his wife was enfeoffed of the manor, to herself and her heirs, four years
2 CONC  before she married the said William.
2 CONT >He died on the morrow of St. Thomas the Apostle in the said year. Heir as above, aged ¾ year.
2 CONT >'''Writ''' to Reginald de Grey, justice of Chester, to permit John de Warenna, earl of Surrey, to hold the lands of Bromfeld and Yal and the castle of Dynasbran until one month from Easter next, and to enquire in what manner the 
2 CONC said William held the same lands and castle, 12 Feb. 15 Edw. I.
2 CONT >'''Chester; Flint.''' Inq. Tuesday before St. George, 15 Edw. I.
2 CONT >The jury know not whether the said William held Bromfeld and Yal and the castle of Dynasbran in his demesne as of fee or for his life or otherwise ; but Master Walter de la Mare and Robert de Tumele by command of John de Warenna,
2 CONC  earl of Surrey, on Thursday after St. Peter ad Vincula, 12 (Edw. I), came to Wrychtesham and delivered seisin of the same lands and castle to the said William; who took the homage of certain persons (names given) and afterwards o
2 CONC f the whole community of the country with hands joined and raised unanimously, appointed his own bailiffs, and gave certain lands of the demesnes in the towns of Sessewyc and Hunkele to Madoc Goch and David ap Howel, and took an a
2 CONC id of the whole community, &c.
2 CONT >Similar writ to Henry de Bray, escheator, concerning the manor of Scolethorp, 12 Feb. 15 Edw. I.
2 CONT >'''Norfolk.''' Inq. Tuesday before St. Gregory, 15 Edw. I.
2 CONT >'''Schulthorpe.''' The manor (extent given) including a custom called 'bussag,' and 'andlepymen' (?) whose toll is worth 24d. yearly, held of Sir John earl of Warrenn' for life, with reversion to the said earl his father.
2 CONT >He died on Sunday after St. Lucy in the said year. Heir as above, aged 38 weeks on Tuesday before St. Gregory in the said year.
2 CONT >'''C. Edw. I. File 47. (13.)'''
2 CONT =<nowiki>————————————————————————————————————-</nowiki>=
