2 CONT <br />  Gilbert de Clare, son of the last earl (but five years old at his father`s death) succeeded upon his mother`s death on 10 May 1305, and the said Ralph`s formal surrender thereof of the title in 1307, the inheritance was di
2 CONC vided between his sisters in 1316, who were:  (1) Eleanor, m. to Hugh le Despencer, the younger son of Hugh, Earl of Gloucester.  (2) Margaret, m. 1st to Piers Faveston, Earl of Cornwall, and 2ndly, to Hugh de Audley, created Earl
2 CONC  of Gloucester after her brother`s death.  (3) Elizabeth, m. 1st. to John de Burgh who d. before his father, Richard, Earl of Ulster; 2ndly to Theobald, Lord Verdon, and 3rdly, to Roger D`Amory, Baron of Armoy.  (4) Sybil, 4th dau
2 CONC . and co-heir of William Mareschal, Earl of Pembroke and Lord of Leinster, married William de Ferrers: Earl of Ferrers, Nottingham and Derby, LORD OF KILDARE, 1245. He
