2 CONT
2 CONT Juliana, daughter of William de Vescy, of Alnwick, Northumberland, and Malton, Yorks, by Agnes, daughter of William de Ferrers, 5th Earl of Derby of the 1138 creation, thus acquiring Arleston, Derbys. [Burke's Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://wc.rootsweb.com/trees/162642/I13274/julianade-vesci/registry
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Richard de Vernon on BEF 1283 in 2nd wife, son of Richard de /Vernon/, of Nether Haddon, Sir and Margaret de /Vipont/. He was born ABT 1253 in Nether Haddon, Bakewell, Derbyshire, England, and died AFT 1330 in Harlasto
2 CONC n, Tamworth, Staffordshire, England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Juliana de /Vesci/, Heiress of Harlaston and Richard de /Vernon/, of Nether Haddon, Sir are:
2 CONT #Richard de Vernon was born ABT 1283 in Nether Haddon, Bakewell, Derbyshire, England, and died BEF 3 FEB 1322/23 in Harlaston, Tamworth, Staffordshire, England (dvp).  Married: Maud de Camville
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disputed Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://groups.google.com/g/soc.genealogy.medieval/c/368MqUvT_c4/m/fxqLROhp9wkJ John P. Ravilious, January 2001
2 CONT
2 CONT There was a thread on the Vernons of Harleston, co. Derby (spelled 
2 CONT Harlaston in the thread) back around May 2001 - this also got into some of 
2 CONT the confusing issues re: the earlier generations.
2 CONT
2 CONT I haven't attempted to propose a definite line for the Vernons of 
2 CONT Harleston prior to the generation you have brought up, primarily because I 
2 CONT have not found sufficient sources to help sort out the confusion (the two 
2 CONT sources I have to hand being a partial account from Burke's, and the Vernon  pedigree from R. Barnes, British Roots of Maryland Families [1999]).
2 CONT
2 CONT The record from CP seems to concur with the MC 5th edition version, that 
2 CONT the descent from de Vesci died out [thereby negating the line given in AR7]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The table of descent from William de Ferrers, Earl of Derby (d. bef 29 Mar 
2 CONT 1254) by Sibyl le Marshal, given in CP Vol IV (Derby), p. 199, shows the 
2 CONT following:
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes = William de Vescy
2 CONT d. 11 May 1290 I of Alnwick and Malton
2 CONT I d. 22 Oct 1253
2 CONT ______________I___________________
2 CONT I I
2 CONT John de Vescy William de Vescy
2 CONT dsp 10 Feb 1288/89 d.s.p.s. 19 July 1297
2 CONT I
2 CONT I
2 CONT John de Vescy
2 CONT dsp Sept 1294
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The _Final Statement_ at the end of this line in the table states, _Issue 
2 CONT of Agnes failed 1297_. This should be corroborated under any CP article 
2 CONT concerning de Vesci, which I do not have to hand; therefore, it appears that  the de Vesci connection for the Vernons of Harleston fails.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hopefully someone else has arrived at a corrected descent for Vernon down  to this generation, or will in the near future.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
