2 CONT [S2] Paget Heraldic Baronage, Paget, Gerald, (Manuscript, filmed by the Genealogical Society of Utah, 1957), chart no. 74 Bohun of Midhurst, FHL microfilm 170063 (Reliability: 3).
2 CONT =<nowiki>-----------------------------</nowiki>=
2 CONT John de Bohun/Joan de la Chapplle 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the Sealer of Writs for King Edward I. She was the daughter of William de la Chapplle, Sergeant of the King's Chapel. (from Gary Lavergne)
2 CONT =<nowiki>--------------------</nowiki>=
2 CONT Inherited Midhurst, Ford, Rustington and Sussex in England and Ireland. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Sir John de Bohun, Baron of Midhurst's Capetian lineage:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Hugh "Magnus" of Paris, count of Paris, duke of the Franks [First Capet]
2 CONT 2 Hugues Capet, roi des Francs
2 CONT 3 Robert II Capet, "the Pious" king of the Franks
2 CONT 4 Henry I, king of France
2 CONT 5 Hugues I 'Magnus', Comte de Vermandois
2 CONT 6 Elisabeth de Vermandois, dame de Crépy
2 CONT 7 Isabel de Beaumont, Concubine #15 of Henry I, Countess Of Pembroke
2 CONT 8 Richard "Strongbow" de Clare, 2nd Earl of Pembroke
2 CONT 9 Isabel de Clare, heiress of Pembroke
2 CONT 10 Sibyl Marshal, Countess of Derby
2 CONT 11 Lady Sibyl de Bohun (de Ferrers)
2 CONT 12 Sir John de Bohun, Baron of Midhurst
2 CONT ----
