2 CONT
2 CONT Agnès de Valence, dame de Danfalize, mariée à Maurice FitzGerald, baron d'Offaly, puis Hugues de Bailleul, lord de Barnard Castle et de Bywell et en troisièmes noces épouse Jean d’Avesnes, seigneur de Beaumont.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I6220&tree=CC
2 CONT
2 CONT No children by her marriage to Hugh De Baliol.
2 CONT
2 CONT Woodhorn is now much reduced in size but its most famous building is the Anglo Saxon church dedicated to St Mary. The first church on the site was probably built of wood when in 739 King Ceowulf granted land to the monks of Lindis
2 CONC farne. Inside the church is an effigy of '''Dame Agnes de Valance''', wife of Hugh Balliol, brother of Edward Balliol who was made King of Scotland by Edward I.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_I_de_Balliol
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Dervorguilla had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Hugh de Balliol, who died without issue before 10 April 1271. He married Agnes de Valence, daughter of William de Valence, 1st Earl of Pembroke.[2]
