2 CONT  Alianor de Bohun was born circa 1240 at Brecknock, Breconshire, Wales.1 She is the daughter of Sir Humphrey de Bohun and Eleanor de Briouze.1 She married Robert de Ferrers, 6th Earl of Derby, son of William de Ferrers, 5th Earl o
2 CONC f Derby and Margaret de Quinci, in 1269. She died on 20 February 1314.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Alianor de Bohun was also known as Eleanor Bohun.1 Her married name became de Ferrers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Alianor de Bohun and Robert de Ferrers, 6th Earl of Derby
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John de Ferrers, 1st Lord Ferrers (of Chartley)+ b. 20 Jun 1271, d. c 1312
