2 CONT     (5) Humphrey de Bohun VII:  (b.1251, d.December 31 or November 30, 1298,
2 CONT     Pleshy, County Essex, buried Walden).  He married July 20, 1275, Maud de
2 CONT     Fiennes, widow of John de Vescy and cousin of Queen Eleanor of England.  Hewas
2 CONT     the third Earl of Hereford and second Earl of Essex and Constable of England.
2 CONT     In 1292 he was fined and imprisoned.  In 1296/7 he escorted John, Earl of
2 CONT     Holland, who had married the Princess Elizabeth Plantagenet, daughter of King
2 CONT     Edward I, to Holland to claim his inheritance.  The princess, age 14, was
2 CONT     married two years later at age 16 to Humphrey's own son Humphrey VII after her
2 CONT     husband's death.  Until his death, Humphrey and Roger Bigod, fifth Earl of
2 CONT     Norfolk, strongly opposed Edward I's measures for arbitrary taxation and early
2 CONT     in 1297 he and Bigod refused to serve in Gascony on the plea they were not
2 CONT     bound to foreign service except in company with the king.  At a levy of the
2 CONT     military forces of the kingdom, the two earls refused to do their duty as
2 CONT     constable and marshal and both were deprived.--Aedc,FHL 929.273,C769w
