1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Margaret Mortimer==
2 CONT [http://thepeerage.com/p1203.htm#i12029]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''F'''[emale]
2 CONT * '''#'''12029
2 CONT * '''b.''' after 1307
2 CONT * '''d.''' 5 May 1337
2 CONT * Last Edited=15 Mar 2008
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Margaret Mortimer''' was born after 1307.1 
2 CONT * She was the daughter of Roger de Mortimer, 1st Earl of March and Joan de Geneville, Baroness Geneville.1 
2 CONT * She married Thomas de Berkeley, 3rd Lord Berkeley, son of Maurice de Berkeley, 2nd Lord Berkeley and Eva la Zouche, before 25 July 1320.1 
2 CONT * She died on 5 May 1337.1 
2 CONT * She was buried at St. Augustine's, Bristol, Gloucestershire, EnglandG.1
2 CONT * From before 25 July 1320, her married name became de Berkeley.1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children of Margaret Mortimer and Thomas de Berkeley, 3rd Lord Berkeley'''
2 CONT # Joan de Berkeley+2 d. 2 Oct 1369
2 CONT # Maurice de Berkeley, 4th Lord Berkeley+1 b. c 1330, d. 8 Jun 1368
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Citations'''
2 CONT # G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct or 
2 CONC Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume II, page 130. 
