1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Cantilupe-65
2 CONT
2 CONT "Milicent De Cantelowe, married (1st) John De Mohaut (or Montalt). They had no issue. She married (2nd) before 12 Dec. 1273 Eudes La Zouche, Knt., son of Roger la Zouche, by Margaret, doubtless daughter of Henry Biset. They had on
2 CONC e son, William, Knt. [1st Lord Zouche of Harringworth], and three daughters, Elizabeth, Eve, Eleanor. " [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Milicent de Cantelowe was born circa 1245 at of Calne, Wiltshire, Aston Cantlow, Warwickshire, England. She married John de Montault, son of Sir Roger de Montalt, Seneschal & Justice of Chester and Cecilia d' Aubeney, before 1254;
2 CONC  No known issue.[2] Milicent de Cantelowe married Sir Eudes la Zouche, son of Roger le Zouche, 2nd Lord Zouche, Sheriff of Devonshire and Margaret Biset, before 13 December 1273; They had 1 son (Sir William, 1st Lord Zouche of Har
2 CONC ringworth) & 3 daughters (Elizabeth, wife of Sir Nicholas Poyntz; Ela, wife of Sir Maurice de Berkeley, 2nd Lord Berkeley; & Eleanor, wife of Sir John de Harcourt).[3][4][5][6] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Milicent de Cantelowe died circa 7 January 1299.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Eudes la Zouche d. bt 28 Apr 1279 - 25 Jun 1279
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT # Elizabeth la Zouche d. bt 1297 - 9 Feb 1309
2 CONT # Eve la Zouche b . c 1271, d. 5 Dec 1314
2 CONT # Sir William la Zouche, 1st Lord Zouche of Harringworth b. 18 Dec 1276 or 21 Dec 1276, d. 11 Mar 1352 or 12 Mar 1352
2 CONT # Eleanor la Zouche b. c 1278
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Lucy-lady-of-Boketon/6000000000437831402 Is not listed as a daughter and had been detached.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Aston Cantlow''' 
2 CONT
