1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Before 1273 the manor [of North Luffenham] had been subinfeudated to George de Cantilupe, who died in that year. Half a fee in North Luffenham was assigned in 1276 to George's sister and co-heiress Milicent, wife o
2 CONC f Eudo la Zouche of Haringworth, formerly married to John de Montalt.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.british-history.ac.uk/report.aspx?compid=66234
2 CONT
2 CONT There are two implications here: one, that he died without heirs, and two, that there was at least one other sister to be co-heiress or to pass the heirship on to her offspring.
2 CONT
