2 CONT John fitz Nicholas, 4th Baron of Kerry and Lixnaw was the son of Nicholas fitz Maurice, 2nd Baron of Kerry and Lixnaw and Slany O'Brien.1 He married, firstly, Honor O'Brien, daughter of unknown O'Brien of Thomond.2 He married, sec
2 CONC ondly, Elinor fitz Gerald, daughter of Gerald fitz Pierce.2 He died circa 1378.2
2 CONT      He succeeded to the title of 4th Baron of Kerry and Lixnaw [I., c. 1295] in October 1339.1 On 10 July 1370 he was taken near Limerick by O'Biren and McCarthy, along with the Earl of Desmond and other nobles.2 He was invested 
2 CONC as a Knight before 1374.3 In August 1375 he was ordered by the King to arrest his son, Maurice FitzJohn, after Maurice seized the goods of a Bristol merchant at Tralee.2 Children of John fitz Nicholas, 4th Baron of Kerry and Lixna
2 CONC w and Elinor fitz Gerald
2 CONT
2 CONT     Garrett fitz Nicholas3
2 CONT     Robert fitz Nicholas3
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of John fitz Nicholas, 4th Baron of Kerry and Lixnaw and Honor O'Brien
2 CONT
2 CONT     Maurice fitz John fitz Nicholas, 5th Baron of Kerry and Lixnaw+2 d. c 1398
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
