2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Maurice de Berkeley "the Resolute" (1218 - 4 April 1281), 8th (feudal) Baron de Berkeley, was an English soldier and rebel, residing at Berkeley Castle in the English county of Gloucestershire.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maurice was born in 1218 to Thomas de Berkeley and Joan de Somery. He married Isabel de Croun FitzRoy, the daughter of Richard FitzRoy, Baron of Chilham (an illegitimate son of King John of England) and Rose de Douvres, sometime b
2 CONC efore 12 July 1247.
2 CONT
2 CONT Berkeley fought in the French Wars and was invested as a knight before 1242. He inherited the title of Baron de Berkeley in 1243 and, on 14 December 1243, he had livery of his father's lands. He fought in the war in North Wales an
2 CONC d in 1264 he joined the Barons against King Henry III. Berkeley died on 4 April 1281 and was buried in St Augustine's Abbey in Bristol.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sir Maurice de Berkeley and Isabel FitzRoy
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Robert de Berkeley
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.Lora de Berkeley
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.John de Berkeley, 1st Baron Marmion+ d. b 7 May 1322
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.Maurice de Berkeley1 b. b 1245, d. 1279
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.Thomas de Berkeley, 1st Lord Berkeley+1 b. 1245, d. 23 Jul 1321
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct or 
2 CONC Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume II, page 127. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT
2 CONT source: thepeerage.com
2 CONT
