2 CONT *Mother     Joan de Bryn
2 CONT *'''     Peter Gerard was born at of Kingsley, Cheshire, Byrn, Lancashire, England. He died before 1380.
2 CONT *Family 
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Sir Thomas Gerard+ d. 27 Mar 1416
2 CONT **John Gerard+ b. c 1370, d. b 1434
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S9463] Unknown author, The History of the County Palatine and City of Chester, by George Ormerod, 1819, p. 62; Burke's Peerage, 1938, p. 1079.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1019.htm#i30612 _______________________
2 CONT *'''Burke's genealogical and heraldic history of the peerage, baronetage and ... 
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=RVggAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA1189&lpg=PA1189&dq=Peter+Gerard+1380&source=bl&ots=2AfC1BmcuM&sig=zl0dKAi9XnNb52MVzsnf0ygb_dM&hl=en&ei=KXijTMmLK5OqsAPal62XAQ&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=4&ved=0CBoQ6AEw
2 CONC Azg8#v=onepage&q=Peter%20Gerard&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.841
2 CONT *   WILLIAM GERARD, who m. the dau. and heir of Peter de Bryn, of Bryn, co Lancaster, and was s. by his son
2 CONT *'''   SIR PETER GERARD, Knt. of Bryn, temp. EDWARD III., who had three sons,
2 CONT **	1. Thomas, his heir, whose line failed 1437.
2 CONT **	2. PETER, whose great grandson, SIR THOMAS GERARD, became the representative of the family.
2 CONT **	3. John, m. Helen, dau. and heir of Richard de Ince, co. Lancaster, ancestor of GERARD, of Ince, and GERARD, Earl of Macclesfield (extinct).
2 CONT *'''Sir Peter d. 1381. His great-great-grandson, above mentioned,
2 CONT *   SIR THOMAS GERARD, Knt. of Bryn, m. Dowse, dau. of Sir Thomas Assheton, Knt. of Assheton-under-Lyme, co. Lancaster, .... etc. __________________________
2 CONT *'''The Victoria history of the county of Lancaster; (1906)
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/cu31924088434554
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/cu31924088434554#page/n451/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.368
2 CONT **	(7) .....
2 CONT **	In 1354 half their moiety of the manor was granted by William Gerard and Joan his wife to '''Peter Gerard and Katherine his wife''' ; Final Conc. ii, 142. In 1416 it was found that Sir T. Gerard had held a moiety of the manor o
2 CONC f Rainhill of the heirs of Henry de Eccleston by knight's service and a rent of 18d. ; but in 1447, in the inquest after the death of Sir Peter Gerard, nothing is said of any manor here, though he had held of John Eccleston 'certa
2 CONC in messuages, with all the lands and tenements, rents, and services' belonging to them ; Lancs. Inq. p.m. (Chet. Soc), i, 123 ; Towneley MS. DD. n. 1465, The manor of Rainhill was included, with other lands there, in a settlement 
2 CONC of the Gerard estates made in 1511 ; Pal. of Lanc. Feet of F. bdle. 11, m. 246. 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/cu31924088434554#page/n455/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.372
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *   Alan de Windle III, later called Sir Alan,(6) was acting as juror at various inquests from 1242 onwards.(7) In 1252 William de Ferrers, earl of Derby, was pardoned for a false claim against him,(8) and next year Alan de Windle
2 CONC  and Thurstan de Holand joined in resisting an encroachment by the earl.(9)  Alan died between 1256 and 1274, and was succeeded by the above-named Peter de Burnhull and his wife Alice, the daughter and heir of Alan.(10) The new lo
2 CONC rd died before 1292,(11) leaving two sons, both under age ; Peter, the elder, died without issue before 1298, and Alan his brother succeeded.(12) He was living in 1318,(13) but did not enjoy the manor long, for his son Peter was i
2 CONC n possession in 1324,(14) but died soon afterwards, when his sisters Joan and Agnes inherited his manors. The former married William Gerard, of Kingsley, in Cheshire, and the latter David de Egerton.(15) Ultimately the whole inher
2 CONC itance was held by the Gerards, so that it may be presumed there was no issue by the other marriage. The manor has descended regularly to the present Lord Gerard of Brynn(16) in Ashton. 
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT **'''	(16) In 1354 a settlement of the manors of Windle and Rainhill was made by fine between''' William Gerard and Joan his wife and '''their son Peter and Catherine his wife''' ; at that time Joan's sister Agnes was still living
2 CONC , so that the Gerards had only half the Burnhull manors; Katherine, the widow of Peter de Burnhull, was also living, and was in the enjoyment of her dower; Final Conc. ii, 142. Katherine had married Hugh de Venables by the beginni
2 CONC ng of 1331 ; De Banc. R. 284, m. 119. 
2 CONT **	In 1383, Agnes and Katherine being dead, another settlement was made of the same manors by Thomas Gerard, '''son of Peter''', and Maud his wife ; Pal. of Lanc. Feet of F. bdle. 2, m. 29. 
2 CONT **	Sir Thomas Gerard, who died in 1416, held Windle by knight's service and the rent of 20d. a year ; Lancs. Inq. p.m. (Chet. Soc), i, 123. The Duchy Feodary of 1483 states that Sir Thomas Gerard then held Windle of Thomas Boteler
2 CONC . For a settlement in 1703 see Pal. of Lanc. Feet of F. bdle. 251, m. 61. 
2 CONT **	(17) Kuerden MSS. iv, W. 38. From Sir Thomas Gerard 20d. for Windle appears in the list of Boteler properties in Pal. of Lanc. Feet of F. bdle. 13, m. 142.  _________________________
2 CONT *	'Gerard01'
2 CONT *William Gerard of Kingsley (d before 1316)
2 CONT *Ormerod starts with William as son of Gerard of Hawarden and father of the William who m. Matilda de Glasshowse by Emma de Kingsley. The continuation, which follows BP1934, shows this William as son of William (m. Emma de Kingsle
2 CONC y) son of William son of Gerard. Ormerod is therefore missing out a William (son of Gerard & grandfather of this William) and this William. Wotton includes the first William (son of Gerard) but omits this one.
2 CONT *  m. Margaret
2 CONT **	1. William Gerard of Kingsley & Catenhall (d before 1352)
2 CONT **	  m. Matilda de Glasshowse (dau of Henry de Glasshowse of Kingsley)
2 CONT ***		A. William Gerard of Kingsley & Catenhall (b c1322)
2 CONT ***		  m. Joan de Bryn (dau of Peter de Bryn of Brynhill or Brindle)
2 CONT ****'''			i. Sir Peter Gerard of Kingsley & Bryn (d before 1380)
2 CONT *****				a. Sir Thomas Gerard of Kingsley & Bryn (d 27.03.1415-6)
2 CONT *****				BP1934 shows this Sir Thomas as father of the John who m. Alice le Boteler. Provisionally, we follow Ormerod & Wotton in showing John as son of Thomas's brother Peter.
2 CONT ******					(1) .... etc.
2 CONT *****				b. Peter Gerard of Kingsley (d 27.03.1415-6)
2 CONT *****				  m. Isabel Strangeways (dau of Thomas Strangeways)
2 CONT *****				NB. There is dispute as to whether Peter or his elder brother, Sir Thomas, was father of ...
2 CONT ******					(1) .... etc.
2 CONT *****				c. John Gerard
2 CONT *****				  m. Ellin Ince (dau/heir of Richard de Ince of Ince)
2 CONT *****				d. Helen Gerard probably of this generation
2 CONT *****				  m. Henry Eccleston of Eccleston (a 1399)
2 CONT ***		B. .... etc.
