2 NICK 4th Laird of Lewis
1 NAME Torquil MacLeod
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1295
2 ADDR
3 STAE Scotland
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1348
2 ADDR
3 STAE Scotland
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} IV. Torquil [Torcal Og] MacLeod, was born ca. 1320. He received from King David II a charter of four davochs of land and the castle of Assynt. He was married to Margaret Nicholson and had the following issue :
2 CONT 1.	Roderick [Ruaidhri Mor] MacLeod , follows V.
2 CONT 2.	Malcolm [Gille-caluim Beag]  , who at the battle of Tuitem Tarbhach was killed in 1406 .
2 CONT 3.	Neil MacLeod , who is the ancestor of the MacLeods of Gairloch . 
2 CONT 4.	Sidheag MacLeod ,who married Angus Mackay of Strathnaver, Chief of the Clan Mackay, who died in 1403. The  alleged ill-treatment  of Sidheag Macleod as a widow caused the MacLeod attack on the Mackays , which resulted in the ba
2 CONC ttle of Tuteam Tarbhach .(Source : Wardlow MS, page 87) . Issue from this marriage : (Source: “Geschiedenis van het geslacht Mackay”  = History van de Mackay family  by Daniel Baron Mackay, 1984, page 36 – 37 )
2 CONT a.	Angus Du (bh) Mackay , born ca. 1389, who became one of the most prominent Chiefs of the Clan Mackay in the middle ages. He died in 1433.
2 CONT b.	Roderick (Rorie) Gallda (Gald) Mackay , born ca. 1391, died in 1411.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===IV TORQUIL MACLEOD OF LEWIS===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/stream/historyofmacleod00mack#page/287/mode/1up History: pp. 287-8 for the family of IV Torquil MacLeod of Lewis]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Undated charter which belongs to the reighn of David II, King of Scots, and therefore before 22 February 1371:  Carta Torgill [Torkill] McCloid de terris de Assember [Essenbit] [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=njp.321010
2 CONC 38096846&view=1up&seq=600 RMA, 1306-1424: Index A, charter number 864 on p.570]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Undated charter which belongs to the reighn of David II, King of Scots, and therefore before 22 February 1371: To  Torkyll McCloyd, of the 4 pennyland of Asseynkt, with the fortalice in the isle therof. [https://babel.hathitrus
2 CONC t.org/cgi/pt?id=njp.32101038096846&view=1up&seq=600 RMS, 1306-1424: Index A, charter number (6) on p.570]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Secondary Source Evidence===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=njp.32101038096846&view=1up&seq=7 Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1306-1424. New Edition, to which are added indexes and remains of t
2 CONC he Lost Charter Rolls. Edited by John Maitland Thomson, LL.D. (H.M. General Register House, Edinburgh, 1912), 780 pp. including indexed and Errata and Coigenda]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT #  [http://archive.org/stream/historyofmacleod00mack#page/288/mode/2up History of the Macleods with genealogies of the principal families of the name. By Alexander Mackenzie (1889), page 288]
2 CONT # [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/mac/macleod06.php Stirnet: Macleod 06]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT "IV. <strong>Torquil Macleod, Fourth of Lewis</strong>. Douglas, giving as his authority the "Index to King David's Book of Charters in the Public Archives," says that this Torquil was granted a charter by King David II. — Torquil
2 CONC o Macleod de Lewis, terrarum bavonie da Assynt cum fortalicio, etc. Skene, however, 
2 CONT points out [Highlanders of Scotland, Vol. II., p. 274] that Torquil is not designated "de Lewis" in this charter, "nor has he any designation whatever " in it. Gregory informs us that from 1344 "the Siol Torquil held Lewis as vass
2 CONC als of the house of Isla," and that in the same reign [David the Second's] Torquil Macleod, Chief of the tribe, had a royal grant of the lands of Assint in Sutherland." This extensive barony Torquil obtained by marriage with Marga
2 CONC ret MacNicol, heiress of the lands in question. These were afterwards, early in the fifteenth century, given in vassalage by Roderick Macleod, V. of Lewis, to his own younger son, Tormod, progenitor of the later Macleods of Assynt
2 CONC , Geanies, and Cadboll. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Torquil Macleod died in the reign of Robert II. — [1371-1390] — when he was succeeded by his only son by Margaret MacNicol of Assynt."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/historyofmacleod00mack#page/286/mode/2up History of the Macleods with genealogies of the principal families of the name]; Alexander Mackenzie; 1889; page 287
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p50630.htm#i506299
2 CONT
2 CONT Torquil MacLeod, 4th of the Lewes1
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #506299
2 CONT Last Edited=23 Aug 2014
2 CONT      Torquil MacLeod, 4th of the Lewes is the son of Norman MacLeod, 3rd of the Lewes.2 He married Margaret MacNicol of Assynt.1
2 CONT      He had a charter of Assynt from King David I in right of his wife.1 Child of Torquil MacLeod, 4th of the Lewes and Margaret MacNicol of Assynt
2 CONT
2 CONT Roderick MacLeod, 5th of the Lewes+2 Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S37] BP2003 volume 2, page 2530. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37] [S37] BP2003. [S37]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "VI. <strong>Torquil Macleod, Sixth of Lewis</strong>. He is said to have made "a great figure" in the reign of James II. [1437-1460.] A charter by the same John of Yle, whose charter was witnessed by this man's father, Roderick M
2 CONC acleod, in 1449, was "witnessed by Torquil Macleoid of Leoghos," in 1461. He married, with issue — his heir and successor."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/historyofmacleod00mack#page/288/mode/2up History of the Macleods with genealogies of the principal families of the name]; Alexander Mackenzie; 1889; page 288
2 CONT
2 CONT == Note ===
2 CONT
2 CONT Fig. 9.2 on page 198 of the History of the Macleods reads: "The MacLeods of Lewis, Siol Torcaill, were named after Torquil Og, son of Murdo, son of Norman, son of Leod. The name Torquil would seem to be a Nicolson name brought int
2 CONC o the Macl.eods following Murdo's marriage to the daughter of a Lewis Nicolson. Earlier the Macl.eods appear to have been based in Skye, which remained (together with Harris) the territory of the Slol Tormoid. (Genealogy based on 
2 CONC Rev. W. Matheson 1979; dates of birth are conjectural). "
