1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Aodh Méith O'Neill (historically recorded as Áed Méith, Aodh Dubh Ó Meith, or Hugh "The Fat") was born circa 1170 in Ulster, Ireland. His traditional death date is recorded in the annals as 1230. His death location is recorded as 
2 CONC Tír Eoghain (Tyrone), Ulster, Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT His epithet "Méith" translates from Gaelic to "The Fat" or "The Stout," while "Dubh" refers to "The Black," denoting his dark hair in contrast to his brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Aodh Mac Muirchertaigh O'Neill, King of Tyrone.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Wives: Beanemidhe Ní Éignigh (a daughter of Ua hÉignigh, Lord of Fermanagh).
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT #Domhnall Óg O'Neill (d. 1241)
2 CONT
2 CONT #Brian Óg O'Neill
2 CONT
2 CONT #Muircheartach O'Neill
2 CONT
2 CONT #Beanmhidhe O'Neill
2 CONT
2 CONT Aodh Méith assumed the kingship of Tír Eoghain following a turbulent period of dynastic conflict. He spent his thirty-four-year reign aggressively defending his territories against military incursions from neighboring Irish rivals
2 CONC  and the newly arrived Anglo-Normans. Through strategic warfare and diplomacy, he established a stable relationship with the Earldom of Ulster. Aodh Méith successfully maintained his sovereignty to die peacefully in his own bed in
2 CONC  1230 as the supreme native ruler of the north, firmly anchoring the lineage from which the Clandeboye O'Neills directly descend.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 👑 The Royal O'Neill Lineage
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Niall Noigiallach, High-King of Ireland (r. ca. 445-453?)
2 CONT 2. Eogan
2 CONT 3. Muiredach
2 CONT 4. Muirchertach Mac Ercae, High-King of Ireland (r. 507-534/36)
2 CONT 5. Domnall, High-King of Ireland (r. 565-566)
2 CONT 6. Aed Uaridnach, High-King of Ireland (r. 604-612)
2 CONT 7. Mael Fithrich (d. 630)
2 CONT 8. Mael Duin (d. 681)
2 CONT 9. Fergal mac Maele Duin, High-King of Ireland (r. 710-722)
2 CONT 10. Niall Frossach, High-King of Ireland (d. 778)
2 CONT 11. Aed Oirdnide, High-King of Ireland (r. 797-819)
2 CONT 12. Niall Caille, High-King of Ireland (r. 833-846)
2 CONT 13. Aed Findliath, High-King of Ireland (r. 862-879)
2 CONT 14. Niall Glundub, High-King of Ireland (r. 916-919)
2 CONT 15. Muirchertach mac Neill, King of Ailech (r. 938-943)
2 CONT 16. Domnall ua Neill, High-King of Ireland (r. 956-980)
2 CONT 17. Muirchertach Ua Neill, King of Mide? (d. 977)
