1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Niall Ruadh O'Neill (also recorded as Red Niall, Niall O'Neill, or Neill Ruadh) was born circa 1165–1170. His traditional death date is recorded in genealogical tracks as 1226. His epithet "Ruadh" translates to "Th
2 CONC e Red" or "Red-Haired", a distinct physical descriptor recorded to distinguish him from his brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Aodh an Macaomh Tóinleasg O'Neill, King of Tyrone.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Wives: Nuala Ní Conchobhair (Nuala O'Conor), who was a princess of Connacht and a direct daughter of Ruaidrí Ua Conchobhair (Roderic O'Connor), the final undisputed High King of Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the father of 
2 CONT
2 CONT Brian Catha an Dúin O'Neill (Brian of the Battle of Down), who was his direct biological son, successor, and future High King of Ireland.His historical significance is defined by his preservation of the sovereign trunk line. He ru
2 CONC led briefly as King of Ulster before dying unexpectedly within a month of taking office at the royal inauguration site of Tulach Óg (Tullaghoge). His highly prestigious marriage to the daughter of the High King Roderic O'Connor ce
2 CONC mented the political status of his branch, ensuring that his son Brian had the elite dynastic backing required to later claim the absolute High Kingship of Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
