2 CONC tyn. In Bartrum's Pedigrees of the Welsh Tribal Patriarchs, #41, Bartum lists two lines for Madog ap Rhys, the first being Rhys ap Cynan ap Iago, which Bartrum points out is chronologically impossible, even after adding a second s
2 CONC et of men named Madog ap Rhys. (Wolcott shows Bartrum was dealing with the wrong Cynan.) The second gives Rhys ap Cunedda ap Iestyn ap Trethach, which Bartrum counts as legendary. (Steven Ferry, March 15, 2023.)
