1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Five Campbells whose possible relationships to each other, and to the main Campbell line descended from Gillespic, have not been ascertained with certainty but are speculated upon by secondary sources as indicated 
2 CONC below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         DUNCAN [II] Campbell [of the Isles] [of Argyll] (-after 28 Aug 1296, maybe after 1306).  The Ragman Roll names "…Duncan Cambel del Illes…" among those who swore allegiance to Edward I King of England at Berwick-upon-Twe
2 CONC ed 28 Aug 1296, in a group which includes some noble names but no other Campbells[158].  His separate entry in the Ragman Roll suggests that Duncan [II] was a different person from Duncan [III] who is shown below.  No other connec
2 CONC tion has been found between the Campbell family and “the Isles”.  Neither the Ane accompt nor Balfour Paul names Duncan [II].  [Robertson indexes a charter under which "Duncan Campbell" was granted "sundry lands in Argyle" by Robe
2 CONC rt I King of Scotland, so dated to after 1306[159], but it is not known whether this document relates to Duncan [II] or Duncan [III] (as indicated by Balfour Paul, see below[160]).] 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY%20UNTITLED.htm#_Toc389126070
