3 TITL Complete Peerage … Extant, Extinct, or Dormant, ed 2 vol 9 - Mortimer Pages.pdf
1 CHAN
2 DATE 26 APR 2022
3 TIME 14:58:22
0 @I6000000006727931407@ INDI
1 NAME Hugh /de Mortimer/ Lord of Chelmhurst
2 GIVN Hugh
2 SURN de Mortimer
2 NSFX Lord of Chelmhurst
2 _MARNM de Mortimer
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1232
2 PLAC Wigmore, Herefordshire, , England
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 23 JUN 1273
2 PLAC Chelmarsh, Bridgnorth, Shropshire, England
2 ADDR
1 OCCU Sheriff of Salop and Staffs
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hugh de Mortimer Lord of Chelmhurst was born ABT 1233 in Wigmore, Herefordshire, England, and died BEF Jun 1273. He was the son of Ralph de Mortimer Lord Mortimer of Wigmore and Gwladus Ddu ferch Llywelyn "y Llygad
2 CONC  Tywyllwch ". 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===family===
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 
2 CONT # Agatha de Ferrers BEF 24 Jul 1255, daughter of William de Ferrers 5th Earl of Derby and Sibilla Marshal. She was born 1234 in Derbyshire, England, and died 22 May 1306.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 
2 CONT # John de Mortimer dsp
2 CONT #  Henry de Mortimer d 1327 married Constance
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT Comments
2 CONT
2 CONT Was https://www.geni.com/people/Isolde-de-Mortimer-Lady-Audley/6000000003785930108 their daughter?  See
2 CONT
2 CONT http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=jweber&id=I06381 & http://http://archiver.rootsweb.ancestry.com/th/read/gen-medieval/2002-01/1011951167
2 CONT
2 CONT ===biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://archiver.rootsweb.ancestry.com/th/read/gen-medieval/2002-01/1011974244
2 CONT
2 CONT Gerald Paget's Baronage (388:1) gives the following information regarding Hugh de Mortimer, of Chelmarsh:
2 CONT
2 CONT HUGH DE MORTIMER, youngest son of Ralph de Mortimer of Wigmore, by Gladys his wife, daughter of Llewellyn Prince of Wales.(Pat. 39 Hen. 3. p.2.m 6). He adhered to Henry III against the Barons, and having lost three good horses at 
2 CONC the siege of Kenilworth Castle, had a grant of 40 marks to recompense him.(Rot.Fin.50 Hen. 3.m 1). Sheriff of Salop and Staffs 1272-3.(Rot. Pip.1 Edw.1).
2 CONT
2 CONT He married shortly after 24th July 1255, Agatha de Ferrers, 6th daughter of William Earl of Derby, and one of the seven coheirs of her mother Sybil, sister and coheir of Walter Marshall Earl of Pembroke.(Pat.39 Hen. 3 p 2.m 6; Mon
2 CONC . Ang. I:727a a 20). By her he had issue,
2 CONT
2 CONT I. HENRY, son and heir, born about 1266 (being 40 years of age at his mother's death).
2 CONT
2 CONT II. HUGH, living 14th April 1300, when he was commissioned by his mother to sue for her purparty of the Marshal lands in Ireland.(Cl.28 Edw.I.m 101).
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh de Mortimer (husband of Agatha) died shortly before 23rd June 1273, when his kinsman Ralph son of Roger de Mortimer of Wigmore was appointed Sheriff of Salop and Staffs in his place (Rot.Fin.1 Edw.1.m 25). His widow who inher
2 CONC ited a seventh of of fourth part of the large estates of the Marshals, including a sixth of Luton, Beds., a seventh of Sturminster-Marshal, Dorset, and lands in Wexford, Kildare and Kilkenny, died shortly before 12th June 1306.(Es
2 CONC ch.34 Edw.I. no 38).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
