1 NOTE Montferrat was in north-west Italy, and the Italian name for it is"Monferrato".
2 CONT It's about midway between Torino (Turin) and Milano (Milan) and south ofthe Po River.  The old capital is now the city of "Casale Monferrato"and, if geographical coordinates help any, that city is at 45 08 N and 827 E.  In italian
2 CONC  province of Alessandria.
2 CONT
2 CONT Montferrat was a lordship in northern Italy, technically a member of the
2 CONT Empire but subject to Provencal and Angevin influences.  The marquis wasa
2 CONT prominent figure on the Ghibelline side in thirteenth centuryMediterranean
2 CONT politics,
