1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darrell Wolcott, Center for the Studies of Ancient Wales: (in discussing Eva ferch Maredudd, wife of Einion Sais) "no single source gets her ancestry right, but I make her father Maredudd to be a brother of Ie
2 CONC uan Llwyd ap Madog ap Dafydd (of Dwnn ii 265). I further think one pair of "Madog ap Dafydd" is missing and that the "Cadwgan" cited as the father of "Dafydd" was NOT "ap Llowarch", but "ap Iorwerth ap Cadwgan ap Llowarch". Thus I
2 CONC  have inserted 6 generations between the Maredudd and Cadwgan which Dwnn ii, 127 cites as father of Efa." (Steven Ferry, July 12, 2020.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Peter Bartrum: Llywarch ap Bran 7; https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173392167863 (Steven Ferry, April 24, 2023.)
