1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darrell Wolcott, Center for the Study of Ancient Wales, in discussing issues with the line in Dwnn ii, 127: "This goes way past my charts (I ended at Einion Sais) but my guess is that Dwnn meant "Dafydd ap Gru
2 CONC ffudd Fychan ap Gruffudd" and that 3 generations are omitted in the pedigree.  I suspect there is a repeating trio of Llewelyn ap Caswallon ap Hywel immediately following the men of those names who were "ap Owain Gwynedd".  And bo
2 CONC th men named Llewelyn ap Caswallon had a son named Gruffudd who named a son Gruffudd Fychan." This gives a stable timeline and would place Angharad ferch Gwilim at c. 1475/80, with her husband Llewelyn ap Heilyn at c. 1465. (Steve
2 CONC n Ferry, July 13, 2020.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Peter Bartrum: https://cadair.aber.ac.uk/dspace/bitstream/handle/2160/5440/Gruffudd%20ap%20Cynan%2010.png?sequence=1&isAllowed=y (Steven Ferry, January 10, 2121.)
