1 OCCU 1st Earl of Ormond, 1st Earl of Ormonde, 1st Earl of Armond, 7th Cheif Butler of Ireland, 1st Earl Ormond, 1st earl of ormond
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT '''James Butler, 1st Earl of Ormonde1'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===From Medlands:===
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/IRELAND.htm#JamesButler1OrmondB
2 CONT
2 CONT JAMES Butler, son of Sir EDMUND Butler & his wife Joan FitzGerald of Kildare ([1305]-[Jan/Feb] 1338, bur Gowran, co. Kilkenny).  He was created Earl of Ormond in 1328.  
2 CONT
2 CONT m (1327) as her first husband, ELEANOR de Bohun, daughter of HUMPHREY de Bohen Earl of Hertford and Essex & his wife Elizabeth of England (-7 Oct 1363).  A manuscript which narrates the descents of the founders of Lanthony Abbey n
2 CONC ames (in order) “Margareta…Humfredus…Johannes…Humfredus decimus…Edwardus et Willielmus…Alianora, Margareta secunda, Eneas, Isabella” as the six sons and four daughters of “Humfredus octavus de Bohun, comes Herefordiæ et Essex, con
2 CONC stabularius Angliæ et dominus Breconiæ” and his wife “Elizabetham filiam regis Edwardi filii regis Henrici tertii”, adding that Eleanor married firstly (after the death of her father) “domino Jacobo le Botyler Hiberniæ”, who was c
2 CONC reated “comitem de Urmond” by King Edward III[1365].  She married secondly (licence 24 Jan 1344, before 20 Apr 1344) Sir Thomas de Dagworth, who was created Lord Dagworth.  
2 CONT
2 CONT James & his wife had four children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         JOHN Butler (Athur 6 Nov 1330-young).  
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         JAMES Butler ([Kilkenny 4 Oct 1331]-Knocktopher Castle 18 Oct or 6 Nov 1382, bur Gowran).  A manuscript which narrates the descents of the founders of Lanthony Abbey names “Jacobus le Botiler” as the son of “domino Jaco
2 CONC bo le Botyler Hiberniæ…comitem de Urmond” and his wife[1366].  He succeeded his father in 1338 as Earl of Ormond.  m as her first husband, ELIZABETH Darcy, daughter of Sir JOHN Darcy & his [second wife Joan Dowager Ctss of Kildare
2 CONC  née de Burgh of the Earls of Ulster] (-24 Mar 1390).  She married secondly ([28 Dec 1383/30 Mar 1384]) Sir Robert de Hereford.  Ancestors of the later Earls of Ormond.  
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.         ALIANORE (-1392).  m (after 20 Jul 1359) GERALD FitzGerald Earl of Desmond, son of MORICE FitzThomas Earl of Desmond & his third wife Aveline FitzMorice (-1398).  
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.         PERNEL (-1368).  m (before 8 Sep 1352) as his first wife, GILBERT Lord Talbot, son of RICHARD Talbot Lord Talbot & his wife Elizabeth Comyn of Badenoch ([1332]-Roales, Spain 24 Apr 1387).  
2 CONT
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #106940, b. circa 1305, d. 6 January 1337
2 CONT
2 CONT      James Butler, 1st Earl of Ormonde was born circa 1305.
2 CONT
2 CONT  He was the son of Sir Edmond Butler and Lady Joan FitzGerald.
2 CONT
2 CONT  He married Eleanor de Bohun, daughter of Humphrey de Bohun, 4th Earl of Hereford and Lady Elizabeth Plantagenet, in 1327. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 6 January 1337.
2 CONT
2 CONT      James Butler, 1st Earl of Ormonde gained the title of 1st Earl of Ormonde on 2 November 1328.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of James Butler, 1st Earl of Ormonde and Eleanor de Bohun
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Petronilla Butler+ d. 1387
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.James Butler, 2nd Earl of Ormonde+ d. 18 Oct 1382
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p10694.htm#i106940
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT James Butler, 1st Earl of Ormonde was born circa 1305 and died on 6 January 1337. He was the son of Sir Edmond Butler and Lady Joan FitzGerald. He married Eleanor de Bohun, daughter of Humphrey de Bohun, 4th Earl of Hereford and L
2 CONC ady Elizabeth Plantagenet, in 1327. They had one daughter and one son:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Petronilla Butler (d. 1387), married Gilbert Talbot, 3rd Baron Talbot, and had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * James Butler, 2nd Earl of Ormonde (b. b 1337-1382), married Elizabeth Darey, daughter of Sir John Darey, Lord Justice of Ireland, and had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography from http://www.harrymclaughlin.com/Descent_From_King_Edward_I_.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT James Butler, First Earl of Ormonde. Born ca 1305. Earl of Carrick. Chief Butler of Ireland. A minor when his father died, obtained, for 2,000 marks, licence to marry whomsoever he pleased. Died 1337. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Pedigree from http://www.thepeerage.com/p10694.htm#i106940
2 CONT
2 CONT James Butler, 1st Earl of Ormonde1
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #106940, b. circa 1305, d. 6 January 1337
2 CONT
2 CONT James Butler, 1st Earl of Ormonde|b. c 1305\nd. 6 Jan 1337|p10694.htm#i106940|Sir Edmond Butler|d. 13 Sep 1321|p15141.htm#i151404|Lady Joan FitzGerald||p15141.htm#i151405|Theobald Butler|b. c 1242\nd. 26 Sep 1285|p15141.htm#i15141
2 CONC 0|Joan FitzJohn|d. fr 25 Feb 1303 - 26 May 1303|p15142.htm#i151411|John F. FitzGerald, 1st Earl of Kildare|d. 12 Sep 1316|p15141.htm#i151406|Blanche de la Roche||p15141.htm#i151408|
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=13 Apr 2008
2 CONT
2 CONT      James Butler, 1st Earl of Ormonde was born circa 1305.1 He was the son of Sir Edmond Butler and Lady Joan FitzGerald.2 He married Eleanor de Bohun, daughter of Humphrey de Bohun, 4th Earl of Hereford and Lady Elizabeth Planta
2 CONC genet, in 1327. He died on 6 January 1337.
2 CONT
2 CONT      James Butler, 1st Earl of Ormonde gained the title of 1st Earl of Ormonde on 2 November 1328.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of James Butler, 1st Earl of Ormonde and Eleanor de Bohun
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Petronilla Butler+ d. 1387
2 CONT
2 CONT     * James Butler, 2nd Earl of Ormonde+ d. 18 Oct 1382
