1 NAME Matilda (Maud) /de Clare/
2 GIVN Matilda (Maud)
2 SURN de Clare
2 _MARNM de Clare
2 NICK Matilda de Clare wife of Married (1) Robert de Clifford and (2) Robert de Welle.
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1276
2 ADDR
3 STAE England
1 DEAT
2 DATE BET 4 MAR 1327 AND 24 MAY 1327
2 PLAC Castle Clifford
2 ADDR
3 CITY Hay
3 STAE England
1 OCCU Baroness Clifford
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://thepeerage.com/p15824.htm#i158232
2 CONT
2 CONT Maud de Clare[1]
2 CONT *F, #158232, 
2 CONT *b. circa 1276, 
2 CONT *d. from 4 March 1326/27 to 24 May 1327
2 CONT *Maud de Clare was born circa 1276 at Gloucestershire, England.[2] She was the daughter of Sir Thomas de Clare, Lord of Thomond and Juliana FitzMaurice.
2 CONT *She married, firstly, Robert de Clifford, 1st Lord Clifford, son of Roger de Clifford and Isabel de Vipont, on 3 November 1295 at Clifford Castle, Herefordshire, England.
2 CONT *She married, secondly, Robert de Welle after 1314.
2 CONT *She died from 4 March 1326/27 to 24 May 1327 [3]
2 CONT *From 3 November 1295, her married name became de Clifford.[1] 
2 CONT *From after 1314, her married name became de Welle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Maud de Clare and Robert de Clifford, 1st Lord Clifford
2 CONT *1.Idoine de Clifford+2 b. c 1300, d. 24 Aug 1365
2 CONT *2.Roger de Clifford, 2nd Lord Clifford3 b. 21 Jan 1299/0, d. c Apr 1322
2 CONT *3.Robert de Clifford, 3rd Lord Clifford+3 b. 5 Nov 1305, d. 20 May 1344
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinc
2 CONC t or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume III, page 247. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.[S125] Richard Glanville-Brown, online <e-mail address>, Richard Glanville-Brown (RR 2, Milton, Ontario, Canada), downloaded 17 August 2005.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume III, page 291.
2 CONT
2 CONT ******************************************************************
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: Maud De Clare 1 2 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sex: F 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: ABT 1285 in Bunratty Castle, Thomond, Clare, Ireland 2 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 1 FEB 1326/27 2 
2 CONT
2 CONT Reference Number: 7604 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Maud (married 2nd by 16 Dec 1315 2nd Lord (Baron) Welles of the 1299 creation and died between 4 March 1326/7 and 24 March 1327), daughter of Thomas de Clare, Lord of Thomond in Connaught, 2nd son of 5th Earl of Hertford and 2nd E
2 CONC arl of Gloucester. [Burke's Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 11 Nov 1315 Abducted & Forcibly Remarried by Robert de Welles.[JohnFaye (8 Jun 05).FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT Maud (married 2nd by 16 Dec 1315 2nd Lord (Baron) Welles of the 1299 creation and died between 4 March 1326/7 and 24 March 1327), daughter of Thomas de Clare, Lord of Thomond in Connaught, 2nd son of 5th Earl of Hertford and 2nd E
2 CONC arl of Gloucester. [Burke's Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 11 Nov 1315 Abducted & Forcibly Remarried by Robert de Welles.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Thomas De Clare b: ABT 1248 in Tunbridge, Kent, England 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Juliane Fitzmaurice Fitzgerald b: ABT 1265 in Dublin, Ireland
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 Robert De Welles b: ABT 1300
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 2 Robert De Clifford b: 1 APR 1274 in Clifford Castle, Clifford, Herefordshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT  Ideona De Clifford b: ABT 1300 in Appleby Castle, Westmorland, England
2 CONT
2 CONT  Robert De Clifford b: 5 NOV 1305 in Clifford Castle, Herefordshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT  John De Clifford b: ABT 1307
2 CONT
2 CONT  Margaret De Clifford b: ABT 1307
2 CONT
2 CONT  Andrew De Clifford b: ABT 1309
2 CONT
2 CONT  John De Clifford b: ABT 1307
2 CONT
2 CONT http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=jcrow&id=I03279
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Married Robert de Clifford at Clifford's Castle, and they had three children: Roger, 2nd Lord Clifford, Robert, 3rd Lord Clifford and Idonia, who married Sir Henry de Percy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After her first husband, Sir Robert de Clifford was slain at the  Battle of Bannockburn in Stirling, Scotland, she was abducted by John le Irish, keeper of Barnard Castle Nov 1315. William de Montagu gathered a force of fourty men
2 CONC  to rescue her. She later married Robert de Welle about Dec 1315.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
