1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Elizabeth Darcy''' was the daughter of Sir John Darcy, 1st Lord Darcy de Knayth and Lady Joan de Burgh.2 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, firstly, James Butler, 2nd Earl of Ormonde, son of James Butler, 1st Earl of Ormonde and Eleanor de Bohun.2   [10. JAMES BUTLER (or LE BOTILLER), Knt., 2nd Earl of Ormond, Chief Governor of Ireland, born at Kilkenny, 
2 CONC Ireland 4 Oct. 1331 (aged 7 in 1338). He married by papal dispensation dated 15 May 1346 (they being related in the 4th degree of kindred) ELIZABETH DARCY, daughter of John Darcy, Knt., of Knaith, Lincolnshire, by his 2nd wife, Jo
2 CONC an, 4th daughter of Richard de Burgh, Knt., 2nd Earl of Ulster, lord of Connaught.]
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, secondly, Sir Robert de Hereford.2  
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Elizabeth Darcy and James Butler, 2nd Earl of Ormonde,  four sons, 
2 CONT * Ralph, 
2 CONT * James [3rd Earl of Ormond], 
2 CONT *Thomas, and 
2 CONT * Maurice, and two daughters, 
2 CONT * Eleanor (wife of Gerald Fitz Maurice, 3rd Earl of Desmond) and 
2 CONT * Joan (wife of Tiege O'Carrol). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT #  [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extin
2 CONC ct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume IV, page 244. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 1027. Hereinafter cited as Burke'
2 CONC s Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Butler, Countess of Ormond
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT   (Redirected from Elizabeth Darcy, Countess of Ormond)
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Butler (nee Darcy), Countess of Ormond (3 April 1332- 24 March 1390), was the wife of James Butler, 2nd Earl of Ormond, and the mother of his six children, including James Butler, 3rd Earl of Ormond.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family and lineage
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Darcy was born on 3 April 1332 at Platten, County Meath, Ireland, the daughter of Sir John Darcy, 1st Baron Darcy of Knaith, Justiciar of Ireland, and his second wife Joan de Burgh. Sir John was a veteran of the Battle o
2 CONC f Crecy. He held the offices of Constable of Nottingham Castle, Constable of the Tower of London, and Sheriff of Lancashire. From 1341- 1346, he was Chamberlain to King Edward III. Elizabeth had a brother Sir William Darcy, who ma
2 CONC rried Catherine FitzGerald, by whom he had issue. She also had numerous half-siblings from her parents' previous marriages. Her father's first wife was Emeline Heron, by whom he had eight children, including his heir, John Darcy, 
2 CONC 2nd Baron Darcy of Knaith. Elizabeth's mother's first husband had been Thomas FitzGerald, 2nd Earl of Kildare, by whom she had three sons, John FitzGerald, Richard FitzGerald, 3rd Earl of Kildare, and Maurice FitzGerald, 4th Earl 
2 CONC of Kildare.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth's paternal grandparents were Roger Darcy and Isabel d'Aton. Her maternal grandparents were Richard de Burgh, 2nd Earl of Ulster and Margaret de Burgh, daughter of Sir John de Burgh and Hawise of Lanvaley.
2 CONT
2 CONT One of her maternal aunts was Elizabeth de Burgh, wife of Robert the Bruce.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Marriages and children
2 CONT
2 CONT On 15 May 1346 in Ormond, Ireland, when Elizabeth was fourteen, she married her first husband James Butler, 2nd Earl of Ormond (4 October 1331- 18 October 1382), the son of James Butler, 1st Earl of Ormond and Lady Eleanor de Bohu
2 CONC n. He was Lord Justice of Ireland in 1359, 1364, and 1376. He was also Constable of Dublin Castle in 1349. He was known as the Noble Earl, however, the Irish called him The Chaste.
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon her marriage to the Earl, Elizabeth acceeded to the title of Countess of Ormond.
2 CONT
2 CONT James and Elizabeth had six children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Ralph Butler
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor Butler (died 1392), married Gerald FitzMaurice FitzGerald, 3rd Earl of Desmond, by whom she had issue, including the 4th and 6th Earls of Desmond.
2 CONT
2 CONT James Butler, 3rd Earl of Ormond (died 6 September 1405), before 17 June 1386, married firstly, Anne Welles, Countess of Ormond, daughter of John Welles, 4th Lord Welles and Maud de Ros, by whom he had issue, including James Butle
2 CONC r, 4th Earl of Ormond. He married secondly, Katherine FitzGerald of Desmond, by whom he had further issue. In 1391, he purchased Kilkenny Castle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Butler
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine Butler (born 1361), married firstly, Thomas Reade, by whom she had one son, Richard, and secondly, Thomas Fleming of Slane.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan Butler, married Tiege O' Carroll[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT James Butler, 2nd Earl of Ormond, died on 18 October 1382 in Knocktopher and was buried in Gowran Church, Co. Kilkenny. Elizabeth married secondly, Sir Robert de Hereford, Seneschal of the Liberty of Tipperary, between 28 December
2 CONC  1383 and 30 March 1384.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Death
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Darcy died on 24 March 1390. She was not quite fifty-eight years old.
2 CONT
