1 NAME Egidia /Stewart/
2 GIVN Egidia
2 SURN Stewart
2 _MARNM Stewart
2 NICK Jean
2 NICK Jill
2 NICK Gill Eglinton
2 NICK Princess Egidia
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1320
2 PLAC Cunninghame, Ayrshire, Scotland
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1406
2 ADDR
3 STAE Scotland
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Walter Stewart, 6th High Steward of Scotland later married Isabel de Graham, daughter of Sir John Graham of Abercorn and Mary of Strathearn. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # John Stewart of Ralston
2 CONT # Andrew Stewart
2 CONT # '''Egidia Stewart'''. She married 1) Sir James Lindsay of Crawford 2) Sir Hugh Eglinton of that ilk 3) Sir James Douglas of Dalkeith
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://www.thepeerage.com/p10793.htm#i107926 thepeerage.com]
2 CONT
2 CONT Egidia Stewart1 
2 CONT * F, #107926, d. before 1406
2 CONT * Last Edited=12 May 2008
2 CONT
2 CONT Egidia Stewart was the daughter of Walter Stewart, 6th High Steward of Scotland and Isabella Graham.1 She married Sir Hugh Eglinton of that Ilk.1 She married Sir James de Lindsay of Crawford, son of Sir David de Lindsay of Crawfor
2 CONC d and Maria Abernethy, on 21 April 1346.2 She married Sir James Douglas circa October 1378. She died before 1406.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Egidia Stewart was also known as Gille Stewart. From 21 April 1346, her married name became de Lindsay. Her married name became Douglas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Egidia Stewart and Sir Hugh Eglinton of that Ilk
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Eglinton+ 3 
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Egidia Stewart and Sir James Douglas
2 CONT
2 CONT Janet Douglas+ 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Egidia Stewart and Sir James de Lindsay of Crawford
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir James de Lindsay of Crawford+ d. 13972 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth de Lindsay 2 
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabel de Lindsay+ 
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT # [S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 214. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.  
2 CONT # [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 951. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Pee
2 CONC rage and Baronetage, 107th edition.  
2 CONT # [S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 1, page 1279. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft#page/14/mode/2up Balfour Paul, Sir James, Scots Peerage,] vol i pp 14-15
2 CONT
