1 NAME John /Stewart of Railston/
2 GIVN John
2 SURN Stewart of Railston
2 _MARNM Stewart of Railston
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE BET 1320 AND 26 JUN 1325
1 DEAT
2 DATE BET 27 JUN 1415 AND 26 JUN 1416
1 OCCU
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == SIR JOHN STEWART OF RAILSTOUN ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir John Stewart of Railston is the son of Walter Stewart, the sixth hereditary steward of Scotland, and his second wife Isabel Graham. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft#page/14/mode/1up The Scots Peerage I
2 CONC : 14]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Lands of Railston ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''It should be noticed that the land called Railston is located in the Cunningham division of Ayrshire, formerly the barony of Cunningham, [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD150%2f89&s
2 CONC t=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=RAILSTOUN&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD150/89] and that the land called Ralston, now part of Paisley, is located in Renfrewshire, formerly the barony of Renfrew. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nr
2 CONC sonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD26%2f3%2f1115&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=ralston&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1501&dt=1700&di=n NRS: GD26/3/1115] Sir John Stewart of Railston had no connection with Ralston in Renfrewshire. According 
2 CONC to Gilbert Burnett, Lyon King of Arms, writing in volume four of the Exchequer Rolls of Scotland: "His lands of Ralston (sic) are described as in the barony of Cunninghame, and are therefor not to be identified with Ralston near P
2 CONC aisley, which gives its name to the family of Ralston of that Ilk." [https://archive.org/details/rotuliscaccariir04grea/page/n191/mode/1up Exchequer Rolls IV: p. clxxxviii]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not been identified for Sir John Stewart of Railstoun. He appears still to have been alive on 27 June 1415, but he died before 26 June 1416. [https://archive.org/details/rotuliscaccariir04grea/page
2 CONC /253/mode/1up Exchequer Rolls IV., 1406-1436: p. 253-4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir John Stewart of Railstoun is reported to have married married Alicia Mure, daughter of Sir Reginald Mure of Abercorn. [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ss4tz/stewart01.php Stirnet: Stewart 01]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Children ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Walter-Stewart-of-Ralston/6000000002187899948?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1589186782618&through=6000000003828038289
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/John-Stewart/6000000134543130821?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1589186872025&through=6000000003828038289
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Marjory-Stewart-of-Ralston/6000000002187899940?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1589186888967&through=6000000003828038289
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Egidia-Stewart-of-Ralston/6000000003054340570
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Stewart-of-Ralston/6000000002116129610?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1589187135297&through=6000000002187899940
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 June 1415: Compotum nobilis domini et potentis, Johannis Senescalli comiti Buchanie, camerarii Scocie, redditum apud Perth die et anno supradictis, a vicesimo septimo die Junii anno et. quartodecimo usque in diem hujus compo
2 CONC ti. . . . . . Et per solucionem factam domino Johanni Senescalli de Railstoun, percipienti per annum pro tempore vite sue viginti libras per manus camerarii ut patet per literas dicti domini Johannis de recepto ostensas super comp
2 CONC otum, de anno compoti, xx li. [https://archive.org/details/rotuliscaccariir04grea/page/235/mode/1up Exchequer Rolls IV., 1406-1436: pp. 235-7]'''
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 June 1416: Compotum Johannis Gil de Haltoun et Johannis de Camera, custumariorum de Perth [Perth, 26 June 1616, from 22 June 1415 to date. . . . . .  Et comiti Buchanie, camerario , per recepcionem quondam domini Johannis Se
2 CONC nescalli de Raistoun, militis, ut patet per literas domini gubernatoris de precepto, sub periculo Johannis de Camera, alterius computancium, vj li. xiij s, iiij d., de quibus camerarius respomdebit. [https://archive.org/details/ro
2 CONC tuliscaccariir04grea/page/253/mode/1up Exchequer Rolls IV., 1406-1436: pp. 253-4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/rotuliscaccariir04grea/page/n8/mode/1up Rotuli Scaccarii Regum Scotorum. The Exchequer Rolls of Scotland. Edited by George Burnett, Lyon King of Arms. Volume IV. A.D. 1406-1436. (H.M. General Register 
2 CONC House, Edinburgh, 1880), 783 pp. including index and corrigenda]
2 CONT
