1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == SIR ANDREW STEWART OF RAILSTOUN==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''domino Andree Senescalli, militi (1400) domino Andree Senescalli de Ralistoun (1407) domino Andree Senescalli de Ralistoun (1409) quondam domino Andree Senescalli de Railstoun (1413)'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Andrew Stewart, here treated, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Walter-Stewart-6th-High-Steward-of-Scotland/6000000003099027666?through=6000000002187899933 and https://www.geni.com/people/Isabel-de-Graham-of-Abercor
2 CONC n/6000000002166220506?through=6000000002187899933 his wife. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/page/15/mode/1up The Scots Peerage I: 15] https://www.geni.com/people/John-Stewart-of-Railston/6000000003828038289
2 CONC ?through=6000000002187899933 is his brother. [https://archive.org/details/rotuliscaccariir04grea/page/164/mode/1up Exchequer Rolls of Scotland IV: 164]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to the late George Burnett: "From 1400 to 1413 an annuity was paid by the chamberlain, sometimes through the custumars of Dundee and Perth, to Sir Andrew Stewart, knight. The designation "of Raliston" is frequently ad
2 CONC ded; and on two occasions he is called brother of Sir John Stewart of Ralstoun. The last payment allowed to him is in the custom account of Dundee of June 1413, when he is said to be deceased". [https://archive.org/details/rotulis
2 CONC caccariir04grea/page/n196/mode/1up Exchequer Rolls IV:  cxciii]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Andrew Stewart of Railstoun was alive on 22 July 1412, [https://archive.org/details/rotuliscaccariir04grea/page/164/mode/1up Exchequer Rolls of Scotland IV: 165] but he died before 26 June 1413. [https://archive.org/details
2 CONC /rotuliscaccariir04grea/page/168/mode/1up Ibidem: 168]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
