2 CONT from  http://digital.nls.uk/histories-of-scottish-families/pageturner.cfm?id=96653992&mode=transcription
2 CONT
2 CONT (2nd) Sir Thomas of Menzies, who held the lands and barony of Garrioch, in Aberdeenshire, during his father's lifetime, and also the lands of "Umyne." He was one of the Scottish Barons who framed the letter to the Pope in 1320, to
2 CONC  which he appended his seal.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT from [https://books.google.com/books?id=rvssAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PT206&ots=bQYLy4OqiQ&dq=alexander%20Menzies%2C%20of%20Fothergill&pg=PT206#v=onepage&q&f=false page "The Clan of Menzies"] The Tartans of the Clans and Septs of Scotland with
2 CONC  the Arms of the Chiefs, Volume 2 W. & A.K. Johnston, 1906 - Clans
2 CONT
2 CONT In the time of Robert I. (1306-30), Alexander Menzies resigned the lands of Dorisdeir, in Nithsdale, which the victor of Bannockburn granted to James, brother of Walter, the Lord High Steward. The same King granted charters to '''
2 CONC Thomas Menzies, Knight''', of the lands of Unwyn (Oyne 1) in the Garioch, and other lands of Fothergill, in Athole. Also two charters to Alexander Menzies of the Barony of Glendochyre, and the darach land of Finlargis (Finlarig ?)
2 CONC .
2 CONT
