1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Annals of Ulster:
2 CONT 1487 John Mac Costello, son of Edmond, son of Meyler, dies, David his son now MacCostello of the Plain
2 CONT 1416 John Mac Costello killed by arrow while plundering his own cousins land Edmond of the plain.
2 CONT 1365 MacCostelloes at war with the Luighni, 6 sons of the O Haras including their 3  Tanists killed 
2 CONT 1361 Gilbert, son of Meiler dies Kia
2 CONT 1346 Waltrin Mac Costelloe killed
2 CONT 1343 Sons of Walter kill MacDermot the Foreigner in his own Castle.
2 CONT 1340 Inuig, youngest daughter of Phillip, wife of MacFinneen , dies
2 CONT 1340 This Jordan, the clan had many over their 800 years, was known as Ruadh, or Red, and  was slain by the   MacCostelloe,s  eternal enemies, Mac Dermot the Foreigner.
2 CONT 1340 William Mac , son of Gilbert, slain by the Tellach Eochacht 
2 CONT 1336 Maig son of Walter slain by MacDermot the Foreigner 
2 CONT 1330 Gilbert slain in his own Castle by MacDermot the Foreigner 
2 CONT 1327 Gilbert with MacWilliam De Burgho 
2 CONT 1325 Gilbert with Walter de Burgho 
2 CONT 1315 Gilbert assists Diarmata MacDermot in the taking of MacDermot the Foreigner wife for hostage
2 CONT 1291 Thomas son of Gilbert  Kia, , David son of Phillip taken hostage and then slain
2 CONT 1282 Phillip MacCostelloe Defeats magnus OConor at Battle of Slieve Gamh
2 CONT 1263 Aed ONeil marries daughter of Miles, son born Brian is King of Tirowen, he dies1291 in Battle of Clannaboy, his son Aed his successor,
2 CONT 1259 Miles MacCostelloe Dies
2 CONT 1213 Gilbert MacCostelloe killed in the Castle of Cael Uisce, or Narrow Watersn BallyShannon.
2 CONT 1211 Gilbert MacCostelloe builds Castle of Cael Uisce under King Johns Justiciar orders.
2 CONT 1195 Gilbert MacGoisdealbh under service to OConor King of Connacht 
2 CONT 1194 Gilbert raids Assaroe.
2 CONT
2 CONT Annals of Ulster are usually off by a year or two to the other Annals, but recent studies have shown it is an older book of Annals,  later scribes confused the dates from the two different date traditions followed, one being the C
2 CONC atholic Church dates, and the other the lists of Irish Kings. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Compare and contrast the info I am posting, and an image slowly appears of a tumultuous life of interactions and constant warfare and feuds , even within families as they grew in size.
2 CONT
2 CONT Keep in mind any relative at all could challenge for the Chieftainship , Called Tanistry, of their clans at any time, the only caveat was you could not be physically not 100% in challenging. 
2 CONT
2 CONT This was why so many hostages offered to competing clans to settle disputes were blinded, or emasculated while in custody, it limited the competitions best people, usually sons of the leading men in the competing tribe.
2 CONT These men Beach me seanachies, storytellers for  their clans, or musicians , such as the Famous blind Harpist OCarrolan, or even monks or priests.
2 CONT
2 CONT Books like Orpens  History of the Normans in Ireland are exquisite examples of a top historian researching as much of the sources he could in the early 1900’s , and then compiling it all in a running story., remarkable in its scop
2 CONC e and breadth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Even the original work By Gerald of Wales is a fascinating story, written while most of the 1169 to 1195 period was ongoing. Gerald was a de Barri, and as such was a Geraldine, and a Monk who was a historian of the times, 
2 CONT
2 CONT I would highly recommend his two books on Ireland and the Invasion, and A geographic tour of Ireland written at the same time. he of course favors his family members and the Welsh in general, but it is very descriptive and accurat
2 CONC e of the Battles during the Conquest .
2 CONT
2 CONT I hope to do the same one day for my clans name founders, and to also find out If I I am directly related to these early Cambro Normans, or to one of their tenants. I do know from DNA tests that I do not match any modern Irish dna
2 CONC  samples available on the various websites, whatever that may mean.
