1 NOTE {geni:about_me} After Domhnall Ó Néill (d. 1325) died, his sons split into factions:
2 CONT
2 CONT The elder branch under Aodh Reamhar took the kingship of Tír Eoghain (the Tyrone heartland).
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry, the younger, wasn’t happy. He felt he’d been cheated of power or land.
2 CONT
2 CONT So Henry challenged his brother’s line for control — first militarily, then politically. The annalists describe him as aimhreidh — literally “disorderly, quarrelsome, prone to strife.”
2 CONT
2 CONT TPD 5/11/25
