1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Henry 'Aimhreidh' O'Neill1
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #546218, d. 16 June 1392 Last Edited=31 Aug 2015
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry 'Aimhreidh' O'Neill was the son of Niall 'Mor' O'Neill, King of Ulster and Beanmidhe MacMahon.2 He married Affric O'Neill, daughter of Aedh O'Neill.1 He died on 16 June 1392. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT He was heir of Cenel Eoghain.1 Henry 'Aimhreidh' O'Neill also went by the nick-name of Henry 'Aimhreidh' (or in English, 'the Turbulent').1 Child of Henry 'Aimhreidh' O'Neill and Affric O'Neill
2 CONT
2 CONT Domnall O'Neill, King of Ulster2 d. 1432
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S37] BP2003 volume 2, page 3005. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT
2 CONT [S37] BP2003. [S37]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Henry Aimhreidh served as the Royadamhna (Royal Heir) of Kinel-Owen. He was "noted for his justice, nobility and generosity." He died on the Festival Day of St. Brendan in 1392. The cause of death is unknown. He married Affric, da
2 CONC ughter of Hugh Reamhar O'Neill. She preceded him in death by three years. [1] His granddaughter, Una, by his son, Domhnall Bocc, married his younger brother (and my 17th great-grandfather), Niall Og O'Neill.
2 CONT
2 CONT Annals of the Four Masters
