1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Theobald de Verdon, 1st Lord Verdun of Alton in Staffordshire
2 CONT *1248 - 1309  (~ 61 years)
2 CONT *Name	Theobald de Verdon, 1st Lord Verdun  [1, 2, 3, 4] 
2 CONT * Born	 1248 	of, Alton, Staffordshire, England   [5, 6, 7] 
2 CONT * Gender	Male 
2 CONT * Name AKA	Thebaud de Verdun  [7] 
2 CONT * Name AKA	Theobald de Verdun  [8, 9] 
2 CONT *Died	24 Aug 1309 	Alton, Staffordshire, England  [5, 6, 8, 10] 
2 CONT * Buried	Croxden Abbey, , Staffordshire, England Find all individuals with events at this location  [10] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes 	
2 CONT
2 CONT BIRTH: Calculate year> Aged 23 in 1271.
2 CONT
2 CONT OFFICE: Constable of Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Person ID	I9668 	Europe: Royal and Noble Houses of Europe Last Modified	14 Dec 2014 
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Sir John de Verdon, Lord of Weobley,   b. Abt 1223, of, Alton, Staffordshire, England ,   d. Bef 17 Oct 1274, , Ireland 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother	Margery de Lacy,   b. Abt 1226, of, Ewyas Lacy, Herefordshire, England  d. 1256  (Age ~ 30 years) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married	Bef 20 Apr 1242  [11] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family	Margery de Bohun,   d. Bef 1304 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married	Bef 6 Nov 1276  [7] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 	
2 CONT *  	1. Sir John de Verdon, 2nd Lord Verdun,   d. 8 Jun 1297,  Ireland.  Unmarried. 
2 CONT *  	2. Sir Theobald de Verdon, 2nd Lord Verdun,   b. 8 Sep 1278, of, Atton Castle, Stafford, England  d. 27 Aug 1316, Alton, Staffordshire, England.  Married 1) Maud de Mortimer; 3 daughters 2) Elizabeth de Clare.  
2 CONT *  	3. Miles de Verdun,   d. 14 February 1347.  Married a daughter of Richard of Exeter.  
2 CONT *  	4. Bertram de Verdun,   d. Yes, date unknown
2 CONT *  	5. Nicholas de Verdon,   d. 1347.  Married Matilda Bermingham.
2 CONT *  	6. Walter de Verdun,   d. Yes, date unknown
2 CONT *  	7. William de Verdun,   d. Yes, date unknown
2 CONT *  	8. Rose de Verdun,   d. Yes, date unknown.  Married William Hussey.
2 CONT * 9.  Bartholomew de Verdun.
2 CONT Last Modified	25 May 2014 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Descendants
2 CONT
2 CONT Smith, Brendan.  ''Crisis and Survival in Late Medieval Ireland: the English of Louth and their Neighbours 1330-1450'' Oxford University Press 2013.  Page 19.  < [https://books.google.com/books?id=7tGTnnBMk8QC&lpg=PR4&pg=PA19#v=on
2 CONC epage&q=Cruys%20&f=true GoogleBooks] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000192532903833&size=large}}
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John de Verdun [k], Lord of Westmeath, b abt 1226, Alton, Staffordshire, England, d 21 Oct 1274, Alton, Staffordshire, England. He md:
2 CONT [1] Margaret de Lacy bef 14 May 1244, Herefordshire, England, daughter of Gilbert de Lacy and Isabel Bigod. He md [2] Eleanor. Child of John de Verdun and Margaret de Lacy was:
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Theobald de Verdun [l], Lord Verdun, Constable of Ireland''', b abt 1248, d 24 Aug 1309, Alton, Staffordshire, England. He md '''Margery de Bohun''' [m] abt 1272, daughter of Sir Humphrey VI de Bohun and Eleanor de Braose. 
2 CONC Child of Theobald de Verdun and Margery de Bohun was:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sir Theobald de Verdun [n], Lord Verdun, Justiciar of Ireland, Knight, b 8 Sep 1278, d 27 Jul 1316, Alton, Staffordshire, England. He md [1] Maud de Mortimer 29 Jul 1302, Wigmore, Herefordshire, England, daughter of Sir Edmund d
2 CONC e Mortimer and Margaret de Fiennes, and [2] Elizabeth de Clare 4 Feb 1314/15. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Theobald de Verdun and Maud de Mortimer were: 
2 CONT # Joan de Verdun b Aug 1303, Wootton in Stanton Lacy, Shropshire, England, d 2 Oct 1334, Alton, Staffordshire, England; md [1] John de Montagu 28 Apr 1317, and [2] Thomas de Furnival 24 Feb 1317/18. 
2 CONT # Elizabeth de Verdun b abt 1306, prob Alton, Staffordshire, England, d 1 May 1360. She md Sir Bartholomew de Burghersh, Lord Burghersh, bef 11 Jun 1320, son of Sir Robert de Burghersh, Lord Burghersh, and Maud de Badlesmere. 
2 CONT # Margery de Verdun b 10 Aug 1310, Alton, Staffordshire, England, d abt 1376/77. She md [1] William le Blount bef 30 Feb 1326/27, [2] Sir Marcus Hussey bef 18 Oct 1339, and [3] Sir John Crophull bef 10 Sep 1355, son of Ralph de Cr
2 CONC ophull and Maud. [2] Eleanor de Bohun abt 1257, daughter of Sir Humphrey V de Bohun, Earl of Hereford and Essex, and Maud de Avenbury. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of John de Verdun and Eleanor de Bohun was: 
2 CONT # Maud de Verdun b abt 1270, of Alton, Staffordshire, England. She md Sir John de Grey, Lord Grey, abt 1285, son of Sir Reynold de Grey, Lord Grey, and Maud de Longchamp.
2 CONT
2 CONT • or see: http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Verdon,_Theobald_de_(DNB00)
