2 CONC , vol. 2, p. 388  Inquisition Post Mortem (abridged) 70. Isabel de Clyfford, one of the daughters and heirs of Robert de Veteri Ponte Writ, 14 May, 20 Edw. I. [1292] Westmoreland. Inq. Friday after St. Barnabas the Apostle, 20 Edw
2 CONC . I Appely. The castle with a moiety of the profits of the county (court?), whose issues are not sufficient for the maintenance of the castle, the sheriff and his clerks, constables and other ministers, held of the king in chief; 
2 CONC and a certain land worth 117s. yearly. Burgham alias Bruham. The manor, including its part of the forest of Quennefel, a park within the said forest, a certain meadow in Cumberland, and a little pasture called Thornholme. Burgh un
2 CONC der Staynmore. The manor, including 30s. from William's Rydding &c. Wynton. The manor, including a water-mill worth 10l. 13s. 4d., but the said Isabel enfeoffed her esquire Adam del Hake of 100s. rent from said mill for life. Kyrk
2 CONC eby Stephan. The manor, [and] Knight's fees in Caberg, Hartecla, Overton and Wateby, Crossebygerad, Little Musegrave, Overton, Helton Bacoun, Great Askeby and Wynanderwat, Bampton Coundale and Gnype, Clyfton, Knoksalkok, Clyburne,
2 CONC  Colleby, Hoffe and Dryebek, Milneburne, Crakanthorpp, Kyrkeberg, Louther Wyllame and Louther Jon, et al. Warthecopp. The advowson of the church. Bruham. The advowson of the church.  She held no land in the county except of the ki
2 CONC ng. Robert de Clyfford her son, aged 18 Easter last, is her next heir. York. Inq. the day of SS. Processus and Martianus, 20 Edw. I. Malteby. The manor, including the advowson of the church, a meadow in the wood, the herbage of Li
2 CONC ttilheye, a mill worth 6 marks whereof Lady Isabel gave to Alice her nurse 5 marks yearly for life, the herbage of Swalesike, and a plot by the park in the main road, held of the honour of Tyk[hill] by scutage of ½ knight's fee, a
2 CONC nd it holds of the same honour 3¼ fees, whereof each render 10s. 8d. yearly. Robert her son, aged 18 on the feast of St. Michael last, is her next heir. E. Inq. p.m. File 1. (27.)  
