2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT It has been established that John and Isabella had at least one child, Edward.  However, other children have been linked to the couple as other possible issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Balliol. Died unmarried.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT These are notes of Stirnet in 2017:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000055369885222
2 CONT
2 CONT (F) John Baliol, Lord of Galloway, King of Scots (b 1249, d 04.1313)
2 CONT
2 CONT m. (before 07.02.1281) Isabel de Warenne (dau of John Plantagenet de Warenne, 7th Earl of Surrey)
2 CONT
2 CONT (i) Edward Baliol, King of Scots (b 1282, dsp c05.1363)
2 CONT (ii)+ other issue - Henry (b c1284/5, dsp 16.12.1332), '''Margaret (or Agnes or Maud) (b c1282, d unm)''', Anne (b c1286)
2 CONT
2 CONT There is some confusion re the identity of King John's daughters. Various sources identify 2 daughters but they are named differently, albeit normally Margaret and Anne. Various sources (including 'RoyalData' and GenEU) suggest th
2 CONC at the younger daughter married Brian FitzAlan of Bedale but TCP (FitzAlan) makes no such suggestion whilst RoyalData notes that it is not certain that Anne ever existed.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_I_de_Balliol (has in the generation before)
2 CONT
2 CONT Maud (or Matilda) de Balliol, married to Bryan FitzAlan, Lord FitzAlan, and feudal Baron of Bedale. They were parents to Agnes FitzAlan (b. 1298), who married Sir Gilbert Stapleton, Knt., of Bedale [5] (1291-1324). Gilbert is bett
2 CONC er known for his participation in the assassination of Piers Gaveston, Earl of Cornwall.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm#JohnIdied13131314B
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN Balliol, son of JOHN de Balliol of Barnard Castle, co Durham & his wife Devorguilla of Galloway ([1250]-in France [either Château Gaillard, Normandy or Bailleut-en-Gouffern, Normandy] [4 Mar 1314/4 Jan 1315], … m (before 7 Fe
2 CONC b 1279) ISABEL de Warenne, daughter of JOHN de Warenne Earl of Surrey & his [second wife ---] ([1265/69]-). 
2 CONT
2 CONT King John & his wife had [two] children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. EDWARD Balliol (-[May 1363/Sep 1365]) … 
2 CONT * 2. [HENRY Balliol (-killed in battle Annan 16 Dec 1332).  …
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Isabella De Warren was born on 1253 in Guildford Castle, Surrey, England to John De Warren, 7th Earl of Surrey and Alice "Le Brun" De Lusignan De Warren. Isabella married John II de Balliol, King of the Scots on February 7, 1280/8
2 CONC 1 and had 5 children: Edward de Balliol, King of the Scots, Henry de Balliol, Margaret de Balliol, Anne De Balliol, and Agnes Maud de Balliol. She passed away on October 23, 1295 in Barnard Castle, Teesdale, Durham, England.
