1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLAND,%20Kings%201066-1603.htm#Edmunddied1296B
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmund m firstly (contract 6 Apr 1269, Westminster Abbey 8/9 Apr 1269) AVELINE de Forz, daughter of WILLIAM de Forz Lord of Holderness, titular Comte d'Aumâle & his wife Isabel de Reviers (Burstwick, Yorkshire 20 Jan 1259-Stockwel
2 CONC l, Surrey 10 Nov 1274, bur Westminster Abbey).  The Continuator of Florence of Worcester records the marriage "VI Id Apr" of "Eadmundus filius Henrici regis" and "filiam et hæredem comitis Aubemarliæ" at Westminster[604].  The Con
2 CONC tinuator of Florence of Worcester records the death in 1274 of "Avelina uxor domini Eadmundi regis filii comitissa Aubermarliæ"[605].  The Chronicle of Thomas Wykes records the death “circa festum Sancti Martini” in 1274 of “uxor 
2 CONC domini Edmundi fratris…regis nostri”[606].  
2 CONT
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://thepeerage.com/p10223.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Aveline de Forz, Countess of Holderness1
2 CONT
2 CONT F, #102229, b. 20 January 1259, d. 10 November 1274
2 CONT
2 CONT Aveline de Forz, Countess of Holderness|b. 20 Jan 1259\nd. 10 Nov 1274|p10223.htm#i102229|William de Forz, Count of Aumale|b. b 1221\nd. 23 May 1260|p10778.htm#i107774|Isabel de Reviers|b. Jul 1237\nd. 10 Nov 1293|p10685.htm#i1068
2 CONC 50|William de Forz, Count of Aumale|d. 29 Mar 1241|p550.htm#i5494|Aveline de Montfichet|d. c Nov 1239|p4891.htm#i48901|Baldwin de Reviers, 6th Earl of Devon|d. 1245|p10683.htm#i106825|Amice de Clare|b. c 1220\nd. 1284|p10683.htm#i
2 CONC 106824|
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=23 Dec 2003
2 CONT
2 CONT Consanguinity Index=0.02%
2 CONT
2 CONT      Aveline de Forz, Countess of Holderness was born on 20 January 1259 at Burstwick, Yorkshire, England.2 She was the daughter of William de Forz, Count of Aumale and Isabel de Reviers.1,2 She married Edmund 'Crouchback' Plantag
2 CONC enet, Earl of Leicester, son of Henry III, King of England and Eleanor of Provence, on 8 April 1269 at Westminster Abbey, Westminster, London, England.2 She died on 10 November 1274 at age 15 at Stockwell, Surrey, England, without
2 CONC  issue.2,1 She was buried at Westminster Abbey, Westminster, London, England.2
2 CONT
2 CONT      Aveline de Forz, Countess of Holderness gained the title of Countess of Holderness.3 She succeeded to the title of Countess of Aumale before 6 April 1269.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
