1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==concerns==
2 CONT '''This John resembles https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-John-Mowbray-of-Althorpe/6000000173822213056.  Are they supposed to be the same person?  Further research is warranted.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==content to clean up==
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_of_Mowbray '''''House of Mowbray on Wikipedia''''']
2 CONT
2 CONT It has been said that the Mowbrays governing center in the North was a [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burton_in_Lonsdale_Castle small castle in Burton-in-Lonsdale].
2 CONT
2 CONT "This was a motte castle with two baileys. In 1322 it was confiscated from the Mowbrays who had been in opposition to King Edward II."
2 CONT
2 CONT ==John de Mowbray, 2nd Baron Mowbray==
2 CONT ''John de Mowbray, 2nd Baron Mowbray (4 September 1286 – 23 March 1322) was the son of Roger de Mowbray, 1st Baron Mowbray. Lord of the manors of Tanfield and Well, Yorkshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''De Mowbray served in the Scottish wars of Edward I. The baron held such offices as sheriff of Yorkshire, governor of the city of York, a warden of the Scottish marches, governor of Malton and Scarborough Castles.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''He took part in the rebellion of Thomas, Earl of Lancaster. He was captured at the battle of Boroughbridge and subsequently hanged at York.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''John de Mowbray married Aline de Braose, (b. 1291 d. ca 1331), daughter of William de Braose, 2nd Baron Braose and Lord of Gower.[1] They had at least two sons:''
2 CONT * John,(b. 29 November 1310, Yorkshire, England d.1361 who succeeded his father to the barony.
2 CONT * Alexander, (c. 1314 – c. 1391.)
2 CONT
2 CONT From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_de_Mowbray,_2nd_Baron_Mowbray
2 CONT
2 CONT ____________________________
2 CONT *'''Sir John de Mowbray, 2nd Baron Mowbray, Gower, & Bramber, Sheriff of York1,2,3,4,5,6,7
2 CONT *'''M, #11355, b. 4 September 1286, d. 23 March 1322
2 CONT *Father      Sir Roger de Mowbray, 1st Baron Mowbray8,9 b. c 1256, d. c 21 Nov 1297
2 CONT *Mother     Rose de Clare8,9 b. c 1255, d. a 1316
2 CONT *'''     Sir John de Mowbray, 2nd Baron Mowbray, Gower, & Bramber, Sheriff of York was born on 4 September 1286 at of Axholme, Lincolnshire, England; Also held property in Haynes & Willington, Bedfordshire; Crick, Northamptonshire
2 CONC ; Burton in Lonsdale, Hovingham, Kirkby Malzeard, & Thirsk, Yorkshire.2,4,6 He married Aline de Brewes, daughter of Sir William de Brewes, 2nd Lord Brewes, Lord Bramber & Gower and Agnes, circa 29 November 1297 at Swansea, Glamorg
2 CONC anshire, Wales; They had 1 son (Sir John, 3rd Lord Mowbray).2,3,4,5,10,6,7 Sir John de Mowbray, 2nd Baron Mowbray, Gower, & Bramber, Sheriff of York died on 23 March 1322 at York, Yorkshire, England, at age 35; Taken prisoner afte
2 CONC r the Battle of Boroughbridge (16 March 1322) and hanged a week later. Buried at Friars Preachers, York, Yorkshire.2,4,6
2 CONT *'''Family      Aline de Brewes b. c 1290, d. c 20 Jul 1331
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Sir John de Mowbray, 3rd Baron Mowbray, Baron of Axholme & Bramber+2,4,5,6,7 b. 29 Nov 1310, d. 4 Oct 1361
