1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://historytheinterestingbits.com/2018/12/08/mary-and-isabella-the-women-in-cages/?fbclid=IwAR2_gcieHQbNCTz6z1Q_gZOiXyMCi0aaPHn5-g42EFxql1yZUNs30KMMOAg
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mary Bruce (c. 1282 – 1323) was the younger sister of Robert the Bruce, King of Scots. During the First War of Scottish Independence, she was captured by the English and imprisoned in a cage at Roxburgh Castle for circa four ye
2 CONC ars. She was the daughter of Robert de Brus, 6th Lord of Annandale, and Marjorie, Countess of Carrick.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Along with the king's other female relatives (Christina Bruce, Marjorie Bruce, his wife Elizabeth de Burgh and supporter Isabella MacDuff), she was captured and betrayed to the English by the Earl of Ross. By order of King Edwa
2 CONC rd I of England, she was then held prisoner in an iron or wooden cage exposed to the public view in Roxburgh Castle. Isabella MacDuff was imprisoned in a similar cage at Berwick Castle. They were both transferred to better conditi
2 CONC ons in 1310. This was not necessarily a humane move, it has been suggested that by this stage Bruce was gaining strength, the women were potentially valuable hostages, and the English did not want them dying of exposure.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She was eventually released in exchange for English noblemen captured at the Battle of Bannockburn.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She married, firstly, Sir Neil Campbell, one of her brother's loyal supporters, by whom she had John Campbell, Earl of Atholl. She married, secondly, Alexander Fraser of Touchfraser and Cowie.
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mary_Bruce _______________________
2 CONT *'''Mary de Brus1,2,3
2 CONT *'''F, #3113, d. before 22 September 1323
2 CONT *Father     Sir Robert de Brus, Earl Carrick, Lord Annandale, Sheriff of Cumberland, Governor of Carlisle Castle4,5 b. Jul 1243, d. 13 Jan 1304
2 CONT *Mother     Margaret of Carrick4,5 b. c 1252, d. b 27 Oct 1292
2 CONT *'''     Mary de Brus married Sir Niel Campbell, son of Sir Colin (Mor) Cambel, circa 1312; They had 1 son (John, Earl of Atholl).2,3 Mary de Brus married Sir Alexander Fraser, Chamberlain of Scotland, Sheriff of Stirling, son of 
2 CONC Sir Andrew Fraser, Sheriff of Stirling and Beatrix le Chen, after 4 March 1316; They had 2 sons (John; & Sir William of Cowie & Durris).2,3 Mary de Brus died before 22 September 1323.3
2 CONT *'''Family 1      Sir Alexander Fraser, Chamberlain of Scotland, Sheriff of Stirling d. 12 Aug 1332
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Sir William Fraser+6 d. 17 Oct 1346
2 CONT **Sir John Fraser, Laird of Aberbothnot+ b. c 1317
2 CONT *'''Family 2      Sir Niel Campbell d. bt 15 Feb 1315 - Nov 1315
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Sir John Campbell, 13th Earl of Atholl2,3 b. c 1313, d. 19 Jul 1333
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S248] Unknown author, The Lineage and Ancestry of HRH Prince Charles, by Gerald Paget, Vol. 1, p. 156.
2 CONT * 2.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 527.
2 CONT * 3.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. I, p. 602-603.
2 CONT * 4.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 520-521.
2 CONT * 5.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. I, p. 595-597.
2 CONT * 6.[S147] Burke's Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Peerage, Baronetage, and Knightage, 1938 ed., by Sir Bernard Burke, p., 2179.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p104.htm#i3113 ______________________
2 CONT *'''Lady Mary Bruce1
2 CONT *'''F, #107865, d. before 22 September 1323
2 CONT *Last Edited=16 Feb 2013
2 CONT *'''     Lady Mary Bruce was the daughter of Sir Robert le Brus, 1st Lord Brus and Margaret, Countess of Carrick.1 She married, firstly, Sir Neil Campbell of Lochow, son of Sir Colin Campbell of Lochow, circa 1312.1 She married, s
2 CONC econdly, Alexander Fraser of Touchfraser and Cowie, son of Andrew Fraser and Beatrix (?), circa 1316.1 She died before 22 September 1323.1
2 CONT *'''      From circa 1312, her married name became Campbell. From circa 1316, her married name became Fraser. In 1332 and was killed at defeat of Scots by an invading host of English lords at Dupplin 12 August issue.2
2 CONT *'''Children of Lady Mary Bruce and Sir Neil Campbell of Lochow
