2 CONT When he died in 1329 his body was buried at Dumferline. His heart was removed and taken on the Crusades by  Sir James
2 CONT (the Black) Douglas,who, just before he was killed in Spain, had hurled it at the enemy. The heart was recovered and taken
2 CONT back to Melrose Abbey where the new king,David II(his son), had asked that it be buried.
