2 CONT *********								  m. Philippe de Brian (dau of Sir Guy de Brian)
2 CONT *********								(ii) Joan de Bohun
2 CONT *********								  m. John de Lisle of Gatcombe (dsp 1369)
2 CONT ********							  m2. (before 06.11.1342) Cicely Filliol (d 08.1381, dau of Sir John Filliol of Kelvedon, etc)
2 CONT *********								(iii) Sir John de Bohun of Midhurst (b 06.01.1362/3, d 25.01.1432/3)
2 CONT *********								  m1. Alice (a 12.1419)
2 CONT *********								(1) Neither Sir John nor any of his successors were called to Parliament and so were not known as Lords in their time.
2 CONT *********								(2) BE1883 reports that Sir John had 2 sons - John (his successor who was father of John whose heirs were his 2 daughters) and Sir Humphrey (who dsp). We follow TCP which suggests that he had just one son ...
2 CONT **********									(a) Sir Humphrey Bohun of Midhurst, Sheriff of Essex and Hertfordshire (b 06.05.1418, d 11.1468)
2 CONT **********									  m. Margaret Estfield (d before 15.03.1445/6, dau of Sir William Estfield, Mayor of London)
2 CONT ***********										((1)) John Bohun of Midhurst (d before 26.04.1494)
2 CONT ***********										  m. (before 25.06.1467) Anne Arderne (dau of Sir Piers Arderne of Latton)
2 CONT ************										((A)) Mary Bohun
2 CONT ************										  m. Sir David Owen of Easebourn
2 CONT ************										((B)) Ursula Bohun
2 CONT ************										  m. Sir Robert Southwell (dsp)
2 CONT *********								  m2. (before 25.10.1429) Anne Halsham (dau of John Halsham of West Grinstead and Applesham)
2 CONT *******						(3) Elizabeth de Bohun
2 CONT *******						  m. Sir John Lesley = John Lisle of Gatcombe
2 CONT *****				The following comes from Visitation (Sussex, 1530+1633-4, Cooke-Covert).
2 CONT ******					b. James Bohun
2 CONT *******						(1) John Bohun
2 CONT ******					c. Cicely Bohun
2 CONT ******					  m. William de Altaripa
2 CONT *Main source(s): BE1883 (Bohun of Midhurst) with some support/input from TCP (Bohun)
2 CONT *From: Stirnet.com
2 CONT * http://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/bb4fz/bohun2.php ______________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT James was born 3 February 1281, prematurely, as a result of his mother's falling downstairs, and hastily christened in Ford church, his godparents being James, a thatcher, and 'Lame Joan' (According to W. St. John Hope in his book
2 CONC  Cowdray and Easebourne Priory)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Sir John de Bohun, 1st Lord Bohun & Baron of Midhurst's Capetian lineage:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Hugh "Magnus" of Paris, count of Paris, duke of the Franks [First Capet]
2 CONT 2 Hugues Capet, roi des Francs
2 CONT 3 Robert II Capet, "the Pious" king of the Franks
2 CONT 4 Henry I, king of France
2 CONT 5 Hugues I 'Magnus', Comte de Vermandois
2 CONT 6 Elisabeth de Vermandois, dame de Crépy
2 CONT 7 Isabel de Beaumont, Concubine #15 of Henry I, Countess Of Pembroke
2 CONT 8 Richard "Strongbow" de Clare, 2nd Earl of Pembroke
2 CONT 9 Isabel de Clare, heiress of Pembroke
2 CONT 10 Sibyl Marshal, Countess of Derby
2 CONT 11 Lady Sibyl de Bohun (de Ferrers)
2 CONT 12 Sir John de Bohun, Baron of Midhurst
2 CONT 13 Sir James de Bohun, Baron of Midhurst and Ballymadden
2 CONT ----
