1 OCCU 2nd Lord, He died on 15 December 1329 at age 47.1, 2 He was buried at Shelford Priory, Nottinghamshire, England.1      He was invested as a Knight on 22 May 1306.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thomas Bardolf was born on October 4, 1282, at Watton at Stone, Hertfordshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Bardolf and Agnes de Grandson were married on the Lake of Neuchatel, Switzerland.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died at Watton at Stone, Hertfordshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is buried at Shelford Priory, Nottinghamshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT grave  https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/86289443/thomas-bardolf
2 CONT
2 CONT www.findagrave.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Thomas Bardolf  Birth 4 Oct 1282  Watton-at-Stone, East Hertfordshire District, Hertfordshire, England Death 15 Dec 1328 (aged 46)  Watton-at-Stone, East Hertfordshire District, Hertfordshire, England Burial  Shelford Priory  
2 CONC Shelford, Rushcliffe Borough, Nottinghamshire, England  Memorial ID 86289443
2 CONT
2 CONT This memorial is dedicated to my ancestor Sir Thomas Bardolf, 2nd Lord Bardolf.  He was the son and heir, of Sir Hugh Bardolf 1st Baron Bardolf of Wormegay and Isabel de Aguillon, Heiress of Addington. He was born October 4, 1282 
2 CONC at Watton at Stone, Hertsford County, England. He was Knighted on May 12, 1306. He was summoned to Parliament from August 26, 1307 to October 23, 1330. He married Agnes, the daughter of William de Grandison, Seigneur de Grandison 
2 CONC on Lake Neufchatel, Switzerland, by Blanche, daughter of Louis de Savoie, Baron Vaud.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members Parents
