2 CONT JOHN Ferrers of Chartley, Staffordshire, son of ROBERT de Ferrers Earl of Derby & his second wife Alianore de Bohun (Cardiff 20 Jun 1271-Gascony [Aug] 1312).  He was summoned to Parliament in 1299, whereby he is held to have becom
2 CONC e Lord Ferrers. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m (licence 1300[423]) as her second husband, HAWISE de Muscegros, widow of WILLIAM de Mortimer of Bridgewater, daughter and heiress of ROBERT de Muscegros of Stowell, Somerset & his wife Agnes --- (21 Dec 1276-[1340/50]).  She mar
2 CONC ried thirdly John de Bures. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT * 1.         JOHN de Ferrers (-before 23 Jul 1324). 
2 CONT * 2.         ROBERT de Ferrers (25 Mar 1309-28 Aug 1350).  m firstly ([21 Nov 1324/20 Oct 1330]) MARGARET, daughter of --- (-after Aug 1331).  m secondly [as her second husband,] JOAN de la Mote of Willisham, Suffolk, [widow of ED
2 CONC MUND de la Mote,] daughter of --- (-London 29 Jun 1375).  Robert & his first wife had one child, John:
2 CONT ** a)         JOHN Ferrers (Southoe [10 Aug] 1331-killed in battle Najera 3 Apr 1367).          see below. 
2 CONT * Robert & his second wife had one child:
2 CONT ** b)         ROBERT Ferrers of Willisham (before 1350-[1380/81]).  He was summoned to Parliament in [1375/79] whereby he is held to have become Lord Le Botiller[424].  m ([1369/72]) as her first husband, ELIZABETH le Botiller, da
2 CONC ughter and heiress of WILLIAM le Botiller of Wem and Oversley, Shropshire & his wife --- ([1344/45]-1411).  She married secondly John Say, and thirdly (1398) Thomas Molinton.  Robert & his wife had one child …
2 CONT *3.         PERONELLE .  m RICHARD Monemuthe of Rowley Regis, son of --- (-killed in battle 1330). 
2 CONT *4.         ELEANOR .  m ([1329]) THOMAS de Lathum, son of --- ([1300/01]-1370). 
