2 CONT 1.  Humphrey was a Constable of England. Unknown GEDCOM info: MH:N134 Unknown GEDCOM info: 31415CCE-3FAF-46F4-ADDE-E920CF8E1792
1 NOTE Earl of Hereford & Essex, Lord High Constable, K. 1321.
1 NOTE !From "Ancestral Roots of 60 Colonist" by WEIS, 6th ed, line 97, page 93; "Humphrey de BOHUN VIII, b ca 1276, slain at Boroughbridge 16 Mar 1321/2, Earl of Hereford and Essex, Lord High Constable of England; m 14 Nov 1302 Elizabet
2 CONC h Plantagenet (6-29) b Aug 1282 d 5 May 1316, dau of King Edward I. (CP IV 669; VI 467-470)."
1 NOTE !From "Ancestral Roots of 60 Colonist" by WEIS, 6th ed, line 97, page 93; "Humphrey de BOHUN VIII, b ca 1276, slain at Boroughbridge 16 Mar 1321/2, Earl of Hereford and Essex, Lord High Constable of England; m 14 Nov 1302 Elizabet
2 CONC h Plantagenet (6-29) b Aug 1282 d 5 May 1316, dau of King Edward I. (CP IV 669; VI 467-470)."
1 NOTE !From "Ancestral Roots of 60 Colonist" by WEIS, 6th ed, line 97, page 93; "Humphrey de BOHUN VIII, b ca 1276, slain at Boroughbridge 16 Mar 1321/2, Earl of Hereford and Essex, Lord High Constable of England; m 14 Nov 1302 Elizabet
2 CONC h Plantagenet (6-29) b Aug 1282 d 5 May 1316, dau of King Edward I. (CP IV 669; VI 467-470)."
1 NOTE !From "Ancestral Roots of 60 Colonist" by WEIS, 6th ed, line 97, page 93; "Humphrey de BOHUN VIII, b ca 1276, slain at Boroughbridge 16 Mar 1321/2, Earl of Hereford and Essex, Lord High Constable of England; m 14 Nov 1302 Elizabet
2 CONC h Plantagenet (6-29) b Aug 1282 d 5 May 1316, dau of King Edward I. (CP IV 669; VI 467-470)."
1 NOTE !    (1) Earl of Hereford and Essex, aged 22 at his father's death, Inq.p.m. 27
2 CONT     Edw. I, No.142; Gave Powderham to his d., Margaret, as a marriage portion;
2 CONT     Killed at Borough Bridge 1322; cr. 8th Earl of Essex 1302-1304: ped.--Vp106
2 CONT     (2) 8th Earl of Hereford; (suc'd in 1229--Dates); conveyed lands in 1302; slain
2 CONT     1321; md 1302-4 Princess Elizabeth, 1282-1316, d. of Edward I--CPv4p669; and
2 CONT     "widow" of John, Earl of Holland--BGT; had 8 sons and 9 daus.--CPv4; had 4
2 CONT     daus.--Dw v1p57
2 CONT     (3) Humphrey de Bohun VIII: (b.1276, d.March 16, 1322 at the Battle of
2 CONT     Boroughbridge, buried at Friars Preachers Church, County York).  He married
2 CONT     November 25, 1302 at Westminster, Lady Elizabeth Plantagenet, daughter of King
2 CONT     Edward I and widow of John, Count of Holland.  Humphrey was fourth Earl of
2 CONT     Hereford and third Earl of Essex and Constable of England.  In 1301 he joined
2 CONT     the barons in their letter of protest to the pope from the parliament of
2 CONT     Lincoln.  He took a leading part in the tournaments of Fulham in 1305 and at
2 CONT     Wallingford in 1307. In 1308 he was sent to Scotland to oppose Robert Bruce.
2 CONT     He was one of the twenty-one ordainers appointed to reform the government and
2 CONT     the king's household.  The ordinances were accepted in October 1311, but three
2 CONT     months later the king recalled his banished favorite, Gaveston, and immediately
2 CONT     the barons, including de Bohun, took arms against Gaveston, captured and
2 CONT     beheaded him.  Edward was powerless to punish the rebellious lords;
2 CONT     negotiations for peace were opened and in October 1313 the earls and their
2 CONT     followers were pardoned.  In 1314 the war with Scotland was renewed and de
2 CONT     Bohun was taken prisoner at the battle of Bannockburn.  He was later exchanged
2 CONT     for Elizabeth, wife of Robert Bruce, King of Scotland, who had long been held
2 CONT     captive in England.  During the next six years the resentment of the barons
2 CONT     increased as the power of the two Despensers, father and son, grew over the
2 CONT     king.  It finally came to a head at the battle of Boroughbridge in which the
2 CONT     king finally defeated the barons and de Bohun lost his life.  Elizabeth was
2 CONT     born August 5, 1282, Rhudlan Castle, County Carnarvon and died May 5, 1316 and
2 CONT     was buried at Walden Abbey.  By her Humphrey had six sons and four daughters.
2 CONT     --Aedc,FHL 929.273,C769w
1 NOTE 4th Earl of Hereford, 3rd of Essex, also Constable of England.
1 NOTE Humphrey de Bohun, 4. jarl av Hereford (1276 - 16. mars 1322) var et medlem av en betydningsfull anglo-normannisk familie fra Marche fra Wales. Hans far var Humphrey de Bohun, 3. jarl av Hereford og hans mor var Maud de Fiennes, d
2 CONC atter av Enguerrand II de Finnes. Han ble født ved Pleshey Castle i Essex, England. Slottet er i dag ikke mer enn en ruin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Humphrey de Bohun etterfulgte sin far og fikk titlene jarl av Hereford og baron de Bohun. Han holdt også tittelen ?Bærer av svanemerket?. Han giftet seg med Elizabeth av Rhuddlan, datter av kong Edvard I av England og hans første
2 CONC  dronning Eleanor av Castilla den 14. november 1302 i Westminister. Hun ga ham ti barn:
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret de Bohun (september 1303 - 1305) 
2 CONT Eleanor de Bohun (oktober 1304), gift med James Butler, 1. jarl av Ormonde og Thomas, Lord Dagworth. 
2 CONT Humphrey de Bohun (1305 - døde ung) 
2 CONT John de Bohun, 5. jarl av Hereford (23. november 1306 - 1335) 
2 CONT Humphrey de Bohun, 6. jarl av Hereford (6. desember 1309 - 1361) 
2 CONT Margaret de Bohun (3. april 1311 - 1391), gift med Hugh Courtenay, 2. jarl av Devon 
2 CONT William de Bohun, 1. jarl av Northampton (1312-1360). Tvillingbror av Edward. 
2 CONT Edward de Bohun (1312 - 1334). Tvillingbror av William. 
2 CONT Eneas de Bohun, død etter 1322, hvor han blir nevnt i farens testamente. 
2 CONT Isabel de Bohun (5. mai 1316). Elizabeth døde i fødselen og dette barnet noen dager etter. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Slaget ved Bannockburn
2 CONT I slaget ved Bannockburn angrep Humphrey de Bohun selveste Robert Bruce, bare for selv å bli kastet til bakken, tatt til fange og senere utvekslet som gissel mot Bruces kone. Men det som først og fremst assosieres med navnet de B
2 CONC ohun og Bannockburn er at Humphrey de Bohuns nevø Henry de Bohun også angrep Robert Bruce, men endte med en krigsøks i skallen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Humphrey de Bohun selv døde senere i slaget ved Boroughbridge på en særdeles motbydelig måte. I boken ?The Greatest Traitor? ved Ian Mortimer, side 124, nevnes det:
2 CONT
2 CONT (Den 4. jarlen av) Hereford ledet angrepet på broen, men han og hans menn gikk rett i en sky av piler. En av de Harcleys spydmenn, skjult under broren, stakk spydet oppover mellom plankene og spiddet jarlen av Hereford opp gjenno
2 CONC m endetarmen, vred jernodden rundt i hans innvoller. Han døde skrikende og snudde angrepet til en panikk. 
