1 OCCU Lord VERDON (2ND), LORD OF WEOBERLY, 2nd Lord Verdun, Constable of Ireland
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Theobald II, Lord of Verdun
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=68807235
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	Sep. 8, 1278 Cheadle Staffordshire, England Death: 	Jul. 27, 1316 Alton Staffordshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theobald_de_Verdun,_2nd_Baron_Verdun
2 CONT
2 CONT Knight, 2nd Lord Verdun of Alton, Staffordshire, of Weobley Herefordshire, of Franham Verdon, Buckinghamshire and of Wilsford, Wiltshire. Hereditary Constable of Ireland, Justiciar of Ireland, hereditary patron of Croxden Abbey.
2 CONT
2 CONT Second but eldest surviving son of Thebaud de Verdun and Margery de Bohun. Grandson of John de Verdun and Margery de Lacy, daughter of Gilbert. Grandson of Humphrey de Bohun and Eleanor de Brewes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Maud de Mortimer, married 29 July 1302 at Wigmore, Herefordshire. Maud was the daughter of Sir Edmund de Mortimer, 1st Lord Mortimer, a descendant of King John and Margaret de Fiennes, daughter of William and descendant
2 CONC  of King Henry II. Her maritagium included the Castle and Manor of Dunamase in Ireland. They had four daughters:
2 CONT * Joan, wife of Sir Thomas de Furnival
2 CONT * Elizabeth, wife of Sir Bartholomew de Burghersh
2 CONT * Margery, wife of Sir John Crophill
2 CONT * Katherine
2 CONT
2 CONT Theobald was knighted by the King in Northumberland on 24 June 1298. He fought in the second line at Falkirk July of 1298. Summoned to Parliament 1299 to 1315 as Theobaldo de Verdun junior, where as he became Lord Verdun.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maud died at Alton, Staffordshire on the 17th or 18th of Sept 1312 after childbirth and buried at Croxden Abbey.
2 CONT
2 CONT Theobald married again, to Elizabeth de Clare, the daughter of Gilbert de Clare, 6th Earl of Gloucester and Joan of England the daughter of King Edward I. She was the widow of John de Burgh, who died in a skirmish on the 18th of J
2 CONC une 1313. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *They had one daughter, Isabel, who would marry Henry de Ferrers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Theobald would die estate at Alton, Staffordshire. His widow would remarry Sir Roger D'Amory by 1317. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Parents:
2 CONT   Thebaud de Verdun (1248 - 1309)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Spouses:
2 CONT   Matilda Maud de Mortimer Verdun (1285 - 1312)*
2 CONT   Elizabeth de Clare (1295 - 1360)*
2 CONT
2 CONT  Children:
2 CONT   Joan De Verdun (1303 - 1334)*
2 CONT   Elizabeth de Verdun Burghersh (1306 - 1360)*
2 CONT   Isabel de Verdun (1315 - 1349)*
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL.htm '''English Medieval Nobility]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ELIZABETH de Clare (Tewkesbury 16 Sep 1295-4 Nov 1360) m secondly (near Bristol 4 Feb 1316) as his second wife, THEOBALD de Verdon Lord Verdon, son of JOHN de Verdon & his wife Margery de Lacy (-27 Jul 1316, bur Croxden Abbey, Sta
2 CONC ffs). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Theobald de Verdun, 2nd Lord Verdun1
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #106932, b. 8 September 1278, d. 27 July 1316
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.thepeerage.com/p10694.htm#i106932  '''Sir Theobald de Verdun]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Theobald de Verdun, 2nd Lord Verdun was born on 8 September 1278.3 He was the son of Theobald Verdun, 1st Lord Verdun and Margery de Bohun.2 He married, firstly, Maud de Mortimer, daughter of Sir Edmund de Mortimer, on 29 July
2 CONC  1302 at Wigmore, Herefordshire, England.3 He married, secondly, Elizabeth de Clare, daughter of Gilbert de Clare, 6th Earl of Gloucester and Joan of Acre, on 4 February 1315/16.3 He died on 27 July 1316 at age 37 at Alton Castle,
2 CONC  Alton, Staffordshire, England.3
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Theobald de Verdun, 2nd Lord Verdun gained the title of 2nd Lord Verdun.1 He lived at Alton, Staffordshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~bhusler/Bill/Reunion/Web%20Cards/ps04/ps04_014.html '''Theobald de Verdun''']
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT aka: 2d Baron Verdon, Knt. of Alton, co. Stafford, 2nd Lord Verdun, lord of half the barony of Weobley co. Herford, Justiciar of Ireland, son and heir of Theobald de Vernun (or le Botiler) by his wife Margery. He was summoned to P
2 CONC arliament v.p. from 29 Dec 1299 by writs directed (till his father's death) Theobaldo de Verdun junior, whereby he also is held to have become Lord Verdun. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 1st Maud de Mortimer, and had three daughters, she died after childbirth. 
2 CONT
2 CONT by Elizabeth de Clare had one dau, Isabel de Verdun m. Henry de Ferrers born posthoumously at Amesbury co. Wilts in 1317.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT # Otway-Ruthven, A. J. “The Partition of the De Verdon Lands in Ireland in 1332.” Proceedings of the Royal Irish Academy. Section C: Archaeology, Celtic Studies, History, Linguistics, Literature 66 (1967): 401–55. http://www.jstor
2 CONC .org/stable/25505141.
2 CONT # Roberts, Gary Boyd. ''The Royal Descents of 600 Immigrants''. Baltimore, MD, USA: Genealogical Publishing Co., (2004). Section: Immigrant Descendants of High Medieval Kings. Page 385. < [https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/coll
2 CONC ections/49324/images/FLHG_RoyalDescentsof600Immigrants-0489?ranMID=50138&ranEAID=4026539&ranSiteID=Xib7NfnK11s-OX.rA2C0xPEjs.87ueVoQw&o_xid=4026539&o_lid=4026539&o_sch=Affiliate+External&pId=93946 Ancestry.com] >; ([https://www.ge
2 CONC ni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000212566386836 document attached.]) "Descent from https://www.geni.com/people/Alfonso-IX-king-of-Leon-and-Galicia/6000000008477543238 & https://www.geni.com/people/Berenguela-I-la-Grande-reina-de-
2 CONC Castilla/6000000001412951572?through=6000000008477543238." 
