1 OCCU Baron of Bergavenny, 1ST BARON HASTINGS
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Hastings, 1st Baron Hastings (6 May 1262 – 28 February 1313) was an English peer and soldier of the Middle Ages. Hastings was a competitor for the Scottish throne in 1290/92 in the Great Cause.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Parents: Henry de Hastings, 1st Baron Hastings (c. 1235–c. 1269), Joanna de Cantilupe, sister and heiress of his uncle George de Cantilupe(d.1273)
2 CONT * Married: Isabel de Valence, Isabel le Despenser
2 CONT
2 CONT ==biography==
2 CONT
2 CONT Baron Hastings, 13th Baron Bergavenny
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Henry de Hastings and Joan de Cantelou / Cantilupe, grandson of Sir Henry de Hastings and Ada of Huntingdon, William de Cauntelo and Eve de Braose.
2 CONT
2 CONT Firstly, husband of Isabel de Valence, daughter of William de Valence, Earl of Pembroke. they were married in 1275 and had six children:
2 CONT * Elizabeth de Hastings, wife of Sir Roger Grey
2 CONT * William de Hastings, married Eleanor Martin
2 CONT * Joan de Hastings, wife of William de Huntyngfield
2 CONT * John de Hastings, 2nd Lord Hastings
2 CONT * Henry de Hastings
2 CONT * Margaret de Hastings
2 CONT
2 CONT Secondly, he was the husband of Isabel le Despenser, daughter of Hugh le Despenser, 1st and last Earl of Winchester and Isabella de Beauchamp. They married before 1308 and had three children:
2 CONT * Thomas de Hastings
2 CONT * Margaret Hastings, wife of Robert de Waterville.
2 CONT * Sir Hugh de Hastings
2 CONT
2 CONT John Hastings was summoned to Parliament as Lord Hastings on 23 June 1295. He received the title of Baron Bergavenny at the death of his uncle, George de Cantilupe in 1273, and inherited Abergavenny Castle as well as the honor of 
2 CONC Abergavenny. John participated in the wars of King Edward I in Scotland, Ireland and France, appointed to Seneschal of Aquitaine. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His attempt to claim the Scottish throne as the grandson of Ada, third daughter of David, Earl of Huntingdon who was the grandson of King David of Scotland was unsuccessful.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Hastings,_1st_Baron_Hastings Wikipedia]
2 CONT * http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=aet%2Dt&id=I9980
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT    Sir John Hastings, 2nd Baron Hastings, Baron Abergavenny, Seneschal of Aquitaine was born on 6 May 1262 at Allesley, Warwickshire, England; Age 6 in 1269. He and Isabel de Valence obtained a marriage license on 15 July 1275 at 
2 CONC Braxted, Essex, England; The marriage may have taken place at Blunham, Bedfordshire instead. Date of Papal Dispensation, being related in the 3rd and 4th degrees of kindred. They had 3 sons (Sir William; John, 2nd Lord Hastings; &
2 CONC  Henry, a cleric) and 3 daughters (Joan, wife of William de Huntingfield; Elizabeth, wife of Sir Roger, 1st Lord Grey of Ruthin; & Margaret, wife of William, 2nd Lord Martin, & of Sir Robert, Lord Wateville). Sir John Hastings, 2n
2 CONC d Baron Hastings, Baron Abergavenny, Seneschal of Aquitaine married Isabel le Despenser, daughter of Sir Hugh le Despenser, Earl of Winchester, Constable of Devizes, Marlborough, Odiham, St. Briavel's, & Striguil Castles and Isabe
2 CONC l de Beauchamp, circa 1308; They had 2 sons (Sir Hugh; & Thomas). Sir John Hastings, 2nd Baron Hastings, Baron Abergavenny, Seneschal of Aquitaine died on 10 February 1313 at age 50; Buried in Hastings Chapel, Church of the Friars
2 CONC  Minor, Coventry, Warwickshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p435.htm#i13069
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Updated from [http://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-1/myheritage-family-trees?itemId=245706521-1-32911&action=showRecord&indId=externalindividual-072435c7f3d55c16baef4ee346a1809b&mrid=eb7ccf01f6bddf34f46bffdc429c29b3 MyH
2 CONC eritage Match] via son [http://www.geni.com/profile-34644176384 John Hastings] by [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 20 2014, 20:14:50 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * John was 1st Baron Hastings. 
2 CONT * He spent much of his life engaged in combat, having fought in the 1290s in the Scottish, Irish, and French wars during the reign of King Edward I "Longshanks" Plantagenet of England.
2 CONT * He was appointed Seneschal of Aquitaine.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/108457598/person/220066392540 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 1 2018, 1:38:40 UTC''www.findagrave.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John de Hastings
2 CONT BIRTH	6 May 1262
2 CONT Allesley, Metropolitan Borough of Coventry, West Midlands, England
2 CONT DEATH	28 Feb 1313 (aged 50)
2 CONT Abergavenny, Monmouthshire, Wales
2 CONT BURIAL	
2 CONT St Michael's Cathedral
2 CONT Coventry, Metropolitan Borough of Coventry, West Midlands, England 
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID	65164944 
2 CONT
2 CONT Baron Hastings, 13th Baron Bergavenny
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Henry de Hastings and Joan de Cantelou / Cantilupe, grandson of Sir Henry de Hastings and Ada of Huntingdon, William de Cauntelo and Eve de Braose.
2 CONT
2 CONT Firstly, husband of Isabel de Valence, daughter of William de Valence, Earl of Pembroke. they were married in 1275 and had six children:
2 CONT * Elizabeth de Hastings, wife of Sir Roger Grey
2 CONT * William de Hastings, married Eleanor Martin
