1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Gerald fitzMaurice FitzGerald''', ''3rd Earl of Desmond'', died in 1398. He was also known by the Irish Gaelic "Gearóid Iarla" (Earl Gerald)
2 CONT
2 CONT Acceded: 1357
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:  son of Maurice FitzGerald, 1st Earl of Desmond, by his third wife Aveline, daughter of Nicholas FitzMaurice, 3rd Lord of Kerry.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: 
2 CONT # after 20 July 1359 to Eleanor (or Ellen) Butler, ''Countess Desmond'', daughter of James Butler, 2nd Earl of Ormond. They had three sons and two daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sons of Eleanor Butler and Gerald FitzGerald:
2 CONT # John FitzGerald, 4th Earl of Desmond
2 CONT # Maurice FitzGerald
2 CONT # James FitzGerald, 6th Earl of Desmond, 'the Usurper'
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughters of Eleanor Butler and Gerald FitzGerald:
2 CONT # Joan, married Maurice FitzJohn, Lord of Kerry
2 CONT # Catherine, married John FitzThomas (C. Ormond)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Silver Shod Steed==
2 CONT
2 CONT After his disappearance in 1398, Gerald sleeps in a cave under [http://www.shannonheritage.com/Attractions/LoughGur/ Lough Gur], and will someday awaken and ride forth on a silver-shod steed to rule again in Desmond.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Career and poetry==
2 CONT
2 CONT Gerald was made Lord Chief Justice of Ireland in 1367, but in 1370 was imprisoned by Brian O'Brien of Thomond.[1] While in prison, Gerald wrote poetry in the Irish language, most famously the poem Mairg adeir olc ris na mnáibh ("S
2 CONC peak not ill of womenkind"). Indeed, Gerald was instrumental in replacing French with Irish as the preferred language of the Hiberno-Norman aristocracy, and typified the cliché among later Irish historians that the Geraldines were
2 CONC  "more Irish than the Irish themselves."
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes==
2 CONT * Gearóid Iarla. The Poet. 
2 CONT * 4th Earl of Desmond whose wife was Elenor Butler. You should be able to relate directly as a grand daughter to King Henry Plantagenet 3rd and all of the Plantagenet kings including William the Conqueror
2 CONT
2 CONT ==links==
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gerald_FitzGerald,_3rd_Earl_of_Desmond
2 CONT * [http://www.shannonheritage.com/Attractions/LoughGur/ Lough Gur]
2 CONT * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desmond_Rebellions Desmond Rebellions]
2 CONT * [http://www.of-ireland.info/castles/shanid.html Shanid Castle]
2 CONT
