2 CONT
2 CONT Angus MacKintosh Born about 1268 in Invercauld, Moray Scotlandmap Son of Shaw Macintosh Jr. and Unknown Unknown Husband of Eva (Gillpatrick) MacKintosh — married before 1295 in Moray, Scotlandmap Father of Seumas Ian MacKintosh Di
2 CONC ed [date unknown] in Scotlandmap Profile manager: Beth Babcock private message [send private message] MacKintosh-102 created 7 Nov 2013 | Last modified 20 Dec 2014 This page has been accessed 360 times.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents
2 CONT
2 CONT [hide] 1 Biography 2 Sources 2.1 Footnotes 2.2 Acknowledgments Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Angus married Eva Gillpatrick and had a son Ian.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT Historical documents and books on Clan MacKintosh. http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clan_Mackintosh
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''Angus Mackintosh, 6th of Mackintosh'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.thepeerage.com/p45043.htm#i450429 The Peerage] #450429,
2 CONT
2 CONT Angus Mackintosh, 6th of Mackintosh
2 CONT * Son of Ferquhard Mackintosh, 5th of Mackintosh.
2 CONT * Married Eva of Chattan, daughter of Dougal, 6th Captain of Clan Chattan, in 1291.
2 CONT * Died in 1345.
2 CONT
2 CONT During his minority, the Comyns seized Meikle Geddes, Rait and the castle of Inverness and the Mackintoshes did not regain them for another hundred years. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1319 he received a grant of lands of Benchar, in Badenoch, from which the Comyns had been expelled.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children of Angus Mackintosh, 6th of Mackintosh and Eva of Chattan'''
2 CONT * William Mackintosh, 7th of Mackintosh d. 1368
2 CONT * John Mackintosh
2 CONT * Angus 'Og' Mackintosh
2 CONT
2 CONT He had five other sons and two daughters. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Citation'''
2 CONT * BP2003 volume 2, page 2512
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Brought up in the court of his uncle, Alexander Og MacDonald, Lord of Islay. Fought against the English at the '''Battle of Bannockburn''' in 1314, under Randolph, Earl of Moray. His lands of Meikle Geddes, Rait Castle and Inverne
2 CONC ss Castle were taken by the Clan Comyn. Married Eva, the daughter of Gilpatric Dougal Dall, the 6th chief of Clan Chattan. After Gilpatric's death Angus became chief of both Clan Mackintosh and Clan Chattan.
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chiefs_of_Clan_Mackintosh Chiefs of Clan MacKintosh]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Pedigree is given in the ancient manuscripts as Shaw mac Gilchrisht mac Ian mac Angus mac Farquhar, etc., (Mac being the Gaelic for son).  He was the leader of the victorious thirty at the battle of the North Inch of Perth, 1396, 
2 CONC which Sir Walter Scott so graphically describes in his “Fair Maid of Perth”.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Pedigree is given in the ancient manuscripts as Shaw mac Gilchrisht mac Ian mac Angus mac Farquhar etc...  (Mac being the Gaelic for son).  He was the leader of the victorious thirty at the battle of the North Inch of Perth, 1396,
2 CONC  which Sir Walter Scott so graphically describes in his "Fair Maid of Perth".
