2 CONT
2 CONT ===SIR ADAM MURE OF ROWALLAN===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Adam Mure of Rowallan is the son of Sir William Mure of Rowallan. According to the Historie, his father died in or about 1348 [https://archive.org/stream/historieanddesc00muirgoog#page/n49/mode/1up Historie, p. 43] and: "Sr
2 CONC  Adame succeided [https://archive.org/stream/historieanddesc00muirgoog#page/n50/mode/1up Ibidem, p. 44]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Adam Mure of Rowallan was the first member of the family to quarter his own paternal coat of arms, viz. Argent, on a fesse Azure three stars of the First, with the arms of his ancestor Sir Walter Comyn, viz. Azure, three ga
2 CONC rbs Or. [https://archive.org/stream/historiedescento1825mure#page/22/mode/1up Historie, pp. 22-3]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not been identified for Sir Adam Mure of Rowallan but his son and heir, also Sir Adam Mure of Rowallan, had a charter for Rowallan on 11 November 1391, and it is supposed that his father may have d
2 CONC ied before this date. [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=njp.32101038096846;view=1up;seq=360 Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, charter number 835 on page 330]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 November 1391: Charter by which Robert III, King of Scots, confirms possession of Rowallan to Sir Adam Mure of Rowallan: "Ade More de Rowalane, militi." [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=njp.32101038096846;view=1up;seq
2 CONC =360 Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, charter number 835 on page 330]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogical Accounts===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/historieanddesc00muirgoog#page/n7/mode/1up The Historie and Descent of the House of Rowallane, 141 pp.]
2 CONT
