1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Joan de Somery1
2 CONT *F, #118850, d. after 18 January 1326/27
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan de Somery was the daughter of Roger de Somery.1 She died after 18 January 1326/27.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Joan de Somery and Thomas de Botetourt
2 CONT *1.John de Botetourt, 2nd Lord Botetourt+1 b. c 1318, d. 1385
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Somery-33
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Joan "Lady of Honesworth" de Somery
2 CONT *Born about 1292 in Dudley Castle, Staffordshire
2 CONT *Died before 12 Feb 1338 
2 CONT *Father	Sir Roger de Somery, Baron Dudley[1] b. 24 Jun 1255, d. 11 Oct 1291
2 CONT *Mother	Agnes[2] d. 23 Nov 1308
2 CONT
2 CONT Joane de Somery was born circa 1292; Age 30 in 1322.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Sir Thomas Botetourt, son of Sir John Botetourt, 1st Lord Botetourt, Admiral of the North Fleet, Constable of St. Briavels Castle, Governor of Framlingham Castle and Maud FitzThomas, before 1318.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT They had 1 son (Sir John, 2nd Lord Botetourt) & 1 daughter (Maud, wife of Sir Reynold, 4th Lord Grey of Wilton).[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Joane de Somery died circa 12 February 1338.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT *Sir Thomas Botetourt b. c 1292, d. c 28 Jul 1322
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT #Maud Botetourt b. c 1316, d. 14 Sep 1391
2 CONT #Sir John Botetourt, 2nd Lord Botetourt b. bt Aug 1317 - Dec 1317, d. 4 Apr 1386
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Johanna was the widow of Thomas Botetourt before or about 1323
2 CONT
