2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000079309152316& Inquisition Post Mortem] for Philip de Aylesbury, Writ, 20 August, 23 Edward III [1349]. <br>
2 CONT Mentions Philip and Margaret his wife, Thomas their son who died in the lifetime of Philip. Philip died on 14 July [1349]. John son of Thomas, aged 13 years and more, was Philip’s heir.
2 CONT
2 CONT CP 25/1/19/81, number 7.<br>
2 CONT Link:	[http://aalt.law.uh.edu/AALT7/CP25%281%29/CP25_1_19/IMG_0148.htm Image of document at AALT]<br>
2 CONT County:	Buckinghamshire.<br>
2 CONT Place:	York.<br>
2 CONT Date:	One week from St Michael, 9 Edward III [6 October 1335].<br>
2 CONT Parties:	John de Saleford', chaplain, querent, and '''Philip de Aylesbury and Margaret, his wife''', deforciants.<br>
2 CONT Property:	'''The manor of Middelton' Kaynes'''.<br>
2 CONT Action:	Plea of covenant.<br>
2 CONT Agreement:	Philip and Margaret have acknowledged the manor to be the right of John, as that which he has of their gift.<br>
2 CONT For this:	John has granted to Philip and Margaret the manor and has rendered it to them in the court, to hold to Philip and Margaret, of the lord king and his heirs for the lives of Philip and Margaret. And after the decease of Ph
2 CONC ilip and Margaret the manor shall remain to '''Thomas, son of the same Philip''', and his heirs, to hold of the lord king and his heirs for ever.<br>
2 CONT Note:	This agreement was made by the command of the lord king.<br>
2 CONT Source: [http://www.medievalgenealogy.org.uk/fines/abstracts/CP_25_1_19_81.shtml#7 Abstracts of Feet of Fines]
