2 CONT *'''Sir Ralph Basset the 1st Lord Basset of Drayton (born before 1265 - 31 December 1299) was an English nobleman of the 13th century who fought in both the Anglo-French War and in the First War of Scottish Independence. He was th
2 CONC e son of Ralph Basset and Margaret de Somery.[1] In 1291, he was granted the governorship of Edinburgh Castle.[2] He was created 1st Lord Basset of Drayton in 1295.
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ralph_Basset,_1st_Lord_Basset_of_Drayton _____________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Ralph Bassett [Parents] was born about 1242 in Stafford, Staffordshire, England. He died on 31 Dec 1299. He married Hawise (Hesewise) De Grey about 1261 in Drayton, Staffordshire, England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hawise (Hesewise) De Grey [Parents] was born about 1239 in Drayton, Staffordshire, England. She married Ralph Bassett about 1261 in Drayton, Staffordshire, England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *F i Margaret Bassett  http://members.cox.net/dhess5/pafg147.htm#3525
2 CONT
2 CONT _______________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Baron Ralph Basset, second Baron 
2 CONT
2 CONT c 1200
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: Baron Ralph Basset m Margaret de Someri
2 CONT
