1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Maude-de-Grey/6000000009459131078?through=6000000174943191003<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Maud Basset was the daughter of Sir Ralph Basset and Margaret de Somery.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Traditionally she was said to have married  https://www.geni.com/people/John-de-Grey-2nd-Baron-of-Wilton/6000000000658152258, son of Sir Reynold de Grey, 1st Lord Grey (of Wilton) and Maud de Longchamp.
2 CONT
2 CONT Before 2002 John's wife was generally thought to be Maud Bassett, but Douglas Richardson found through his research into property transfer and dispute records, and marriage records of the time that Maud de Verdun, the daughter of 
2 CONC Eleanor (de Bohun) Verdun was most certainly the wife of this John de Grey. Corrections were made to the Complete Peerage: Volume 6: Grey of Wilton, following the evidence submitted by Douglas Richardson in 2002 regarding facts he
2 CONC  brought to light through his study of documentary evidence from over 700 years before.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://mospace.umsystem.edu/xmlui/bitstream/handle/10355/45935/HazellBasFamMar.pdf?sequence=1&isAllowed=y
2 CONT
2 CONT Although her sons, Ralph V and Roger, are listed has having been born in the 1240s, her daughter Matilda Basset is noted to have been born shortly before her father’s death at Evesham.70
