2 CONC , i. 461. 3. VCH Lancs. iii. 25. 4. DKR, xl. 532; Chetham Soc. n.s. xcvi. 70. 5. Chetham Soc. xcv. 123-4; n.s. xciii. 38-39; Ormerod, ii (1), 96, 131-2; VCH Lancs. iv. 143; DKR, xxxii. 353; xxxvi (2), 195. 6. Lancs. Feet of Fines,
2 CONC  iii. 18, 35; Test. Ebor. i. 188, 190; CCR, 1389-92, p. 71; Cal. Scots Docs. (supp.) v. nos. 4153, 4292, 4348, 4387; Chetham Soc. xcv. 11, 25, 61; DKR, xxxii. 364; xxxvii (2), 301; Scrope v. Grosvenor, i. 288; M.J. Bennett. ‘Late 
2 CONC Med. Soc. in N.W. Eng.’ (Lancaster Univ. Ph.D. thesis, 1975), 69. 7. DL28/27/3; DL29/738/12100; DL42/15, ff. 64v, 70v, 101v, 110v, 131v; Chetham Soc. n.s. lxxxvii. 55, 59, 75-77, 102-3; DKR, xliii. 3. 8. DKR, xxxvi (2), 7, 196; Be
2 CONC nnett, 50-52, 63; C219/10/6, 11/1A, 4; CCR, 1402-5, p. 460; 1413-19, p. 194; Chetham Soc. xcix. 30; n.s. xcv. 83. 9. Chetham Soc. xcv. 123-4; n.s. xciii. 37-38; xcvi. 155-7.
2 CONT
