2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT #  [http://archive.org/stream/historyofmacleod00mack#page/288/mode/2up History of the Macleods with genealogies of the principal families of the name. By Alexander Mackenzie (1889), page 288]
2 CONT # [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/mac/macleod06.php Stirne[t: Macleod 06]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT "V. <strong>Roderick Macleod, Fifth of Lewis</strong>. "In 1449 a charter of John of Yle is witnessed by Roderick Macleoid of Leoghuis." He married Margaret, daughter of the Lord of the Isles, with issue — 
2 CONT * Torquil, his heir and successor. 
2 CONT * Tormod, to whom he gave the Barony of Assynt, and from whom are descended the Macleod families of Assynt, Geanies, and Cadboll, an account of which will be given in their proper order. 
2 CONT * Margaret, who, as his second wife, married William Mackintosh, VII. of Mackintosh, with issue ; among others, Malcolm Beg, who succeeded his nephew, Ferquhard, as X. of Mackintosh, and carried on the succession, though his uncle
2 CONC  Ferquhard left three sons, the eldest of whom was the legal heir.
2 CONT
2 CONT Roderick died at an advanced age, when he was succeeded by his eldest son."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/historyofmacleod00mack#page/288/mode/2up History of the Macleods with genealogies of the principal families of the name]; Alexander Mackenzie; 1889; page 288
2 CONT
