2 CONT Roderick MacLeod, 5th of the Lewes1
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #506301 Last Edited=23 Aug 2014
2 CONT      Roderick MacLeod, 5th of the Lewes is the son of Torquil MacLeod, 4th of the Lewes and Margaret MacNicol of Assynt.2 He married Margaret Macdonald, daughter of Alastair Macdonald, 10th Earl of Ross.1
2 CONT      He was living in 1449.1 Children of Roderick MacLeod, 5th of the Lewes and Margaret Macdonald
2 CONT
2 CONT Torquil MacLeod, 6th of the Lewes+2 Tormod MacLeod2 Margaret MacLeod+2 Child of Roderick MacLeod, 5th of the Lewes
2 CONT
2 CONT unknown daughter MacLeod+2 Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S37] BP2003 volume 2, page 2530. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37] [S37] BP2003. [S37]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT . Roderick MacLeod [Ruaidhri Mor], who was born ca. 1350. It is mentioned in the clan tradition that this Roderick Macleod fought at the battle of Harlaw in 1411, together with his cousin , John Macleod of Dunvegan, under personal
2 CONC  command of Donald of the Isles . The latter granted on 8 Oct. 1415 a charter to Angus Mackay of Strathnaver and his son whilst this charter was witnessed by this Roderick MacLeod . He also appears in other documents . According t
2 CONC o Sir Robert Douglas of Glenbervie in 1798 this Roderick MacLeod married Margaret Macdonald, daughter of the Lord of the Isles . However Canon R.C. MacLeod in 1927 states Roderick to be married to a daughter of John MacLeod of Dun
2 CONC vegan . So who is correct ?
2 CONT Issue from this marriage:
2 CONT 1. Torquil [Torcall] MacLeod, who follows VI .
2 CONT 2. Norman MacLeod , who his father gave the Barony of Assynt to. From him descend The MacLeods of Assynt, Geanies and Cadboll.
2 CONT 3. Roderick MacLeod , who is mentioned in a papal document of 15 may 1403 as not to be of good health and may have died at a young age .
2 CONT 4. Margaret MacLeod , who married William MacKintosh , VII  of MacKintosh , of whom the Chiefs of MacKintosh descend .
