0 @N6000000003796207305@ NOTE ==================================================================
1 CONT
1 CONT A Grandchild's Heritage URL:  http://www.reach.net/~roanne/macmurrough.html
1 CONT
1 CONT Generation No. 60-62
1 CONT
1 CONT 60 Labhradh: son of Breasal Bealach. Had the following sons: 
1 CONT Eanna Cinnsealaigh, who is described below. 
1 CONT Deagh, a quo Ui Deagha Mor; in Ui Cinnsealaigh lands. 
1 CONT
1 CONT 61 Eanna Cinnsealaigh: elder son of Labhradh; married Conang; was named Ceann-Salach by Cednathech the Druid, whom he slew at Croghan Hill, in the King's County, where Eanna defeated Eochaidh Muigh Meadhoin (Eochy Moyvone), the Mo
1 CONC narch, 365. Had following children: 
1 CONT Feidhlimidh (Felim) 
1 CONT Eochu (Eochaidh) Cinnsealaigh, who was exiled to Scotland by the Irish Monarch Niall of the Nine Hostages, whom Eochu later assassinated near Boulogne, on the river Leor (now the Lianne). 
1 CONT Crimthann Cass, who is described below 
1 CONT Earc 
1 CONT Aongus 
1 CONT Conal 
1 CONT Trian 
1 CONT Cairpre 
1 CONT
1 CONT 62 Crimthann Cass: 3rd son of Eanna Cinnsealach; was King of Leinster for 40 years; baptized by St. Patrick at Rathvilly around 448; slain in 484 by his grandson Eochaidh Guinech of the Hy-Bairche. Married Mell, daughter of Erebra
1 CONC n of the Desies in Munster (son of Eoghan Bric, son of Art Cuirb, son of Fiacha Suighde, son of Felim Rachtmar). Had following children: 
1 CONT Ingen, wife of Daire MacErcadh of the Hy-Bairche 
1 CONT Nathach (Dathi), who is described below 
1 CONT Fiacra the Fair, made first bishop of Leinster by St.Patrick 
1 CONT Eithne Uathach, wife of Aongus MacNadfraech, King of Munster 
1 CONT Fergus, who defeated Diarmuid MacCearbhaill at Drum Laeghaire, by the side of Cais in Hy-Faelain, defending the Boromha Tribute 
1 CONT Aongus 
1 CONT Etchen 
1 CONT Cobthach 
1 CONT
1 CONT ===================================================================
