0 @N6000000001783480812@ NOTE Basic Life Information
1 CONT
1 CONT Maud Marshal born about 1192 in Pembroke, Pembroke, Wales. This lady, upon the decease of her youngest brother, Anselm, Earl of Pembroke, s.p., in 1245, and the division of the estates, obtained as her share the manor of Hempsted-
1 CONC Marshall, in Berks, with the office of marshal of England. She had likewise the manors of Chepstowand Carlogh. [Sir Bernard Burke, Dormant, Abeyant, Forfeited, and Extinct Peerages, Burke's Peerage, Ltd., London, 1883, p. 358, Mar
1 CONC shal, Earls of Pembroke]
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriages and Children
1 CONT
1 CONT Maud’s first marriage was to Hugh Bigod, Earl of Norfolk.
1 CONT Roger Bigod, 4th Earl of Norfolk (who inheritied Hempsted-Marshall, in Berks, with the office of marshal of England.  It was surrendered to the crown by her grandson, Rogert Bigod, 5th Earl of Norfolk)
1 CONT
1 CONT Her second marriage was to William de Warren, Earl of Surrey
1 CONT
1 CONT Her third marriage was to Walde de Dunstanville.
1 CONT
1 CONT Death
1 CONT
1 CONT She died 27 Mar 1248 and was buried in Tintern Abbey, Chapel Hill, Monmouthsire, England.
1 CONT <http://www.juch.org/myancestors/aqwg78.asp>
0 @N6000000001783480854@ NOTE Basic Life Information
1 CONT
1 CONT Maud Marshal born about 1192 in Pembroke, Pembroke, Wales. This lady, upon the decease of her youngest brother, Anselm, Earl of Pembroke, s.p., in 1245, and the division of the estates, obtained as her share the manor of Hempsted-
1 CONC Marshall, in Berks, with the office of marshal of England. She had likewise the manors of Chepstowand Carlogh. [Sir Bernard Burke, Dormant, Abeyant, Forfeited, and Extinct Peerages, Burke's Peerage, Ltd., London, 1883, p. 358, Mar
1 CONC shal, Earls of Pembroke]
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriages and Children
1 CONT
1 CONT Maud’s first marriage was to Hugh Bigod, Earl of Norfolk.
1 CONT Roger Bigod, 4th Earl of Norfolk (who inheritied Hempsted-Marshall, in Berks, with the office of marshal of England.  It was surrendered to the crown by her grandson, Rogert Bigod, 5th Earl of Norfolk)
1 CONT
1 CONT Her second marriage was to William de Warren, Earl of Surrey
1 CONT
1 CONT JohnDe Warenne (1231-1304) whosucceeded his father as earl
1 CONT Isabel de Warenne (1228-1282) who married Hugh d'Aubigny, 5th Earl of Arundel
1 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_de_Warenne,_6th_Earl_of_Surrey
1 CONT
1 CONT Her third marriage was to Walde de Dunstanville.
1 CONT
1 CONT Death
1 CONT
1 CONT She died 27 Mar 1248 and was buried in Tintern Abbey, Chapel Hill, Monmouthsire, England.
1 CONT <http://www.juch.org/myancestors/aqwg78.asp>
