0 @N6000000001220386404@ NOTE [beaufort.ged]
1 CONT
1 CONT Isabel m. 1st to Gilbert de Clare, Earl of Gloucester; and 2ndly, to Richa rd, Earl of Cornwall. This lady had, as her portion, Kilkenny. [Sir Berna rd Burke, Dormant, Abeyant, Forfeited, and Extinct Peerages, Burke's Peera ge, Lt
1 CONC d., London, 1883, p. 358, Marshal, Earls of Pembroke][2753682.ged]
1 CONT
1 CONT !Daughter and coheiress of William, Earl of Pembroke, and Isabel de Clare. [Magna Charta Baro ns, p. 83]
1 CONT
1 CONT FOSTER, NEWLIN LINES - 21st ggrandmother
1 CONT
1 CONT !Wife of Gilbert de Clare; mother of Richard de Clare. [Ped. of Charlemagne, Vol. I, p. 126]
1 CONT
1 CONT b. 1206 [Judy Martin]
1 CONT
1 CONT !The Genealogical Society of Utah; Gareth Rice;
1 CONT
1 CONT m. William Marshall and their daughter Isabella wed the younger Gilbert de Clare, Earl of Glo ucester, thus reuniting the two branches of the de Clare family early in the 13th century. [T he de Clare Family by Daniel Mersey <http:
1 CONC //www.castlewales.com/clares.html]
1 CONT
1 CONT Dau of William Marshal and Isabel de Clare; m. Gilbert de Clare and was mother of Avicia, Isa bel, and Richard; m. Robert de Mauteby and was mother of John de Mauteby; she apparently die d in childbirth or shortly thereafter. [Tho
1 CONC mas Bledsoe <bledsoe@housingpartnership.net, 28 Ap r 2003]
