0 @N6000000003175357898@ NOTE Clan Donald is one of the oldest, and probably the largest and most famous of all the Highland clans. Its Celtic heritage goes back into antiquity
1 CONT The clan takes it's name from Donald "de Isla", the 3rd Lord of the Isles and grandson of Somerled, who succeeded his father Reginald, and under his guidance the clan attained great eminence. According to Highland tradition, Donal
1 CONC d made a pilgrimage to Rome to do penance, and obtain absolution for the various enormities of his former life; and, on his return, evinced his gratitude and piety by making grants of land to the monastery of Saddel, and other rel
1 CONC igious houses in Scotland. He died in 1269.
1 CONT    He was succeeded by his son Angus Mor the original "Mac" (meaning "son of"
