0 @N6000000004571333427@ NOTE The first remarkable Man of this Family, we find mentioned in History is Colin surnamed More, or Great from whom the Heads of this Family are termed in the Highland Tongue M'calen More, or the Sons of Colin More. 
1 CONT He was one of the Magnates Scotiae, that were summoned to Berwick upon the Part of Robert de Bruce, when he and all the other Competitors for the Crown of Scotland, on the Demise of Queen Margaret, had referres the Decision of the
1 CONC ir Claims to Edward I, of England.
1 CONT He had engaged in many conflicts, with McDougald of Lorn, his neighbour, in one of which he was slain.
1 CONT
1 CONT "Cailein Mor killed by the MacDoygalls at the string of Lorne"
