0 @N6000000001220381514@ NOTE [2753682.ged]
1 CONT
1 CONT NEWLIN, FOSTER LINES
1 CONT
1 CONT Dau. of Llewellyn ap Iorwerth and Joan; m.c. 1219, John de Braose; m.2 aft 1233, Walter de Cl ifford of Clifford's Castle, Herefordshire; mother of Maud de Clifford. [Ancestral Roots, p . 31]
1 CONT
1 CONT Research suggests that Margaret was the daughter of Llywelyn's second wife, who was the daugh ter of the Lord of the Isles. This marriage was eventually voided due to Llywelyn's earlier m arriage. [Douglas Richardson ,dcrdcr4@aol.
1 CONC com]
1 CONT
1 CONT Despite her efforts to keep her children following her husband's untimely death, she was over ruled. Royal favourites valued the granting of aristocratic wardships because it placed addit ional domains within their power, albeit t
1 CONC emporarily. Her son William became a ward of Henr y III's chief minister, Peter de Rivaux.
1 CONT    Relations with her son William seem to have deteriorated after she married Walter de Cliff ord. The couple issued several claims against William arising from her first marriage. Willia m was called to answer charges that he sei
1 CONC zed his mother's goods as they were transported tow ards Chichester and imprisoned her men. ["Barons de Braose" <http://freespace.virgin.net/doug .thompson/BraoseWeb/stage.htm]
1 CONT
1 CONT Dau. of Llewelyn, Prince of Wales, and Joan, Princess of Wales; m. Richard de Braose; mothe r of Margaret de Braose who m. Roger Colville. [WFT Vol 23 Ped 3286]
1 CONT
1 CONT Dau. of Llewellyn and Eve FitzWarine; m. John de Braiose; mother of William who m. Aline de M ulton. [Ed Mann <edlmann@mail2.lcia.com]
1 CONT
1 CONT Dau. of Llewelyn Fawr ap Iorwerth and Joan of England; m. John de Braose. [Carrie Holbrook, < familygirlsza@cox.net, 7 feb 2002]
1 CONT
1 CONT Dau. of Llewelyn ap Iorwerth and Joan of England; m. John de Braose and was mother of John, W illiam, Llywelyn, Roger, Hugh and Richard; m. Walter de Clifford and was mother of Maud.  [df ox <pifox@shentel.net, 30 Mar 2002]
1 CONT
1 CONT m. Braose and Clifford; mother is unknown and could be Joan. [Ken <KHF333@aol.com, 7 Jun 2002 ]
1 CONT
1 CONT Dau of Llewelyn 'the Great' ap Iorwerth, Prince of Wales, and Tangwystl verch Llywarch; m. Wa lter III de Clifford and was mother of Maud and Lucia.  [Larry Overmire <larryover@worldnet.a tt.net, 18 Jun 2003]
1 CONT
1 CONT b.c. 1208, d. 1268; dau of Llywelyn ap Iorwerth; m. Walter III de Clifford and was mother o f Maud; m. John de Brewes and was mother of John, Joane, William and Richard. [Dave Utzinge r <utz@aol.com, 11 Jul 2003]
