1 CONT At one time was treasurer of the Church of York. Emden stated that he "was younger son of Ric hard (de Clare), earl of Gloucester and Hertford. Studying at Oxford with his brother, Thomas , in 1257 .. presented by his father [to R
1 CONC otherfield] May 1258..." If this is true, Bogo woul d be son of Maud de Lacy, not her brother. But as Gilbert de Clare, Maud de Lacy's eldest son , was born 2 Sep 1243, this would have Bogo begin presented to Rotherfield at a very
1 CONC  young ag e in 1258 if younger brother of Gilbert. But even placing Bogo back a generation, we would ha ve that he was brother-in-law of Maud (de Lacy) de Clare, not her brother. Bogo/Bevis died a t London 26 Oct 1294.
