1 CONC t le Brus, Earl of Carrick|b. Jul 1243<BR> Last Edited=10 May 2003
1 CONT Robert le Brus, Earl of Carrick was the son of Sir Robert de Brus, Lord of Annandale <p10248.htm> and Christina de Ireby.1 He was born in July 1243.2 He was also reported to have been born circa July 1253. He married Margaret of C
1 CONC arrick, Countess of Carrick <p10248.htm>, daughter of Neil of Carrick, 2nd Earl of Carrick <p10462.htm> and Margaret Stewart <p10785.htm>, in 1271 at Turnberry Castle, Turnberry, Ayrshire, Scotland.2 He married Eleanor (?) <p10248
1 CONC .htm> after 1292.2 He died before 4 April 1304.2 He was buried at Abbey of Holm Cultram.2  He was also known as Robert Bruce. Through his marriage, Robert le Brus, Earl of Carrick gained the title of Earl of Carrick in 1271.2 He a
1 CONC bdicated as Earl of Carrick on 27 October 1292.2 He succeeded to the title of Lord of Annandale before 4 July 1295.2
1 CONT Children of Robert le Brus, Earl of Carrick and Margaret of Carrick, Countess of Carrick <p10248.htm>:
1 CONT Neil Bruce <p10352.htm> d. c Sep 1306 Lady Christina Bruce <p10788.htm>+ d. 1356/57 Robert I Bruce, King of Scotland <p10209.htm>+ b. 11 Jul 1274, d. 7 Jun 1329 Isabella Bruce <p10352.htm>+ b. c 1275, d. 1358 Edward Bruce, Earl of
1 CONC  Carrick <p10351.htm>+ b. b 1292, d. 14 Oct 1318 Sir Thomas Bruce <p10351.htm> b. b 1292, d. 9 Feb 1307 Alexander Bruce <p10351.htm> b. b 1292, d. 9 Feb 1307 Lady Mary Bruce <p10787.htm>+ b. b 1292, d. b 22 Sep 1323 Margaret Bruce
1 CONC  <p10790.htm>+ b. b 1292 Matilda Bruce <p10790.htm>+ b. b 1292, d. bt 1323 - 1329
1 CONT Citations
