0 @N6000000003949925920@ NOTE Lord (feudally) of Arwystli, Caereinion, Cyfeiliog, Mawddwy, Upper Mochnant and Y Tair Swydd by grant of Henry III 1241, though he later supported Llywelyn the Last, Prince of Wales. [Burke's Peerage]Gruffydd was granted lordship 
1 CONC of southern Powys by Henry III in 1240 but had a constant struggle with Llywelyn , finding himself in exile, imprisoned in 1263, in exile again in 1273. When reinstated in 1277, held lands under the English King.
