0 @N6000000001579451292@ NOTE Robert II.,
1 CONT King of Scotland, first of the Stuart line, was only son of Walter Stuart and Marjory, daughter of Robert Bruce, and was born in 1316. He took part in the battle of Halidon Hill, and acted a prominent part in the affairs of govern
1 CONC ment during the minority of David II. He held the office of regent of Scotland during the captivity in England of his uncle David, 1346-1357, and succeeded to the throne on his death, in 1371. He was engaged for several years in w
1 CONC ar with England, in which he was aided by the French; lived chiefly in retirement during his latter years, the Earl of Fife being named regent in 1389; and died at Dundonald Castle, in 1390.
0 @N6000000001713334102@ NOTE Was in command of the second division of the Scotch Army at Halidon Hill, and
1 CONT was one of the few who escaped the carnage of that disastrous day.
1 CONT See Europäisch Stammtafeln Band II tafel 69.
1 CONT There is some confusion over which daughter is which and who are their mothers
1 CONT which still needs some clarification.
1 CONT
1 CONT Name: Robert Stuart/Stewart (King of Scotland)
1 CONT Sex: M
1 CONT Note: Alt spelling: Steward
1 CONT Birth: 2 MAR 1316 in Scotland
1 CONT Death: 19 APR 1390 in Ayrshire, Scotland
1 CONT *Note: Robert II, 1316-90, king of Scotland (1371-90), nephew and successor of David II. He
1 CONT was the first sovereign of the house of Stuart/Stewart, which eventually succeeded to the
1 CONT English as well as the Scottish throne. The son of Walter the Steward and Marjory, daughter of
1 CONT Robert I, he was regent three times (1333-35, 1338-41, and 1346-58) for David II during the
1 CONT latter's exile and captivity. He thus led the resistance to Edward de Baliol and Edward III of
1 CONT England. Robert rebelled against his uncle in 1363 when David recognized Edward III as his
1 CONT successor. On David's death (1371), however, he succeeded peacefully to the throne, in
1 CONT accordance with the succession law adopted in 1318. Robert's first marriage took place after
1 CONT the birth of several of his sons, but their succession to the throne was legitimized by an act of
1 CONT Parliament in 1373. Through most of his reign the government was dominated by two of these
1 CONT sons-John, earl of Carrick (later Robert III) and Robert Stuart/Stewart, later 1st duke of
1 CONT Albany. The Scots in alliance with France fought off several English invasions; they invaded
1 CONT England without assistance in 1388 and won a great victory at Otterburn. Robert was
1 CONT succeeded by Robert III.
1 CONT *Note: In 1357, England recognized Scotland's independence.
1 CONT *Note: By 1377 the Stuart/Stewart family held 7 of the then 16 Earldom's.
1 CONT
1 CONT Father: Sixth Lord High Steward of Scotland Walter Stuart/Stewart b: 12
1 CONT Mother: Marjorie Bruce (daughter of King Robert I - Robert the Bruce)
1 CONT
