1 CONT English and Robert became so le regent, meeting with such success in his
1 CONT efforts to restore the royal auth ority that the king was able to return
1 CONT to Scotland in 1341. Having handed ove r the duties of government to
1 CONT David, the Steward escaped from the battle of N eville's Cross in 1346,
1 CONT and was again chosen regent while the king was a capt ive in England. Soon
1 CONT after this event some friction arose between Robert and his royal uncle.
