0 @N6000000001578993009@ NOTE The last Earl of Warenne. In 1304, he succeeded his grandfather John, the Seventh Earl from whom he inherited the estates and peerage. He was Governor of Scotland. In 1307, John quarreled with Piers Gaveston . He joined the party 
1 CONC of barons at Scarborough in 1312, he took Gaveston prisoner, under terms of protection. He was angered by the execution of Gaveston, and went over to Edward II .
1 CONT In 1316, he was excommunicated for adultery with Isabel de Houland and Maud de Neirford, there were several children by both liaisons. He later married Isabel.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1317, the family seat at Sandal Castle  was burned to the ground by Thomas Lacy , Earl of Lancaster; In 1319, he was forced into giving the Manor of Wakefield  to the Earl of Lancaster.
1 CONT By about 1320, the Earl of Lancaster had made it a strongly defended stone fortress. After Lacy's execution in 1322, the Manor reverted to the Crown but was restored to John in 1326.
1 CONT
1 CONT He died without legitimate heirs, and on the death of his wife in 1359, his estates reverted to the crown – in 1362, Edward III  gave it to his son Edmund Langley  – and the earldom went to John's nephew, Richard FitzAlan, Second 
1 CONC Earl of Arundel
