1 CONC  Earl of Leicester, son of Henry III, King of England and Eleanor of Provence, on 8 April 1269 at Westminster Abbey, Westminster, London, England.2 She died on 10 November 1274 at age 15 at Stockwell, Surrey, England, without issu
1 CONC e.2,1 She was buried at Westminster Abbey, Westminster, London, England.2
1 CONT      Aveline de Forz, Countess of Holderness gained the title of Countess of Holderness.3 She succeeded to the title of Countess of Aumale before 6 April 1269.
