0 @N6000000003658774276@ NOTE From Magna Carta Ancestry:
1 CONT
1 CONT JOAN DE CLARE, married (1st) DUNCAN OF FIFE, 9th Earl of Fife (in Scotland), son and heir of Colbran, Knt., Earl of Fife, by Anne, possibly daughter of Alan Durward, Knt.  he was born about 1262 (aged 8 in 1270).  They had one son
1 CONC , Duncan. ... He was admitted to the possession of his Earldom in 1284.  He was chosen one of the six Regents of the Kingdom [Scotland] in 1286.  DUNCAN OF FIFE, Earl of Fife, was murdered by Sir Patrick Abernethy and others at Pe
1 CONC tpolloch 25 Sept. 1288.  His widow, Joan, married (2nd) after 22 April 1299 GERVASE AVENEL, Knt.).  She and her 2nd husband, Gervase, and her son, Duncan were exiles in England about 1324.
