0 @N6000000003051190629@ NOTE Great-great grandson of William de Mowbray, Magna Charta surety.
1 CONT Baron Gower and Brember, Governor of the City of York and of Scarborough Castle, sheriff of Yorkshire.
1 CONT
1 CONT [Wikipedia, "John de Mowbray, 2nd Baron Mowbray", retrieved 24 Dec 07]
1 CONT John de Mowbray, 2nd Baron Mowbray (b. 04 Sep 1286 d. 23 Mar 1321) was the son of Roger de Mowbray, 1st Baron Mowbray.
1 CONT
1 CONT De Mowbray served in the Scottish wars of Edward I. The baron held such offices as sheriff of Yorkshire, governor of the city of York, a warden of the Scottish marches, governor of Malton and Scarborough Castles.
1 CONT
1 CONT He took part in the rebellion of Thomas, Earl of Lancaster. He was captured at the battle of Boroughbridge and subsequently hanged at York.
1 CONT
1 CONT John de Mowbray married Aliva de Braose, (b. 1291 d. ca 1331), daughter of William de Braose, Lord Braose of Gower. They had at least two sons:
1 CONT - John,(b. 29 Nov 1310,Yorkshire,England d.1361 who succeeded his father to the barony.
1 CONT - Alexander, (b. c 1314 d. c 1391.)
