0 @N6000000002188014994@ NOTE Richard FitzAlan, 8th Earl of Arundel
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Richard FitzAlan, 8th Earl of Arundel (February 3, 1266/7 – March 9, 1301/2) was an English nobleman.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was son of John FitzAlan, 7th Earl of Arundel and Isabella de Mortimer, daughter of Roger Mortimer, 1st Baron Wigmore.
1 CONT
1 CONT Richard was feudal Lord of Clun and Oswestry. After attaining his majority in 1289 became in fact Earl of Arundel, by being summoned to Parliament by a writ directed to the Earl of Arundel. He was knighted by King Edward I of Engl
1 CONC and in 1289. He fought in the Welsh wars, 1288; in Gascony 1295-97; and in the Scottish wars, 1298-1300.
1 CONT
1 CONT He married before 1285 to Alasia of Saluzzo (also known as Alice), daughter of Thomas I of Saluzzo in Italy. Their children were:
1 CONT
1 CONT Edmund FitzAlan, 9th Earl of Arundel. 
1 CONT Eleanor FitzAlan, married Henry de Percy, 1st Baron Percy 
1 CONT Alice FitzAlan, married Stephen de Segrave, 3rd Lord Segrave 
1 CONT Margaret FitzAlan, married William Botiler 
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT John FitzAlan Earl of Arundel
1 CONT 1272 - 1302 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Edmund FitzAlan 
